{"level":30,"time":1776951751094,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016zoGLDAMt6s1DdUHyMHzBw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. I've read:\n1. The grouping file (2.md) - covering Underground Utility Routing and Placement\n2. The README.md - site plan details with 39 sheets and supplementary documents\n3. The facts.md - site property details\n\nNow I need to understand applicability of this grouping to this specific site. Let me check the key things:\n\n**Grouping 2 (EL-2) Focus:** Underground Utility Routing and Placement\n\nKey frameworks:\n1. LDC Subchapter E - CTC and Urban Roadway sites\n2. Regulating Plan Districts (Plaza Saltillo TOD, North Burnet/Gateway)\n3. Hill Country Roadway Corridors\n4. Planting Zone Prohibition (Austin Water)\n5. Transformer Pad and Clearances\n6. AE Facility Access\n7. Utility Easement Licensing\n8. Table B Connectivity (parking areas)\n\n**Site Details:**\n- Address: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n- Regulating Plan: None\n- Roadway: Valley View Road (ASMP Street Level 1 — Local Street, NOT in AMTP)\n- Site Area: 2.16 acres\n- Hill Country Roadway Corridor: Not mentioned, so likely NO\n\nLet me check applicability:\n\n1. **LDC Subchapter E Framework (CTC or Urban Roadway)?**\n   - Valley View Road is a Local Street, NOT a CTC or Urban Roadway\n   - Not subject to Subchapter E § 2.2.2.B.3 or § 2.2.3.B.3\n   - Items EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.4 likely NOT applicable\n\n2. **Regulating Plan (Plaza Saltillo TOD or NBG)?**\n   - Facts confirm \"Regulating Plan: None\"\n   - Items EL-2.5 through EL-2.8 do not apply\n\n3. **Hill Country Roadway Corridor?**\n   - No mention in facts.md, so I need to verify proximity to Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway\n   - Item EL-2.2 requires investigation\n\n4. **Utilities Proposed?**\n   - Sheet 21 shows Preliminary Electrical Design, indicating utility work is planned\n\n. Sheet 19 documents the Utility Tap Plan, confirming utilities are part of the proposal and triggering several applicable items.\n\n5. **Parking Areas?**\n   - With 39 townhome units proposed, parking areas almost certainly exist and are relevant to Table B requirements under EL-2.24.\n\n6. **Detention/Retention Ponds?**\n   - The site includes a stacked biofiltration/detention pond shown on Sheet 15, making EL-2.10 applicable.\n\n7. **Street Trees/Planting Zones?**\n   - Landscape and tree plans appear on Sheets 30-31. I should verify whether right-of-way planting zones with AW infrastructure are present, as this affects EL-2.11 and EL-2.12 applicability.\n\nThe parkland deficiency noted in the facts suggests EL-2.13 may apply. Light rail doesn't appear to be involved, so EL-2.14 is likely inapplicable. Extensive easements are documented—greenbelt access, city drainage, and plat-dedicated easements—which could trigger EL-2.15 through EL-2.22. Sheet 21's Preliminary Electrical Design Plan shows transformers, making EL-2.22 relevant. Tree wells may appear in the landscape plan and would determine EL-2.23 applicability.\n\nI should focus my research on a narrower set. The detention pond makes EL-2.10 worth checking. I need to verify whether overhead utilities exist for EL-2.9, examine the landscape and utility plans for EL-2.11 and EL-2.12, and cross-reference the easement details against the facts to assess EL-2.15, EL-2.16, and EL-2.17. The easement complexity particularly suggests EL-2.16 could be relevant.\n\nFor the remaining items, I'll need to check the demolition plan for abandoned utilities (EL-2.18), review demolition and ROW plans for public utility termination (EL-2.19), confirm the absence of USTs (EL-2.20), and examine the utility and electrical plans for power pole relocation (EL-2.21), transformer pads (EL-2.22), and tree well outlets (EL-2.23). I should also determine if parking utilities apply under Table B (EL-2.24). Starting with the guide will help me identify which sheets are most critical to review.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17724,"cache_read_input_tokens":22307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17724},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f19fb8e-f97f-429a-bf6c-feca3089c5bd","uuid":"7eaf8268-dd3e-47af-96df-c466283943f0"}
