{"level":30,"time":1776951752605,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01YFfLz2syoAc2yVB2Pg5i4Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I understand the site:\n\n**Site:** Valley View Townhomes - 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n**Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n**Proposed Use:** 39 multi-family townhome units, 8 buildings\n**Flood Zone:** Zone X (outside floodplain)\n**Watershed:** West Bouldin Creek (Urban)\n**Regulating Plan:** None (from facts.md line 52)\n**Street Type:** Valley View Road is a Local Street (ASMP Level 1, not in AMTP), not a CTC or Urban Roadway\n\n**Key for this grouping:**\n- No mention of overhead utilities from the facts or existing conditions\n- Need to check the utility plan (Sheet 21) for overhead utilities and electrical clearances\n- No transmission lines mentioned\n- Need to check for stormwater infrastructure staging areas with clearances\n\nFrom the grouping file, I can see there are 28 checklist items to evaluate. The applicability is determined by:\n1. EL-1.1: Only if overhead utilities remain and site fronts CTC or Urban Roadway → Valley View Road is a Local Street, NOT CTC or Urban Roadway, so this does NOT apply\n2. EL-1.2, EL-1.3: Only if overhead electric distribution utilities are present\n3. EL-1.4: Only if vault proposed near overhead power lines\n4. EL-1.5: Only if items 1.2, 1.3, or 1.4 apply\n5. EL-1.6: Only if overhead AE utilities present and customer service entrance facilities proposed\n6. EL-1.7: Only if overhead service drops cross truck traffic areas\n7. EL-1.8: Only if utilities cross Texas Gas Service lines\n8. EL-1.9: Only if proposed utilities cross AE underground facilities\n\n\n9. EL-1.10: Only if non-AE utilities share a joint trench with AE\n10. EL-1.11: Only if utilities are routed within public ROW\n11. EL-1.12: Only if utility lines cross over or under water/wastewater infrastructure\n12. EL-1.13: Only if utilities are bored beneath roads or structures\n13. EL-1.14: Only if large-diameter cleanouts are part of the proposal\n14. EL-1.15: Only if storm drain access points are positioned near AE poles\n15. EL-1.16: Only if utilities run parallel within electrical/PUE zones\n16. EL-1.17: Only if utility poles are located near water easements or transmission structures\n17. EL-1.18: Only if demolition activities occur near transmission lines\n18. EL-1.19: Only if construction work is adjacent to transmission ROW\n19. EL-1.20: Only if demolition is proposed\n20. EL-1.21: All sites with proposed utilities\n21. EL-1.22: Only if permanent SCM staging areas are required—the site has a stormwater feature but I need to verify applicability thresholds\n22. EL-1.23: Only if maintenance access drives are needed for SCMs\n23. EL-1.24: Only if work zones fall below overhead utilities\n24. EL-1.25: Only if staging or spoils areas are proposed\n25. EL-1.26: Only if overhead electric utilities are present\n26. EL-1.27: Only if overhead utilities exist on the site\n27. EL-1.28: Only if overhead utilities are present on sloped terrain\n\nI should check Sheet 21 for overhead utility information, review Sheet 8 for any demolition near transmission lines, examine sheets showing utility crossings and stormwater details, and look at Sheets 15-16 to assess stormwater features and staging area requirements. Starting with the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan will help clarify the overhead utility situation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8306,"cache_read_input_tokens":31399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8306},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"