{"level":30,"time":1776951756681,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014we9ajww6ZDRZqpjjxxFLT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Now I have the context. This is the Valley View Townhomes project (SP-2025-0126C) at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704. Key facts:\n\n1. **Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density) — NO regulating plan applies\n2. **Regulating Plan:** None (not Plaza Saltillo TOD, not NBG)\n3. **Roadway:** Valley View Road — ASMP Street Level 1 (Local Street), NOT a CTC or Urban Roadway per Subchapter E\n4. **Hill Country Roadway:** Need to check if within 1,000 feet of the five named roadways (Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, Southwest Parkway)\n5. **Utilities:** Site has water, wastewater, storm sewer, and electrical service proposed\n\nNow I need to determine applicability of each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1 (CTC/Urban Roadway):** Valley View Road is a Local Street, NOT a CTC or Urban Roadway. NOT APPLICABLE.\n\n**EL-2.2 (Hill Country Roadway Corridor):** Need to check if within 1,000 feet of Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway. The address is 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704. Valley View Road is in south Austin, likely closer to Southwest Parkway or RM 2244. I should check this.\n\n**EL-2.3, EL-2.4 (CTC/Urban Roadway undergrounding):** NOT APPLICABLE (not a CTC or Urban Roadway).\n\n\nSince no regulating plan applies, EL-2.5 through EL-2.8 don't trigger. For the overhead utility zone, I need to review the electrical plan to see if any overhead lines remain. The biofiltration-detention pond on Sheets 15-16 means I should verify utilities don't run beneath it. Street tree planting restrictions also need checking against existing ROW conditions.\n\nRegarding transformers in parkland, the site is in a Parkland Deficient Area, but that indicates a shortage rather than confirming parkland exists on the property itself. I need to determine if there's actual parkland present. Light rail proximity also requires verification. Several utility easements are noted in the facts, some undepicted, so I should check whether any encroach into the proposed right-of-way. Licensing requirements apply as well, and I need to confirm what items fall within the applicable scope.\n\nFor private utilities, I'll review the right-of-way plans. The demolition plan should show any abandoned utilities being removed. Existing public utilities in the ROW need proper termination procedures. Since no underground storage tanks are registered, that's not a concern. Power pole relocations require Austin Energy coordination documentation. Sheet 21 indicates transformers are present, so transformer pad compliance needs verification. If tree wells are included in the design, electrical outlets must be addressed. Finally, I need to determine whether Table B utility routing requirements apply based on the net area calculation.\n\nThe site measures 2.16 acres in MF-2 zoning, which is residential, so Table B likely doesn't apply unless surface parking exists between the building and the principal street. I'll cross-reference the electrical site plan on Sheet 21, utility plans on Sheets 19-20, and the landscape plan on Sheet 31 to verify all these conditions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8483,"cache_read_input_tokens":31919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8483},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"a1c4c183-57d5-48c2-b0c4-50c1786cc203"}
