imity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60bcd99d-409f-4cd6-a909-b056cb4b2c38","uuid":"1c8ea7cb-fb02-47d3-817f-6b36611f2a33","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951761878,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WtcGqgZi8LM4XZ1N3dbr8T","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n     4→\n     5→NORTH\n     6→[North Arrow Symbol]\n     7→SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n     8→0 10 20 50\n     9→\n    10→## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n    11→\n    12→This block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n    13→- Building footprints\n    14→- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n    15→- Sidewalks and pathways\n    16→- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n    17→- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n    18→- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n    19→- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n    20→- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n    21→- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n    22→- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n    23→\n    24→## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n    25→\n    26→NOTE:\n    27→FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    56→3759 VALLEY\n    57→VIEW ROAD,\n    58→AUSTIN,\n    59→TEXAS 78704\n    60→\n    61→## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n    62→\n    63→PROJECT NAME:\n    64→VALLEY VIEW\n    65→TOWNHOMES\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"cce22d5d-64d7-49ba-b99d-6e3c326a2202","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
