{"level":30,"time":1776951769796,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FSxwGUxJhh3xJzn2Guctfu","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Cover\n     2→\n     3→Cover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n    11→*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    12→*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n    13→*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n    14→*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n    15→*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n    16→*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n    17→*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n    18→*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n    19→*   Private Hydrants: 1\n    20→*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n    25→*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n    26→*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n    27→*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n    28→*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n    29→*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n    30→*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n    31→*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n    32→*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60bcd99d-409f-4cd6-a909-b056cb4b2c38","uuid":"119d2c58-4a05-4ecb-8d4b-1ccbb98d689b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Cover\n\nCover sheet containing project details, location map, and sheet index.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis is the cover sheet for the Valley View Townhomes site plan (SP-2025-0126C). It serves as the primary reference document for the project, containing the sheet index, site development data, fire department requirements, a location map, and required municipal compliance notes.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Project Area: 2.16 Acres\n*   Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n*   Total Residential Units: 39 units\n*   Total Plan Sheets: 39 sheets\n*   Fire Flow Demand (@ 20 psi): 3000 GPM (Reduced to 1500 GPM with sprinkler system)\n*   Building Fire Area: 13,344 s.f.\n*   Occupancy Classification: R3\n*   Construction Classification: Type V-B\n*   Sprinkler System Type: NFPA 13D\n*   Private Hydrants: 1\n*   Mapsco / City of Austin Grid: #614S / #G19\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 15:** text_block — Project title, address (3759 Valley View Road), and permit number (SP-2025-0126C). READ for core project identification.\n*   **Block 4:** table — Site Development Data. READ for project team contact information, legal description, and exact acreage values. \n*   **Block 6:** table — Sheet List Table. READ to understand the structure of the 39-page drawing set and locate specific disciplines (grading, drainage, landscaping, etc.).\n*   **Block 7:** table — Austin Fire Department requirements. READ for specific fire design codes, fire flow demands (in GPM), and building classification data.\n*   **Blocks 1 & 30:** drawing & text_block — Project Location Map and associated scale/coordinate data. VISION for the spatial layout of the site relative to major cross streets (Manchaca, Clawson Rd, 290); READ Block 30 for Mapsco #614S and Grid #G19.\n*   **Blocks 8 & 31:** text_block — Environmental status notes. READ to confirm the site is in the West Bouldin Creek Watershed, is outside the 100-year floodplain, and is not in the Edwards Aquifer zone.\n*   **Blocks 16, 17, 25, 26, 27:** various — Project-specific requirements and waivers. READ for specific stipulations including private hydrant maintenance (Block 16), private biofiltration pond maintenance (Block 17), parkland dedication fees for 39 units (Block 25), a specific DCM waiver (Block 26), and Traffic Control Plan requirements (Block 27).\n*   **Block 5:** table — Revisions/Corrections. READ to confirm no revisions have been logged yet.\n*   **Blocks 2, 3, 9-14, 18-24, 28-29, 32, 33:** various — Boilerplate, Administrative Notes, and Seals. READ selectively if reviewing general contractor responsibilities, standard city ordinances (lead-free water, recycling, USTs), engineer certifications, liability disclaimers, or standard erosion control notes. Includes empty approval stamps and review tables.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951769919,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013GQQivdMJSgW7QAs9Q146M","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n     4→\n     5→NORTH\n     6→[North Arrow Symbol]\n     7→SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n     8→0 10 20 50\n     9→\n    10→## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n    11→\n    12→This block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n    13→- Building footprints\n    14→- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n    15→- Sidewalks and pathways\n    16→- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n    17→- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n    18→- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n    19→- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n    20→- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n    21→- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n    22→- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n    23→\n    24→## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n    25→\n    26→NOTE:\n    27→FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    56→3759 VALLEY\n    57→VIEW ROAD,\n    58→AUSTIN,\n    59→TEXAS 78704\n    60→\n    61→## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n    62→\n    63→PROJECT NAME:\n    64→VALLEY VIEW\n    65→TOWNHOMES\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f19fb8e-f97f-429a-bf6c-feca3089c5bd","uuid":"18f905a8-c9ed-4515-aa3c-0e1ea9f274d1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
