ation Pond Plantings\nMin = (20% of Filtration Area) 166 Plants 171 Plants\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This section contains a site plan for Unit 501, showing the layout of the area including retaining walls, a pond, and various drainage features. Key elements include PVC pipes, rip-rap, cleanouts, and specific elevations (e.g., TW 681.00, FG 672.00). It also notes a 'Biofiltration Media' area and details like a 'Pond Outfall Weir' and 'Concrete Structural Retaining Wall'.\n\nA detailed site plan drawing showing Unit 501. It includes property lines, topographic lines, and various infrastructure elements.\n\nKey features labeled:\n- Unit 501\n- Stone Pavers\n- Fire Pit\n- Concrete Splash Pad\n- Pond Outfall Weir See Detail on Sheet 16\n- Top of Biofiltration Media El = 672.00\n- Cleanout (Typ) FL 6\": 669.75\n- MUTCD Compliant Vertical Water Surface Marker Per DCM 8.3.3(B)(8)\n- 6\" PVC Raised Outlet Pipe See Detail 1.6.7.C-3 FL In 6\": 669.31\n- Discharge PVC Through Wall Install 6\" Threaded Cap on End of PVC with 1.33\" Hole Drilled in Bottom of Cap FL In 6\": 670.50\n- 3' x 4' Concrete Splash Pad w/ 3' wide Rip-Rap\n- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.27%\n- 6.58 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n- 6.42 lf 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\n- 26.08 lf 6\" Perforated PVC @ 1.00%\n- Rock Flow Spreader 6\"-12\"(H) x 3'(W) 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n- 6' Wide Rock Rip-Rap 5-8\" Dia. Rock\n- 63.64 lf 24\" HDPE @ 1.35%\n- 24\" Pipe Through Pond Wall FL In 24\": 672.94\n- Concrete Structural Retaining Wall w/ Fall Protection Railing (By Others)\n- End Retaining Wall\n- 8' Wide Concrete Maintenance Path\n- Pond Maintenance Gate 2-4' Swing Gates\n- 8' Wide Maintenance Ramp 4:1 Max Slope\n- Ramp Landing\n- Sedimentation\n- Create Swale to Direct Flows Along Pond Wall\n\nVarious elevations are marked, such as TW 681.00, FG 672.00, FG 672.94, etc.\n\n## Block 5: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the filtration pond at different elevations.\n\n**FILTRATION POND:**\n\n| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 672.00 | 831 | 0 |\n| 673.00 | 831 | 831 |\n| 674.00 | 831 | 1,661 |\n| 675.00 | 831 | 2,492 |\n| 676.00 | 831 | 3,323 |\n| 677.00 | 831 | 4,153 |\n| 677.50 | 831 | 4,568 |\n\n*in one foot or less increments\n\n## Block 6: table — A table presenting variables and their values for a falling head orifice calculation. It includes surface area, orifice coefficient, head values, time, and calculated orifice area and diameter. Below the table is the formula used for the calculation.\n\n**Falling Head Orifice Calculator**\n\n| Surface Area (sq. ft.) | | 1942 |\n| Orifice coefficient (use 0.6 per DCM) | | 0.6 |\n| $h_1$ (ft) | | 5.15 |\n| $h_2$ (ft) | | 0 |\n| t (hrs.) | | 48 |\n| $A_o$ orifice area (sq. ft.) | | 0.011 |\n| Orifice diameter (in.) | | 1.39 |\n\n$$A_o = \\frac{-2A}{C_d * t * \\sqrt{2g}} * [\\sqrt{h_2} - \\sqrt{h_1}]$$\n\n## Block 7: table — Two tables providing calculations for a 100-year event. The top table details 'Biofiltration Entrance' with Entrance Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations. The bottom table details 'Pond Outfall' with Exit Velocity and D50 Rock Rip-Rap calculations.\n\n| Biofiltration Entrance (100-yr) |\n|---|---|\n| **Entrance Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n| Q100= 18.83 cfs | Q100= 18.83 cfs |\n| L= 18 feet | A= 13.5 sf |\n| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.39 fps |\n| V= 1.39 fps | D50= 0.25 in |\n\n| Pond Outfall (100-yr) |\n|---|---|\n| **Exit Velocity Calculation** | **D50 Rock Rip-Rap Calculation** |\n| Q100= 15.60 cfs | Q100= 15.60 cfs |\n| L= 12 feet | A= 9.0 sf |\n| D= 0.75 feet | V= 1.73 fps |\n| V= 1.73 fps | D50= 0.39 in |\n\n## Block 8: table — A table showing the stage, area, and storage for the sedimentation pond at different elevations.\n\n**SEDIMENTATION POND:**\n\n| Stage (ft msl)* | Area (sf) | Storage (cf) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 672.00 | 0 | 0 |\n| 673.00 | 1,024 | 512 |\n| 674.00 | 1,060 | 1,554 |\n| 675.00 | 1,096 | 2,632 |\n| 676.00 | 1,132 | 3,747 |\n| 677.00 | 1,169 | 4,897 |\n| 677.50 | 1,189 | 5,487 |\n\n## Block 9: table — A table outlining the required characteristics for biofiltration medium, including percentages of different soil components and testing criteria.\n\n**Table 1 - Biofiltration Medium Characteristics**\n\n| Parameter | Results* | Criteria | Criteria Met?* |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Percent Sand + Coarse Fragments (ASTMD-422) | | 70 - 90% | |\n| Percent Clay (< 0.002 mm) | | 3 - 10% | |\n| Percent Silt + Clay (< 0.05 mm) | | ≤ 27% | |\n| Percent Organic Matter (ASTM D-2974) | | 0.5 - 5% | |\n| Is any \"Red Death\" included in medium? | | None allowed | |\n| Is the mixture free of trash, stones, weeds, or other undesirable material? | | None allowed | |\n| Is the medium well-mixed and homogenous? | | Must be homogenous | |\n\n## Block 10: table — A table summarizing discharge flow rates in cfs for different analysis points (Ex POA 1, Ex POA 2, Ex POA 3) across 2-year, 10-year, 25-year, and 100-year storm events, based on Atlas 14 data.","numLines":150,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}}}
