{"level":30,"time":1776951770798,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EJ9eL8W7TYcGhfDcUXKcmp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, so I've reviewed the key sheets:\n\n**Key Findings on Applicability:**\n\n1. **Overhead Utilities:** Sheet 21 shows **underground** electrical design - transformers, pull boxes, underground lines. No mention of overhead electrical utilities. I should check if there are any overhead utilities shown elsewhere.\n\n2. **Demolition Plan (Sheet 8):** No mention of transmission lines or overhead utilities in the demolition notes.\n\n3. **Stormwater Feature:** There is a biofiltration-detention pond (Unit 501 area based on Sheet 15-16). According to the grouping file:\n   - EL-1.22 applies \"Only when permanent SCM staging areas are required: site contains a COA-maintained or residential development (single-family/duplex) SCM with combined total storage volume >5,000 cu ft OR maximum ponding depth >3 ft\"\n   - From Sheet 15, the pond has:\n     - Water Quality Volume: 6,237 cf provided (>5,000 cu ft) ✓\n     - Maximum Ponding Depth: 3.65 ft (>3 ft) ✓\n   - The grouping specifies \"permanent SCM staging areas (required for COA-maintained SCMs and residential single-family/duplex development SCMs)\"\n   - This project is 39 multi-family townhome units (not single-family/duplex), so this would be a commercial SCM, which is \"not subject to this requirement unless COA-maintained\"\n   - Need to check if this is COA-maintained or privately maintained\n\n4. **Street Classification:** Valley View Road is a Local Street (not CTC or Urban Roadway), so EL-1.1 does NOT apply.\n\nLet me check the facts.md and other documents to see if there's any mention of COA-maintained SCM or if it's privately maintained. Sheet 15 says \"Partial biofiltration and onsite detention pond associated with Unit 501\" and from facts.md: \"Stormwater Feature: Stacked biofiltration / detention pond (privately maintained)\"\n\n\nSince the SCM is privately maintained and this is a multi-family development rather than single-family/duplex, EL-1.22 and EL-1.23 don't apply. The street classification rules out EL-1.1, and the underground electrical design means overhead utility requirements like EL-1.2 through EL-1.7, EL-1.24, and EL-1.26 through EL-1.28 aren't relevant here.\n\nLooking at what could be applicable: EL-1.9 and EL-1.10 might come into play depending on whether utility crossings interact with the AE underground system. EL-1.11 could apply if utilities are proposed within the right-of-way. Utility crossing standards EL-1.12 through EL-1.14 and EL-1.16 warrant review, along with EL-1.15 if storm drain access points are positioned near poles. EL-1.20 and EL-1.21 regarding demolition and field verification may also be relevant to confirm existing conditions.\n\nI should also consider EL-1.25 for staging and spoils management. Now I need to examine the utility sheets more closely, especially the crossing details and Sheet 3 for any general notes about utility coordination.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4822,"cache_read_input_tokens":45077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4822},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"a8c73065-a43a-4dd3-ad62-2a97c88db278"}
