r licensing and clearances. The 88 parking spaces (10 surface, 78 garage) don't trigger Table B requirements since the site is 2.16 acres in residential zoning, making EL-2.24 likely inapplicable. I should examine the site visually to confirm whether utilities pass beneath the detention pond and verify transformer pad compliance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4861,"cache_read_input_tokens":57409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4861},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f19fb8e-f97f-429a-bf6c-feca3089c5bd","uuid":"4184e3f3-41f6-4f2a-8d1d-675813ad8302"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951781681,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018s6Nqo2wzpUu8JovxKYKSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me use the vision tool to examine specific aspects of utility placement and easements that require visual analysis:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4861,"cache_read_input_tokens":57409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4861},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f19fb8e-f97f-429a-bf6c-feca3089c5bd","uuid":"79bb9366-e46b-49c0-b32e-55f4b08d03a4"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951781950,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017Hej49chGbJiptuT17gqn9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good information. Based on Sheet 15, the biofiltration-detention pond is shown in the site plan at Unit 501 with piping through it (24\" HDPE @ 1.35%, 6\" PVC pipes). I need to check if utilities from other buildings (not Unit 501) route under the pond or if the pond is specifically for Unit 501 only.\n\nFrom Sheet 19, I saw utilities are routed across the site. Let me now check the site plan overlay (Sheet 9) and storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) to see the overall utility routing relative to the pond.\n\nBut first, let me think about applicability:\n\n1. **EL-2.1** (CTC/Urban Roadway): Valley View Road is a Local Street — NOT APPLICABLE\n2. **EL-2.2** (Hill Country Corridor): Need to check if within 1,000 feet\n3. **EL-2.3, EL-2.4** (CTC/Urban Roadway ROW): NOT APPLICABLE\n4. **EL-2.5-EL-2.8** (Plaza Saltillo TOD, NBG): NOT APPLICABLE (no regulating plan)\n5. **EL-2.9** (10-foot overhead zone): APPLICABLE if overhead utilities remain\n6. **EL-2.10** (Utilities under pond): APPLICABLE — pond is proposed\n7. **EL-2.11, EL-2.12** (Planting zone restrictions): APPLICABLE if ROW street trees exist\n8. **EL-2.13** (Transformers in parkland): APPLICABLE if parkland exists\n9. **EL-2.14** (Light rail corridor): Need to check\n10. **EL-2.15** (Easement encroachment): APPLICABLE — multiple easements recorded\n\n\n11. **EL-2.16** (Easement licensing): APPLICABLE — need to verify. For items 17-23, I should check if power poles are being relocated, whether transformer pads are proposed, and if any tree-related requirements apply. Also need to verify if private utilities are present in ROW, if abandoned utilities are being removed, and whether public utilities in ROW need termination.\n\n19. **EL-2.24** (Table B routing): NOT APPLICABLE since the site is residential MF-2, not exceeding 3 acres in nonresidential zoning.\n\nTo complete my review, I need to examine the site plan, storm sewer plan, utility tap public plan, and electrical details sheets to confirm these determinations. I should also check the cover sheet for Hill Country Roadway status and review the Master Comment Report for any outstanding issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6816,"cache_read_input_tokens":55801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6816},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"2ea03fed-c01d-45b4-ade9-a00a6156cc03"}
