{"level":30,"time":1776951812017,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKCDrb4vGTwtbLQJneHJtH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 29 — Addressing Plan\n     2→\n     3→Site plan showing building layouts and individual unit addresses.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Addressing Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, illustrating the layout, numbering, and finished floor elevations of the proposed residential buildings. Its primary purpose is to define the unit addressing scheme, building square footages, and spatial relationships between the structures, property boundaries, and existing site features like easements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   Plan Scale: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50 (Units 101-104)\n    12→*   Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 201-206)\n    13→*   Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 301-305)\n    14→*   Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 401-405)\n    15→*   Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0 (Units 501-504)\n    16→*   Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0 (Units 601-604)\n    17→*   Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0 (Units 701-705)\n    18→*   Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 801-806)\n    19→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    20→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    21→*   Tree Protection (CRZ) Mulch Requirement: 3-inch layer of hardwood mulch\n    22→\n    23→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    24→\n    25→*   **Block 1: drawing** — Main site addressing plan showing the townhome layout, individual unit locations, building dimensions, and property lines. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of buildings, unit addressing sequences, finished floor elevations (FFEs), and locations of surrounding easements and utility infrastructure. \n    26→*   **Block 2: notes** — Information regarding the primary elevation control points for the project. READ the block content for the exact benchmark elevations, datum (NAVD 88), and point descriptions.\n    27→*   **Block 6: text_block** — The legal description of the property being developed. READ the block content for the subdivision name, lot number, and recording information (Volume 73, Page 76).\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes** — Environmental and administrative disclaimers, including fencing installation near trees. READ the block content for hand-digging requirements and mulch specifications inside the Critical Root Zone (CRZ), as well as utility verification responsibilities.\n    29→*   **Blocks 4, 5: various** — Boilerplate and administrative details, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo and the Professional Engineer's seal. READ the block content for the engineer of record's license number (Jason K. Rodgers, 97881) and signature date.\n    30→\n    31→---\n    32→\n    33→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    34→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca44c-cd40-46be-bd59-597db07f0864","uuid":"dc450f14-b696-4441-80d6-9a5132a8f756","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 29 — Addressing Plan\n\nSite plan showing building layouts and individual unit addresses.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Addressing Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, illustrating the layout, numbering, and finished floor elevations of the proposed residential buildings. Its primary purpose is to define the unit addressing scheme, building square footages, and spatial relationships between the structures, property boundaries, and existing site features like easements.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   Plan Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Building 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50 (Units 101-104)\n*   Building 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 201-206)\n*   Building 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 301-305)\n*   Building 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 401-405)\n*   Building 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0 (Units 501-504)\n*   Building 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0 (Units 601-604)\n*   Building 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0 (Units 701-705)\n*   Building 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50 (Units 801-806)\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n*   Tree Protection (CRZ) Mulch Requirement: 3-inch layer of hardwood mulch\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing** — Main site addressing plan showing the townhome layout, individual unit locations, building dimensions, and property lines. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of buildings, unit addressing sequences, finished floor elevations (FFEs), and locations of surrounding easements and utility infrastructure. \n*   **Block 2: notes** — Information regarding the primary elevation control points for the project. READ the block content for the exact benchmark elevations, datum (NAVD 88), and point descriptions.\n*   **Block 6: text_block** — The legal description of the property being developed. READ the block content for the subdivision name, lot number, and recording information (Volume 73, Page 76).\n*   **Block 3: notes** — Environmental and administrative disclaimers, including fencing installation near trees. READ the block content for hand-digging requirements and mulch specifications inside the Critical Root Zone (CRZ), as well as utility verification responsibilities.\n*   **Blocks 4, 5: various** — Boilerplate and administrative details, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo and the Professional Engineer's seal. READ the block content for the engineer of record's license number (Jason K. Rodgers, 97881) and signature date.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951812098,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 3 and identify all notes related to electric transmission lines and transmission clearances. Specifically, look for:\n\n1. Any mention of transmission structures, transmission lines, or transmission easements\n2. Specific clearance distances (25 feet, 20 feet, etc.) mentioned for transmission\n3. Restrictions on digging, grading, trees, or equipment near transmission facilities\n4. Requirements for roads or access corridors in transmission easements\n5. Any references to Austin Energy transmission requirements\n\nProvide the exact text of any notes found related to transmission lines and electrical clearances.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 3, all requested information is consolidated under the section titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** located in the top-center of the document. Below is the exact transcription of these notes, which detail the transmission structures, clearance distances, restrictions, access requirements, and Austin Energy guidelines:\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes**\n1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. Retention ponds, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 25 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust control to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be roll/mount curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    * any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    * any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected.\n    * any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n\n*(The following unnumbered paragraphs immediately follow Note 16 under the same section heading)*\n\nAustin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n\nThe owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n\nAny relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1425,"outputTokens":1167,"totalTokens":6490,"reasoningTokens":3898},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 3 and identify all notes related to electric transmission lines and transmission clearances. Specifically, look for:\n\n1. Any mention of transmission structures, transmission lines, or transmission easements\n2. Specific clearance distances (25 feet, 20 feet, etc.) mentioned for transmission\n3. Restrictions on digging, grading, trees, or equipment near transmission facilities\n4. Requirements for roads or access corridors in transmission easements\n5. Any references to Austin Energy transmission requirements\n\nProvide the exact text of any notes found related to transmission lines and electrical clearances."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-jbRu7WpgR1BuTZBHqBsVeKU4","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:43:32 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-s