{"level":30,"time":1776951841370,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01M9fdhzPzipWisCLL81ufEA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - Sheet 29 is the Addressing Plan. This confirms that unit addresses are shown (Units 101-104, 201-206, etc.). This means new addresses are being created and an addressing plan has been developed. I need to verify if it's been approved by 911 Addressing/Address Management Services.\n\nNow let me assess the AULCC applicability and ROW work. The key question is: are the water/wastewater taps going to involve work in the public ROW that triggers AULCC?\n\nFrom the Land Development Engineering review, it notes that License Agreements and Encroachment Agreements require AULCC submittal and review prior to application. This suggests that if there is any ROW work, it would go through AULCC.\n\nThe water tap on Sheet 20 shows a connection to an existing main in the public ROW. The fire hydrant is also proposed. These are likely to be in the ROW and would trigger AULCC if they exceed the thresholds (300 lf citywide, 25 lf in DAPCZ).\n\nSince this property is NOT in DAPCZ (it's in South Austin), the threshold would be 300 lf. A single water tap (47-70 lf based on the sheet description) plus wastewater connection (likely 50-100 lf) plus fire hydrant installation would probably total less than 300 lf, which would mean NO AULCC is required.\n\nHowever, I need to be careful here because:\n1. The grouping mentions \"water/wastewater/reclaimed water main ASSIGNMENTS\" not taps\n2. I haven't seen confirmation that the ROW work is indeed <300 lf\n3. The project might have other ROW work not yet visible\n\nLet me now systematically go through each checklist item and make determinations:\n\n**EL-3.1 - ESPA**\n- Applicability: YES - new electrical service required\n\n\n- Found: Austin Energy completeness check is complete, but no ESPA approval letter is visible in the materials\n- Status: NOT VERIFIABLE - The completeness check doesn't confirm ESPA approval itself\n\n**EL-3.2 - AEU Clearance**\n- Applicability: YES - all sites served by Austin Energy\n- Found: Austin Energy completeness check complete; no separate AEU clearance letter documented\n- Status: NOT VERIFIABLE - Completeness check alone doesn't demonstrate AEU clearance\n\n**EL-3.3 - Electric Service Availability Letter**\n- Applicability: Only when serving utility is uncertain\n- South Austin is clearly AE service area, no uncertainty\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-3.4 - AE service area note**\n- Applicability: YES - all AE service area sites\n- Found: Sheet 3 contains Austin Energy notes; service area note presence not yet confirmed\n- Status: NEEDS CHECKING - requires explicit verification in the document blocks\n\n**EL-3.5 - Developer responsibility note for conduit**\n- Applicability: YES - new AE infrastructure required\n- Found: Sheet 3, Block 8 includes notes on developer obligations for easements and access, plus erosion control and tree protection requirements\n- Status: NEEDS VERIFICATION - must confirm if conduit requirements and current AE standards are specifically addressed\n\n**EL-3.6 - Four Standard Austin Energy Notes**\n- Applicability: YES - consolidated site plan\n- Found: Sheet 3, Block 8 lists five Austin Energy notes\n- Status: NEEDS VERIFICATION - exact wording must be confirmed against standards\n\n**EL-3.7 - Transformer/pull box design approval**\n- Applicability: YES - new transformers and pull boxes appear on Sheet 21\n- Found: Preliminary electrical design shows these components\n- Status: NOT VERIFIABLE - no Austin Energy approval documentation present, only preliminary design\n\n**EL-3.8 - Guy anchor coordination**\n- Applicability: Only if new driveways near existing guy anchors\n- Status: NEEDS CHECKING - driveway proximity to poles requires verification\n\n**EL-3.9 - Preconstruction meeting note**\n- Applicability: Only if demolition proposed\n- Demolition completed in 2022\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-3.10 - Electrical easement documents**\n- Applicability: Only if new electrical easements required\n- Status: NEEDS CHECKING - proposed infrastructure shown but easement necessity unclear\n\n**EL-3.11 - AE land development application (georeferenced AutoCAD)**\n- Applicability: Only when submitting land development application to AE\n- Status: NEEDS VERIFICATION - Austin Energy completeness review suggests involvement, but formal application submission status uncertain\n\n**EL-3.12 - AE personnel access to facilities**\n- Applicability: Only when development adjacent to existing or proposed AE facilities\n- Status: NEEDS CHECKING - proposed transformers and pull boxes present; access routes need verification\n\n**EL-3.13 - Moonlight tower 100-ft permit**\n- Applicability: Only if moonlight tower nearby\n- Project location in South Austin (Valley View Rd) falls outside traditional moonlight tower zones\n- Status: LIKELY N/A but requires human judgment\n\nMoonlight tower requirements (EL-3.14 and EL-3.15) follow the same applicability and status as EL-3.13. Street light-related items (EL-3.16 through EL-3.22) are all N/A since no street lights appear on the private development plans. Electrical and MEP plan coverage (EL-3.19) needs verification to confirm all utility infrastructure is included across the site frontage, while Great Streets lighting (EL-3.20) doesn't apply given the project's South Austin location outside that boundary.\n\nFor utility clearances, AULCC applicability (EL-3.23) hinges on whether ROW work exceeds 300 linear feet, includes 25+ feet in DAPCZ, or involves pole relocation—likely not triggered if work is under 300 lf with no pole moves. Gattan, telecom, and dry utility clearances (EL-3.24 through EL-3.26) all require confirmation of whether those infrastructure types are actually present or affected. CIP clearance (EL-3.27) is unlikely to apply in South Austin.\n\nThe Additional Review Acknowledgement table (EL-3.29) is mandatory across all sites but wasn't visible in the reviewed cover sheet sections—this is a critical gap. ROW utility coordination (EL-3.28) depends entirely on whether AULCC gets triggered. Street naming (EL-3.30) needs verification since the plans show individual units but don't clearly indicate if named driveways or streets are proposed. Addressing plan approval (EL-3.31) only applies if new addresses are actually required.\n\nFor the 39 new units shown on Sheet 29, each has an individual address assigned, but there's no visible documentation confirming 911 Addressing approval of this plan. The transmission easement present on Sheet 3 Block 20 includes 16 notes, though I need to verify whether all 8 required plat notes per AEDC 1.16.0(8) are actually included. I should cross-reference the standard transmission notes against what's shown and check if additional documentation exists in the Bluebeam link or elsewhere.\n\nLooking at the most critical items, several appear problematic: the Additional Review Acknowledgement table seems absent from Sheet 1 cover despite being mandatory; the ESPA approval letter isn't visible; AEU clearance documentation is missing; and while an Address Validation Letter exists for the 911 Addressing requirement, it doesn't constitute formal approval from 911 Addressing itself. These gaps represent the clearest deficiencies I can identify from the available materials.\n\nFor the remaining items, Austin Energy's notes appear present throughout the sheets, and various requirements either don't apply to this particular site or have been adequately addressed. Now I need to check whether Block 8 contains the exact wording of the four standard Austin Energy notes as specified in the grouping requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4138,"cache_read_input_tokens":69847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4138},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca44c-cd40-46be-bd59-597db07f0864","uuid":"67edeba0-8b5b-4415-882b-18798b6ad758"}
