{"level":30,"time":1776951851213,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. TRANSFORMER PAD LOCATIONS: Identify all transformer pad locations shown on this sheet. For each transformer pad:\n   - Note the exact location (building reference, distance from structures)\n   - Identify any visible clearance zones or fencing\n   - Note if the pad appears to be on customer property or in the public ROW\n   - Identify any adjacent structures, buildings, or fences within 10 feet of the pad\n\n2. ELECTRICAL ROUTING: Describe how electrical lines are routed:\n   - Are all electrical lines underground from buildings to property line?\n   - Are there any overhead electrical lines shown?\n   - Identify the routing path of electrical conduits relative to buildings and parking areas\n\n3. AE EASEMENTS: Look for any marked utility easements or dedicated AE easement areas on the drawing\n\n4. CLEARANCES & ACCESS: Note any visible information about:\n   - Truck access paths to transformer locations\n   - Clearance areas around electrical equipment\n   - Distance from transformers to buildings/structures\n\nPlease provide specific measurements, coordinates, or building references where visible.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39) for Valley View Townhomes, here is the detailed information requested:\n\n### 1. TRANSFORMER PAD LOCATIONS\n\nThere are four distinct \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations identified on this sheet.\n\n*   **Pad 1 (West side, near entrance):**\n    *   **Exact Location:** Located on the west side of the property, west of Bldg. 2 (Unit 201) and south of the main entrance drive.\n    *   **Clearance/Fencing:** There are no visible clearance zone boundaries (dashed lines) or fencing drawn around this pad.\n    *   **Property/ROW:** It appears to be located on customer property, just inside the property boundary line and east of a \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n    *   **Adjacent Structures (<10ft):** Using the 1\"=20' scale, the pad is located extremely close (appears less than 5 feet) to a curved line labeled \"Retaining Wall\". It is approximately 15-20 scale feet from the nearest building wall of Unit 201.\n*   **Pad 2 (Center, between Bldg. 4 and 5):**\n    *   **Exact Location:** Located in the narrow space between the east end of Bldg. 4 (Unit 404) and the west end of Bldg. 5 (Unit 504).\n    *   **Clearance/Fencing:** No visible clearance zones or fencing indicated.\n    *   **Property/ROW:** Located centrally on customer property.\n    *   **Adjacent Structures (<10ft):** Based on the scale, this pad sits in a tight corridor and appears to be less than 10 feet from the exterior side walls of both Unit 404 and Unit 504.\n*   **Pad 3 (Southwest side, near Bldg. 8):**\n    *   **Exact Location:** Located on the west side of Bldg. 8, immediately adjacent to Unit 801.\n    *   **Clearance/Fencing:** No visible clearance zones or fencing indicated.\n    *   **Property/ROW:** Located on customer property.\n    *   **Adjacent Structures (<10ft):** The drawing shows this pad situated almost flush against the exterior wall of Unit 801. The distance is visually less than 5 scale feet.\n*   **Pad 4 (Southeast side, between Bldg. 6 and 7):**\n    *   **Exact Location:** Located in the space between the east end of Bldg. 7 and the west side of Bldg. 6 (near Unit 602/603).\n    *   **Clearance/Fencing:** No visible clearance zones or fencing indicated.\n    *   **Property/ROW:** Located on customer property.\n    *   **Adjacent Structures (<10ft):** Using the scale, this pad appears to be approximately 10 to 15 feet from the nearest walls of the adjacent buildings.\n\n### 2. ELECTRICAL ROUTING\n\n*   **Underground vs. Overhead:** All proposed electrical lines on the site appear to be routed underground. The blue routing lines are explicitly labeled in at least two places as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** (one label is on the far left entering the property, and another is in the center of the site crossing the main driveway). There are no overhead electrical lines, poles, or \"OH\" labels shown for the proposed internal site routing.\n*   **Routing Path:** The electrical routing (shown as solid blue lines) enters the property from the west from an existing point. It connects to an initial \"Electrical Pull Box\". From there, the underground conduit network branches out, primarily running underneath or alongside the internal concrete driveways and parking areas. The lines connect various \"Electrical Pull Box\" locations, route to the four \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, and terminate at points labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"** located on the exterior walls of every building.\n\n### 3. AE EASEMENTS\n\n*   **Findings:** A thorough scan of the document does not reveal any areas explicitly labeled as an \"AE Easement\" or \"Austin Energy Easement\".\n*   **Other Easements Present:** The drawing does show other historical/existing utility easements, such as:\n    *   \"Wastewater Easement\" (far left)\n    *   \"Sidewalk Easement\" (far left)\n    *   \"5' P.U.E.\" (top right)\n    *   \"Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\" (bottom right)\n    *   \"Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\" (bottom center edge)\n    However, no dedicated proposed AE easement boxes or boundaries are designated on this specific sheet.\n\n### 4. CLEARANCES & ACCESS\n\n*   **Truck Access Paths:** There are no specific paths, turning radii, or marked routes delineated for utility truck access from the driveways to any of the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations.\n*   **Clearance Areas:** The drawing does not display any required clearance areas (such as standard 10' front / 3' side clearance boxes) drawn around any of the electrical equipment or transformer pads.\n*   **Distance to Buildings/Structures:** As noted in section 1 (using the provided 1\"=20' scale):\n    *   Pad 1 is <5' from a retaining wall and ~15'-20' from Bldg. 2.\n    *   Pad 2 is <10' from both Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5.\n    *   Pad 3 is <5' (nearly flush) against Bldg. 8.\n    *   Pad 4 is ~10'-15' from Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1549,"outputTokens":1277,"totalTokens":4788,"reasoningTokens":1962},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. TRANSFORMER PAD LOCATIONS: Identify all transformer pad locations shown on this sheet. For each transformer pad:\n   - Note the exact location (building reference, distance from structures)\n   - Identify any visible clearance zones or fencing\n   - Note if the pad appears to be on customer property or in the public ROW\n   - Identify any adjacent structures, buildings, or fences within 10 feet of the pad\n\n2. ELECTRICAL ROUTING: Describe how electrical lines are routed:\n   - Are all electrical lines underground from buildings to property line?\n   - Are there any overhead electrical lines shown?\n   - Identify the routing path of electrical conduits relative to buildings and parking areas\n\n3. AE EASEMENTS: Look for any marked utility easements or dedicated AE easement areas on the drawing\n\n4. CLEARANCES & ACCESS: Note any visible information about:\n   - Truck access paths to transformer locations\n   - Clearance areas around electrical equipment\n   - Distance from transformers to buildings/structures\n\nPlease provide specific measurements, coordinates, or building references where visible."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-g63ymFtWnzOdq2xNrqVMQEr1","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/