{"level":30,"time":1776951853642,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNp1Vs6mpg2EU5ghA4g82C","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 18 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 3: form — Empty block designated for Austin Water review.\n     4→\n     5→AUSTIN WATER\n     6→REVIEW BLOCK\n     7→\n     8→## Block 6: form — Stamp indicating the expiration timeframe for Austin Water approval.\n     9→\n    10→AW EXPIRATION STAMP\n    11→\n    12→THREE YEARS FROM THE\n    13→DATE OF SIGN-OFF\n    14→\n    15→## Block 7: notes — Note stating that the contractor must verify utility locations prior to starting work.\n    16→\n    17→THE CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY ALL VERTICAL AND HORIZONTAL LOCATIONS\n    18→OF EXISTING UTILITIES, BELOW GROUND AND OVERHEAD, PRIOR TO STARTING\n    19→ONSITE UTILITY WORK.\n    20→\n    21→## Block 9: notes — Note detailing the requirement for new water meters to conform with Austin Water's automated metering infrastructure technology.\n    22→\n    23→AUTOMATED METERING INFRASTRUCTURE: EFFECTIVE MARCH 2022, NEW WATER\n    24→METERS INSTALLED SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE WITH AW'S AUTOMATED\n    25→METERING INFRASTRUCTURE TECHNOLOGY, AND WITH THE APPLICABLE STANDARD\n    26→PRODUCT LIST. APPLICANTS FILING A SITE PLAN OR SUBDIVISION PLAN WILL BE\n    27→REQUIRED TO COORDINATE WITH THE AUSTIN WATER PLAN REVIEWER FOR DETAILS\n    28→ON APPROVAL AND INSTALLATION.\n    29→\n    30→## Block 11: notes — General notes regarding the responsibilities of the engineer, the use of electronic files, and a disclaimer from Austin Water.\n    31→\n    32→GENERAL NOTES\n    33→\n    34→ALL RESPONSIBILITY FOR THE ADEQUACY OF THESE PLANS REMAINS WITH THE ENGINEER. APPROVAL OF\n    35→THESE PLANS BY THE CITY OF AUSTIN DOES NOT REMOVE THESE RESPONSIBILITIES.\n    36→\n    37→\"REVIEWED BY AUSTIN WATER\" APPLIES ONLY TO AW PUBLIC INFRASTRUCTURE, ALL OTHER WATER AND\n    38→WASTEWATER INFRASTRUCTURE INSIDE PRIVATE PROPERTY ARE UNDER THE JURISDICTION OF BUILDING\n    39→INSPECTIONS.\n    40→\n    41→USE OF ELECTRONIC FILES GENERAL DISCLAIMER: USE OF THE ATTACHED FILES IN ANY MANNER INDICATES\n    42→YOUR ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS AS SET FORTH BELOW. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO ALL OF THE\n    43→TERMS AND CONDITIONS, PLEASE CONTACT AUSTIN WATER PIPELINE ENGINEERING, PROJECT COORDINATOR\n    44→PRIOR TO USE OF THE REFERENCED INFORMATION. PLEASE BE ADVISED THAT THE ATTACHED FILES ARE IN A\n    45→FORMAT THAT CAN BE ALTERED BY THE USER. DUE TO THIS FACT, ANY REUSE OF THE DATA WILL BE AT THE\n    46→USER'S SOLE RISK WITHOUT LIABILITY OR LEGAL EXPOSURE TO THE CITY OF AUSTIN AND USER SHALL\n    47→INDEMNIFY AND HOLD HARMLESS THE CITY OF AUSTIN FROM ALL CLAIMS, DAMAGES, LOSSES AND EXPENSES\n    48→INCLUDING ATTORNEY'S FEES ARISING OUT OF OR RESULTING FROM USING THE DIGITAL FILE. IN ADDITION,\n    49→IT IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE USER TO COMPARE ALL DATA WITH THE PDF VERSION OF THIS DRAWING. IN\n    50→THE EVENT THERE IS A CONFLICT BETWEEN THE PDF VERSION DRAWING AND THE ELECTRONIC FILE, THE PDF\n    51→VERSION DRAWING SHALL PREVAIL.\n    52→\n    53→## Block 14: notes — Note providing contact information for the Development Services Department for inspection arrangements and fee payments.\n    54→\n    55→INSPECTION NOTES\n    56→\n    57→PLEASE CONTACT DEVELOPMENT SERVICES DEPARTMENT, SITE AND SUBDIVISION\n    58→INSPECTION AT SITESUBINTAKE@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV FOR ARRANGEMENTS FOR\n    59→PAYMENT OF INSPECTION FEES AND JOB ASSIGNEMENT FOR INSPECTION OF THE\n    60→PUBLIC UTILITIES TO THIS SITE. INSPECTION FEES MUST BE PAID BEFORE ANY\n    61→PRE-CONSTRUCTION MEETING CAN BE CALLED.\n    62→\n    63→## Block 15: notes — Note outlining the contractor's responsibility for handling and disposing of asbestos pipe.\n    64→\n    65→PRIOR TO THE HANDLING AND DISPOSAL OF ASBESTOS PIPE, THE CONTRACTOR'S\n    66→WORK PLAN WILL BE REVIEWED AND COORDINATED THROUGH COA BUILDING\n    67→SERVICES DEPARTMENT - ASBESTOS, LEAD AND MOLD MANAGEMENT GROUP\n    68→MANAGER WHO CAN BE REACHED AT 512-974-7137. IT IS THE CONTRACTOR'S\n    69→RESPONSIBILITY TO UTILIZE A TRAINED, CERTIFIED AND LICENSED ASBESTOS\n    70→ABATEMENT CONTRACTOR IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE FEDERAL, STATE AND LOCAL\n    71→REGULATIONS.\n    72→\n    73→## Block 16: notes — Note regarding modifications to Austin Water signed and stamped sheets and unethical engineering practices.\n    74→\n    75→MODIFICATIONS TO AUSTIN WATER SIGNED AND STAMPED SHEETS ARE NOT\n    76→PERMITTED. ALL DESIGN MODIFICATIONS WILL NEED TO BE SUBMITTED VIA THE ABC\n    77→PORTAL FOR A PLAN CORRECTION OR REVISION. ALL UNETHICAL ENGINEERING\n    78→PRACTICES, INCLUDING MODIFYING CITY STAMPED PLAN SHEETS, SHALL BE\n    79→REPORTED TO THE TEXAS BOARD OF PROFESSIONAL ENGINEERS AND LAND\n    80→SURVEYORS (PELS).\n    81→\n    82→REFERENCE: TEXAS ENGINEERING PRACTICE ACT AND RULES, SUBCHAPTER C:\n    83→PROFESSIONAL CONDUCT AND ETHICS\n    84→\n    85→## Block 18: table — Form for additional review acknowledgement regarding onsite water reuse & AW reclaimed information, automated metering information, and AULCC requirement.\n    86→\n    87→ADDITIONAL REVIEW ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\n    88→\n    89→ONSITE WATER REUSE & AW RECLAIMED INFORMATION\n    90→DOES THIS DEVELOPMENT HAVE A TOTAL GROSS FLOOR BUILDING\n    91→AREA OF 250,000 SQ.FT. OR MORE.\n    92→[ ] YES\n    93→[x] NO\n    94→\n    95→DISTANCE TO NEAREST EXISTING AW RECLAIMED MAIN?\n    96→[ ] 250' OR LESS\n    97→[ ] 251' TO 500'\n    98→[x] GREATER THAN 500'\n    99→\n   100→AUTOMATED METERING INFORMATION\n   101→IS THIS PROJECT WITHIN THE CURRENT SERVICE AREA OF AWs\n   102→DATA COLLECTION UNIT (DCUs), (REFER TO AUTOMATED\n   103→METERING INFRASTRUCTURE NOTE UNDER GENERAL NOTES,\n   104→FOR CLARIFICATION)\n   105→[x] YES\n   106→[ ] NO\n   107→\n   108→DOES THIS PROJECT REQUIRE A DEDICATED EASEMENT FOR\n   109→DCU INFRASTRUCTURE?\n   110→[ ] YES\n   111→[x] NO\n   112→\n   113→AULCC REQUIREMENT\n   114→DOES THIS PROJECT REQUIRE AULCC REVIEW?\n   115→(>300 LF OF W/WW PIPING IN ROW)\n   116→[ ] YES\n   117→[x] NO\n   118→IF YES, PLEASE PROVIDE UCC#______________\n   119→\n   120→## Block 20: table — Table listing proposed product types for water main, wastewater main, reclaimed water main, water service, wastewater service, and reclaimed water service, along with their length, pipe size, and number of metered services.\n   121→\n   122→AW INFRASTRUCTURE INFORMATION\n   123→\n   124→| PROPOSED PRODUCT TYPE\n   125→(TO BE INSTALLED) | LENGTH OF PIPE (L.F.) | SIZE OF PIPE (INCH) | NO. OF METERED\n   126→SERVICES |\n   127→|---|---|---|---|\n   128→| WATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n   129→| WASTEWATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n   130→| RECLAIMED WATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n   131→| WATER SERVICE | 45 | 8\" | 1 |\n   132→| WASTEWATER SERVICE | 7 | 6\" | 1 |\n   133→| RECLAIMED WATER SERVICE | NA | NA | NA |\n   134→\n   135→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca44c-cd40-46be-bd59-597db07f0864","uuid":"cdb4e944-fc34-4a99-8e1c-70a7ca98168f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 18 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 3: form — Empty block designated for Austin Water review.\n\nAUSTIN WATER\nREVIEW BLOCK\n\n## Block 6: form — Stamp indicating the expiration timeframe for Austin Water approval.\n\nAW EXPIRATION STAMP\n\nTHREE YEARS FROM THE\nDATE OF SIGN-OFF\n\n## Block 7: notes — Note stating that the contractor must verify utility locations prior to starting work.\n\nTHE CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY ALL VERTICAL AND HORIZONTAL LOCATIONS\nOF EXISTING UTILITIES, BELOW GROUND AND OVERHEAD, PRIOR TO STARTING\nONSITE UTILITY WORK.\n\n## Block 9: notes — Note detailing the requirement for new water meters to conform with Austin Water's automated metering infrastructure technology.\n\nAUTOMATED METERING INFRASTRUCTURE: EFFECTIVE MARCH 2022, NEW WATER\nMETERS INSTALLED SHALL BE IN CONFORMANCE WITH AW'S AUTOMATED\nMETERING INFRASTRUCTURE TECHNOLOGY, AND WITH THE APPLICABLE STANDARD\nPRODUCT LIST. APPLICANTS FILING A SITE PLAN OR SUBDIVISION PLAN WILL BE\nREQUIRED TO COORDINATE WITH THE AUSTIN WATER PLAN REVIEWER FOR DETAILS\nON APPROVAL AND INSTALLATION.\n\n## Block 11: notes — General notes regarding the responsibilities of the engineer, the use of electronic files, and a disclaimer from Austin Water.\n\nGENERAL NOTES\n\nALL RESPONSIBILITY FOR THE ADEQUACY OF THESE PLANS REMAINS WITH THE ENGINEER. APPROVAL OF\nTHESE PLANS BY THE CITY OF AUSTIN DOES NOT REMOVE THESE RESPONSIBILITIES.\n\n\"REVIEWED BY AUSTIN WATER\" APPLIES ONLY TO AW PUBLIC INFRASTRUCTURE, ALL OTHER WATER AND\nWASTEWATER INFRASTRUCTURE INSIDE PRIVATE PROPERTY ARE UNDER THE JURISDICTION OF BUILDING\nINSPECTIONS.\n\nUSE OF ELECTRONIC FILES GENERAL DISCLAIMER: USE OF THE ATTACHED FILES IN ANY MANNER INDICATES\nYOUR ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS AS SET FORTH BELOW. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO ALL OF THE\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS, PLEASE CONTACT AUSTIN WATER PIPELINE ENGINEERING, PROJECT COORDINATOR\nPRIOR TO USE OF THE REFERENCED INFORMATION. PLEASE BE ADVISED THAT THE ATTACHED FILES ARE IN A\nFORMAT THAT CAN BE ALTERED BY THE USER. DUE TO THIS FACT, ANY REUSE OF THE DATA WILL BE AT THE\nUSER'S SOLE RISK WITHOUT LIABILITY OR LEGAL EXPOSURE TO THE CITY OF AUSTIN AND USER SHALL\nINDEMNIFY AND HOLD HARMLESS THE CITY OF AUSTIN FROM ALL CLAIMS, DAMAGES, LOSSES AND EXPENSES\nINCLUDING ATTORNEY'S FEES ARISING OUT OF OR RESULTING FROM USING THE DIGITAL FILE. IN ADDITION,\nIT IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE USER TO COMPARE ALL DATA WITH THE PDF VERSION OF THIS DRAWING. IN\nTHE EVENT THERE IS A CONFLICT BETWEEN THE PDF VERSION DRAWING AND THE ELECTRONIC FILE, THE PDF\nVERSION DRAWING SHALL PREVAIL.\n\n## Block 14: notes — Note providing contact information for the Development Services Department for inspection arrangements and fee payments.\n\nINSPECTION NOTES\n\nPLEASE CONTACT DEVELOPMENT SERVICES DEPARTMENT, SITE AND SUBDIVISION\nINSPECTION AT SITESUBINTAKE@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV FOR ARRANGEMENTS FOR\nPAYMENT OF INSPECTION FEES AND JOB ASSIGNEMENT FOR INSPECTION OF THE\nPUBLIC UTILITIES TO THIS SITE. INSPECTION FEES MUST BE PAID BEFORE ANY\nPRE-CONSTRUCTION MEETING CAN BE CALLED.\n\n## Block 15: notes — Note outlining the contractor's responsibility for handling and disposing of asbestos pipe.\n\nPRIOR TO THE HANDLING AND DISPOSAL OF ASBESTOS PIPE, THE CONTRACTOR'S\nWORK PLAN WILL BE REVIEWED AND COORDINATED THROUGH COA BUILDING\nSERVICES DEPARTMENT - ASBESTOS, LEAD AND MOLD MANAGEMENT GROUP\nMANAGER WHO CAN BE REACHED AT 512-974-7137. IT IS THE CONTRACTOR'S\nRESPONSIBILITY TO UTILIZE A TRAINED, CERTIFIED AND LICENSED ASBESTOS\nABATEMENT CONTRACTOR IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE FEDERAL, STATE AND LOCAL\nREGULATIONS.\n\n## Block 16: notes — Note regarding modifications to Austin Water signed and stamped sheets and unethical engineering practices.\n\nMODIFICATIONS TO AUSTIN WATER SIGNED AND STAMPED SHEETS ARE NOT\nPERMITTED. ALL DESIGN MODIFICATIONS WILL NEED TO BE SUBMITTED VIA THE ABC\nPORTAL FOR A PLAN CORRECTION OR REVISION. ALL UNETHICAL ENGINEERING\nPRACTICES, INCLUDING MODIFYING CITY STAMPED PLAN SHEETS, SHALL BE\nREPORTED TO THE TEXAS BOARD OF PROFESSIONAL ENGINEERS AND LAND\nSURVEYORS (PELS).\n\nREFERENCE: TEXAS ENGINEERING PRACTICE ACT AND RULES, SUBCHAPTER C:\nPROFESSIONAL CONDUCT AND ETHICS\n\n## Block 18: table — Form for additional review acknowledgement regarding onsite water reuse & AW reclaimed information, automated metering information, and AULCC requirement.\n\nADDITIONAL REVIEW ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\n\nONSITE WATER REUSE & AW RECLAIMED INFORMATION\nDOES THIS DEVELOPMENT HAVE A TOTAL GROSS FLOOR BUILDING\nAREA OF 250,000 SQ.FT. OR MORE.\n[ ] YES\n[x] NO\n\nDISTANCE TO NEAREST EXISTING AW RECLAIMED MAIN?\n[ ] 250' OR LESS\n[ ] 251' TO 500'\n[x] GREATER THAN 500'\n\nAUTOMATED METERING INFORMATION\nIS THIS PROJECT WITHIN THE CURRENT SERVICE AREA OF AWs\nDATA COLLECTION UNIT (DCUs), (REFER TO AUTOMATED\nMETERING INFRASTRUCTURE NOTE UNDER GENERAL NOTES,\nFOR CLARIFICATION)\n[x] YES\n[ ] NO\n\nDOES THIS PROJECT REQUIRE A DEDICATED EASEMENT FOR\nDCU INFRASTRUCTURE?\n[ ] YES\n[x] NO\n\nAULCC REQUIREMENT\nDOES THIS PROJECT REQUIRE AULCC REVIEW?\n(>300 LF OF W/WW PIPING IN ROW)\n[ ] YES\n[x] NO\nIF YES, PLEASE PROVIDE UCC#______________\n\n## Block 20: table — Table listing proposed product types for water main, wastewater main, reclaimed water main, water service, wastewater service, and reclaimed water service, along with their length, pipe size, and number of metered services.\n\nAW INFRASTRUCTURE INFORMATION\n\n| PROPOSED PRODUCT TYPE\n(TO BE INSTALLED) | LENGTH OF PIPE (L.F.) | SIZE OF PIPE (INCH) | NO. OF METERED\nSERVICES |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n| WASTEWATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n| RECLAIMED WATER MAIN | NA | NA | NA |\n| WATER SERVICE | 45 | 8\" | 1 |\n| WASTEWATER SERVICE | 7 | 6\" | 1 |\n| RECLAIMED WATER SERVICE | NA | NA | NA |\n\n","numLines":135,"startLine":1,"totalLines":135}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951853642,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sgd5Yz9svyNwunEkGBUqDB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 28 — Construction Details 7\n     2→\n     3→Construction details for storm drain manholes and catch basins.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides construction details and standard specifications for storm drainage infrastructure, specifically focusing on City of Austin standards for manholes and ParkUSA catch basins. It includes detailed cross-sections, plan views, and dimensional tables to guide the installation of pre-cast and cast-in-place drainage structures.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Catch Basin Concrete Specification:** 4500 PSI design strength at 28 days\n    11→*   **Catch Basin Reinforcement:** Grade 60 steel rebar conforming to ASTM A615\n    12→*   **Catch Basin Castings:** Grey cast iron conforming to ASTM A48-76 Class 30\n    13→*   **Catch Basin Sizes:** Models range from CB-12 (12\"x12\"x24\", 180 lbs) to CB-84 (84\"x84\"x72\", 19,500 lbs)\n    14→*   **Manhole Frame & Cover Size:** 800 mm (32\") or 813 mm (32\")\n    15→*   **Manhole Lid Weights:** 325 N (73 lbs) for cast iron; 778 N (175 lbs) for ductile iron\n    16→*   **Manhole Lid Load Test Requirement:** 20,000-pound proof load test (AASHTO M-306)\n    17→*   **Minimum Manhole Diameter to Pipe Size Ratios:**\n    18→    *   1.2 m (4') dia. for 450 to 600 mm (18\" to 24\") pipes\n    19→    *   1.5 m (5') dia. for 750 to 1.05 m (30\" to 42\") pipes\n    20→    *   1.8 m (6') dia. for 1.2 to 1.6 m (48\" to 64\") pipes\n    21→    *   2.1 m (7') dia. for 1.5 to 1.7 m (60\" to 66\") pipes\n    22→*   **Junction Manhole Intersecting Pipes:** Diagram shows 460 mm (18\"), 610 mm (24\"), and 760 mm (30\") I.D. pipes\n    23→*   **Box Manhole Requirement:** Used for 760 mm (30\") and larger pipes, requiring Class \"A\" Concrete and Item 406 reinforcing steel\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: diagram — Catch Basin Details (ParkUSA)**. Contains a comprehensive dimensional schedule (Models CB-12 through CB-84) alongside structural diagrams. READ for precise model dimensions, grate sizes, weights, and material specifications (concrete, reinforcement, castings). Use VISION to understand the isometric view and section layout parameters (W1, H1, T1, etc.).\n    28→*   **Blocks 8 & 1: diagrams — Pre-Cast Concrete Storm Drain Manhole (City of Austin Std 506S-3, Parts 1 & 2)**. Block 8 shows the primary cross-section and sizing tables, while Block 1 shows adjusting rings and alternative section details. READ Block 8 for minimum manhole diameter to pipe size requirements. Use VISION on both blocks to examine the structural geometry, base slab configurations, and optional step placements.\n    29→*   **Blocks 6, 7 & 9: diagrams — Storm Drain Manhole Ring and 813 mm (32\") Cover (City of Austin Std 503S-4S, Parts 1-3)**. Detailed drawings of the lid, ring section, and manufacturing notes. READ Block 9 for casting specifications, specific weight requirements, and load testing standards. Use VISION on Blocks 6 and 7 to examine the physical lid layout, pick bar placement, and machine finish details.\n    30→*   **Block 5: diagram — Typical Box Manhole for 760 mm (30\") & Larger Pipe (City of Austin Std 506S-5)**. Cross-section of a cast-in-place box manhole with associated construction notes. READ the notes for concrete class and steel reinforcement requirements. Use VISION for spatial layout, reinforcement placement, and mortar details.\n    31→*   **Blocks 2 & 4: diagrams — Manhole Plan Views**. Plan views illustrating a typical manhole at an angle (Block 2) and a typical junction manhole (Block 4) showing intersecting pipe diameters. Use VISION to examine the flow inverts, pipe configurations, and how the manhole invert must be formed to provide smooth water flow.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→- `block-7.md` — diagram: Detailed diagram and specifications for a catch basin, including model dimensions, grate options, an\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"48cf74b1-b476-49ba-9f1c-1c2868a50e63","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-28/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 28 — Construction Details 7\n\nConstruction details for storm drain manholes and catch basins.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides construction details and standard specifications for storm drainage infrastructure, specifically focusing on City of Austin standards for manholes and ParkUSA catch basins. It includes detailed cross-sections, plan views, and dimensional tables to guide the installation of pre-cast and cast-in-place drainage structures.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Catch Basin Concrete Specification:** 4500 PSI design strength at 28 days\n*   **Catch Basin Reinforcement:** Grade 60 steel rebar conforming to ASTM A615\n*   **Catch Basin Castings:** Grey cast iron conforming to ASTM A48-76 Class 30\n*   **Catch Basin Sizes:** Models range from CB-12 (12\"x12\"x24\", 180 lbs) to CB-84 (84\"x84\"x72\", 19,500 lbs)\n*   **Manhole Frame & Cover Size:** 800 mm (32\") or 813 mm (32\")\n*   **Manhole Lid Weights:** 325 N (73 lbs) for cast iron; 778 N (175 lbs) for ductile iron\n*   **Manhole Lid Load Test Requirement:** 20,000-pound proof load test (AASHTO M-306)\n*   **Minimum Manhole Diameter to Pipe Size Ratios:**\n    *   1.2 m (4') dia. for 450 to 600 mm (18\" to 24\") pipes\n    *   1.5 m (5') dia. for 750 to 1.05 m (30\" to 42\") pipes\n    *   1.8 m (6') dia. for 1.2 to 1.6 m (48\" to 64\") pipes\n    *   2.1 m (7') dia. for 1.5 to 1.7 m (60\" to 66\") pipes\n*   **Junction Manhole Intersecting Pipes:** Diagram shows 460 mm (18\"), 610 mm (24\"), and 760 mm (30\") I.D. pipes\n*   **Box Manhole Requirement:** Used for 760 mm (30\") and larger pipes, requiring Class \"A\" Concrete and Item 406 reinforcing steel\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: diagram — Catch Basin Details (ParkUSA)**. Contains a comprehensive dimensional schedule (Models CB-12 through CB-84) alongside structural diagrams. READ for precise model dimensions, grate sizes, weights, and material specifications (concrete, reinforcement, castings). Use VISION to understand the isometric view and section layout parameters (W1, H1, T1, etc.).\n*   **Blocks 8 & 1: diagrams — Pre-Cast Concrete Storm Drain Manhole (City of Austin Std 506S-3, Parts 1 & 2)**. Block 8 shows the primary cross-section and sizing tables, while Block 1 shows adjusting rings and alternative section details. READ Block 8 for minimum manhole diameter to pipe size requirements. Use VISION on both blocks to examine the structural geometry, base slab configurations, and optional step placements.\n*   **Blocks 6, 7 & 9: diagrams — Storm Drain Manhole Ring and 813 mm (32\") Cover (City of Austin Std 503S-4S, Parts 1-3)**. Detailed drawings of the lid, ring section, and manufacturing notes. READ Block 9 for casting specifications, specific weight requirements, and load testing standards. Use VISION on Blocks 6 and 7 to examine the physical lid layout, pick bar placement, and machine finish details.\n*   **Block 5: diagram — Typical Box Manhole for 760 mm (30\") & Larger Pipe (City of Austin Std 506S-5)**. Cross-section of a cast-in-place box manhole with associated construction notes. READ the notes for concrete class and steel reinforcement requirements. Use VISION for spatial layout, reinforcement placement, and mortar details.\n*   **Blocks 2 & 4: diagrams — Manhole Plan Views**. Plan views illustrating a typical manhole at an angle (Block 2) and a typical junction manhole (Block 4) showing intersecting pipe diameters. Use VISION to examine the flow inverts, pipe configurations, and how the manhole invert must be formed to provide smooth water flow.\n\n---\n\n- `block-7.md` — diagram: Detailed diagram and specifications for a catch basin, including model dimensions, grate options, an\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
