{"level":30,"time":1776951858625,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TT9BpbkCr57UHRLeJntjL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YLTLF4sKDEYoKmw3UM3Dde","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the preliminary electrical design plan and report:\n1. What overhead electrical utilities or poles are shown on this sheet, if any? Where are they located relative to the buildings?\n2. What clearance dimensions or measurements are shown between electrical facilities (transformers, pull boxes, meters) and building structures?\n3. Are there any overhead conductor clearance zones or clearance envelope boundaries drawn or labeled on this sheet?\n4. Are there any utility poles shown near or adjacent to the site boundaries?\n5. What is the relationship between any shown utility infrastructure and the transmission easement mentioned in the general notes?\n\nReport what you actually see on the plan - specific locations, dimensions, and clearances depicted."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3189,"cache_read_input_tokens":54547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3189},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"dfbe8fbb-62a0-43f9-8f93-2134384983f7"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951858628,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the preliminary electrical design plan and report:\n1. What overhead electrical utilities or poles are shown on this sheet, if any? Where are they located relative to the buildings?\n2. What clearance dimensions or measurements are shown between electrical facilities (transformers, pull boxes, meters) and building structures?\n3. Are there any overhead conductor clearance zones or clearance envelope boundaries drawn or labeled on this sheet?\n4. Are there any utility poles shown near or adjacent to the site boundaries?\n5. What is the relationship between any shown utility infrastructure and the transmission easement mentioned in the general notes?\n\nReport what you actually see on the plan - specific locations, dimensions, and clearances depicted.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951858893,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WXSYfQK3M17WhPa5Q2SPtp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This vision analysis of Sheet 21 has revealed several critical issues:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Clearances (EL-2.22):** According to UCM § 1.10.4:\n   - Hot-stick side (padlocked side): 10 feet from any adjacent building or structure\n   - Non-operator sides: 3 feet from removable ventilated fence\n   - Operator/control sides: 5 feet from removable ventilated fence\n   - Pads must be at least 2 feet from back of sidewalks\n\nThe vision analysis shows:\n- Pad 1: < 5 feet from a retaining wall, ~15-20 feet from Unit 201\n- Pad 2: < 10 feet from both Unit 404 and Unit 504 (appears to be IN the space between them, so less than 10 feet)\n- Pad 3: < 5 feet (nearly flush) against Unit 801 — this is a CLEAR VIOLATION of the 10-foot clearance\n- Pad 4: ~10-15 feet from buildings (appears acceptable but borderline)\n\nThe vision confirms that Pad 2 and Pad 3 appear to have clearance issues. Pad 3 is particularly problematic as it's nearly flush against Unit 801.\n\n2. **AE EASEMENT (EL-2.22):** No dedicated AE easement is shown on Sheet 21. The vision notes that no \"AE Easement\" or \"Austin Energy Easement\" is labeled. This is concerning because UCM § 1.10.4 and related sections typically require a dedicated AE easement encumbering transformer pad areas.\n\n3. **Underground Electrical Lines (EL-2.1):** The vision confirms that all electrical lines are underground, which is good.\n\n4. **Truck Access (EL-2.22):** No specific truck access paths or turning radii are delineated for utility truck access to transformer pads. \n\nThe pads may lack adequate AE-truck-accessible paths as required by UCM § 1.3.16, which could be a significant deficiency. Next, I should examine the landscape plan on Sheet 31 to assess street trees and planting zones.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2097,"cache_read_input_tokens":69565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2097},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"4b118ab3-e099-458b-bfac-fa07aa1f5a95"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951858903,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WXSYfQK3M17WhPa5Q2SPtp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me examine the landscape plan for street trees and planting zones:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2097,"cache_read_input_tokens":69565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2097},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"4e29621f-beeb-4827-913f-bd654cd0b7f3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951859040,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Please examine this General Notes sheet and provide a detailed description of all text content related to: (1) Electric transmission structures, lines, or easements on or near the site - any mentions of voltage levels (69 kV, 138 kV, 345 kV), towers, poles, clearances, or transmission easement boundaries; (2) Electric utility notes regarding Austin Energy, AE, overhead lines, or underground conduit; (3) Any safety requirements or construction restrictions related to electric utilities. Provide the exact text of these notes if visible.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan General Notes sheet, here is the exact transcription and description of all text content related to electric transmission structures, electric utility notes, and related safety/construction restrictions. \n\nPlease note: Specific voltage levels (e.g., 69 kV, 138 kV, 345 kV) are **not** explicitly mentioned in the text of these notes.\n\n### 1. \"Electric Transmission Notes\"\nThis section is located in the top-right quadrant of the sheet. It contains 16 numbered items and five unnumbered paragraphs detailing strict clearances, safety requirements, and operational restrictions near transmission facilities. \n\n**Exact Transcription:**\n> \"1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n> 2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n> 3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505 7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n> 4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n> 7. No staging areas, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 25 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n> 8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n> 9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n> 10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n> 11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be machine roll/drop.\n> 12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n> 13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n> 14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n> 15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n> 16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\nDirectly below item 16 in the same column, there are five unnumbered paragraphs. *(Note: These paragraphs are a nearly verbatim duplication of the numbered \"Electric Notes\" found on the left side of the page, transcribed in Section 2 below).*\n\n> \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n> \n> The owner/developer of this subdivision/site shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n> \n> The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n> \n> The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n> \n> Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner/developer's expense.\"\n\n### 2. \"Electric Notes\"\nThis section is located in the left-center column of the sheet, directly below \"Site Plan Release Notes.\" It outlines general responsibilities regarding Austin Energy (AE) overhead and underground facilities. \n\n**Exact Transcription:**\n> \"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n> 2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/site shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n> 3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n> 4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n> 5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### 3. Additional Safety & Utility Mentions\n*   **General Construction Notes (Item 2):** Requires coordinating with the state utility dig line prior to commencement: \n    > \"Contractor shall call Texas 811 (811 or 1-800-344-8377) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\"\n*   **Bottom Center Logo:** A prominent logo for **\"Texas 811\"** is displayed with the text: \n    > \"Call Before You Dig!!\"\n\n### Summary of Key Quantitative Clearances/Restrictions Noted:\n*   **25 Feet:** Minimum clearance from the base of transmission structures/poles for planting trees (Note 1), digging/grading (Notes 2 & 15), staging areas/dumpsters/aerial equipment (Note 7), and sprinklers (Note 14).\n*   **20 Feet:** OSHA requirement for clearance from energized transmission lines during construction (Note 3); minimum distance for fire hydrants from any transmission structure (Note 13).\n*   **10 Feet:** Distance at which barricades must be erected from electric transmission structures during construction (Note 4); radius of responsibility for initial tree pruning/removal around the centerline of proposed overhead electric facilities (Electric Note 3).\n*   **46,000 lbs:** The structural support capacity required for roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement (Note 12).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1422,"outputTokens":2053,"totalTokens":6580,"reasoningTokens":3105},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine this General Notes sheet and provide a detailed description of all text content related to: (1) Electric transmission structures, lines, or easements on or near the site - any mentions of voltage levels (69 kV, 138 kV, 345 kV), towers, poles, clearances, or transmission easement boundaries; (2) Electric utility notes regarding Austin Energy, AE, overhead lines, or underground conduit; (3) Any safety requirements or construction restrictions related to electric utilities. Provide the exact text of these notes if visible."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-09V97Vgspcz57AFUg2j4FaJT","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:44:19 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::nnvwq-1776951784350-a4b73821f820"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on 