{"level":30,"time":1776951862542,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mNTmf1jsuvQKKf59kkXd6","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md:7:FYI: If the number of dwelling units changes before payment is made, before the site plan is approved or after it is approved, it is the applicant's responsibility to notify PARD and the case manager in order to have the cost estimate revised. The note on the coversheet must also reflect the correct number of dwelling units paid for and be consistent with all other site plan sheets.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md:10:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/11-aw-utility-development-services.md:8:U1: The site is within an area of capacity concern for wastewater service. The landowner must obtain City approval of a Service Extension Request for wastewater service. For more information pertaining to the Service Extension Request process and submittal requirements contact the Austin Water SER team at ser@austintexas.gov. Austin Water reserves the right to make additional comments and to establish other requirements with the Service Extension Request review.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/11-aw-utility-development-services.md:12:U1: The review comments will be satisfied once Pipeline Engineering has approved the water and wastewater utility plan. For plan review status, contact Dan Lofton with Pipeline Engineering at (512)972-0234 or Daniel.Lofton@austintexas.gov.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/overview.md:11:   Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md:36:U0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md:46:a. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Services Department.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md:47:b. Approval of this Site Plan does not include Building and Fire Code approval nor building permit approval. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:48:* U0: Parallel parking shall be the default configuration of all on-street parking. Back-in angled parking must be approved by the City Transportation Engineer or applicable Director. Head-in angled parking is prohibited as an on-street parking type. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:78:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:107:* U1: Comment remains. Waiver request approved, please pay waiver fee. Please ensure sidewalk meets TCM 4.1.3, “Meandering paths should avoid sharp turns or transitions and gradually transition no more than 1 ft. off path per 5 ft. of sidewalk length and maintain a straight section no less than the width of the sidewalk between transitions.”\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:36:* U0: Free standing dry stacked rock walls are not acceptable in any SCM. Grouted rock walls are acceptable only if the design includes an impermeable barrier such as an approved geomembrane liner or reinforced concrete retaining wall.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:45:* U1: Comment remains, the 25-foot drainage easement is located on your site plans property. You are required to demonstrate adequate conveyance of the offsite flow going through your property. You also cannot have a retaining wall within a drainage easement unless it has been approved. If you need to provide the reference sheets, please do so. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:69:* U1: Comment pending. We still need an analysis of the existing channel on the site. If you are planning to discharge to it, we will need to ensure it has capacity. Please note that your outfall is within an electrical easement. You will need to provide approval from the easements’ owner to do this. Please note the intent of this code is also to cause no adverse impact to your neighbors.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:109:* U0: Due to the proximity of proposed retaining wall to the ROW, public easement, and/or the neighboring property, this plan needs to be reviewed by the Land Development Engineering division of the Transportation and Public Works Department. Please email PDFs of the plan set to elizabeth.robinson@austintexas.gov and copy this reviewer. This comment will be cleared once an approval memo is provided.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:112:* U1: FYI applies until approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md:23:  (1) The site plan application has been approved; or \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md:34:* The site plan will be approved when all requirements from each review discipline have been addressed.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/01-general-information-and-case-manager-review.md:64:* U0: Add the following approval block to lower right of coversheet only:\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:10:* U0: Payment of the site plan environmental inspection fee is required prior to permit/site plan approval. The fee is payable through the AB+C portal. EV Review will be approved prior to payment of this fee. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this fee has been paid. The case manager will confirm payment of the environmental inspection fee prior to permit issuance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:15:* U0: Payment of the landscape inspection fee is required prior to permit/site plan approval. The fee is payable through the AB+C portal. EV Review will be approved prior to payment of this fee. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this fee has been paid. The case manager will confirm payment of the landscape inspection fee prior to permit issuance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:20:* U0: Provide a fiscal estimate for erosion/sedimentation controls and revegetation based on ECM Appendix S-1. For sites with a limit of construction greater than one acre, the fiscal estimate must include a $3000 per acre of LOC clean-up fee. The approved amount must be posted with the City prior to permit/site plan approval. [LDC 25-8-186, ECM 1.2.1, ECM Appendix S-1] \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:22:U01: The ESC fiscal estimate has been approved. Contact the Fiscal Office at fiscalsurety@austintexas.gov for ESC fiscal posting instructions. EV Review will be approved prior to posting of ESC fiscal. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this posting has occurred. The case manager will confirm posting of ESC fiscal prior to permit issuance.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:3:*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:12:Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/12-water-quality-review.md:55:* U1: Comment pending environmental approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:70:Excessive pruning constitutes removal of a regulated tree per Land Development Code 25-8-603. Pruning shall conform to the most recent ANSI A300 pruning standard. Not more than twenty-five percent of the foliage shall be removed within an annual growing season. Failure to account for the particular branch structure of any regulated tree may result in a plan revision or project delay if approved plans require pruning that would not comply with crown preservation requirements."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca44c-cd40-46be-bd59-597db07f0864","uuid":"4df7f8c9-4130-4c00-b09e-2f52a41f917e","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md:7:FYI: If the number of dwelling units changes before payment is made, before the site plan is approved or after it is approved, it is the applicant's responsibility to notify PARD and the case manager in order to have the cost estimate revised. The note on the coversheet must also reflect the correct number of dwelling units paid for and be consistent with all other site plan sheets.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md:10:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/11-aw-utility-development-services.md:8:U1: The site is within an area of capacity concern for wastewater service. The landowner must obtain City approval of a Service Extension Request for wastewater service. For more information pertaining to the Service Extension Request process and submittal requirements contact the Austin Water SER team at ser@austintexas.gov. Austin Water reserves the right to make additional comments and to establish other requirements with the Service Extension Request review.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/11-aw-utility-development-services.md:12:U1: The review comments will be satisfied once Pipeline Engineering has approved 