roval. The fee is payable through the AB+C portal. EV Review will be approved prior to payment of this fee. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this fee has been paid. The case manager will confirm payment of the landscape inspection fee prior to permit issuance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:20:* U0: Provide a fiscal estimate for erosion/sedimentation controls and revegetation based on ECM Appendix S-1. For sites with a limit of construction greater than one acre, the fiscal estimate must include a $3000 per acre of LOC clean-up fee. The approved amount must be posted with the City prior to permit/site plan approval. [LDC 25-8-186, ECM 1.2.1, ECM Appendix S-1] \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:22:U01: The ESC fiscal estimate has been approved. Contact the Fiscal Office at fiscalsurety@austintexas.gov for ESC fiscal posting instructions. EV Review will be approved prior to posting of ESC fiscal. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this posting has occurred. The case manager will confirm posting of ESC fiscal prior to permit issuance.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:3:*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:12:Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/12-water-quality-review.md:55:* U1: Comment pending environmental approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:70:Excessive pruning constitutes removal of a regulated tree per Land Development Code 25-8-603. Pruning shall conform to the most recent ANSI A300 pruning standard. Not more than twenty-five percent of the foliage shall be removed within an annual growing season. Failure to account for the particular branch structure of any regulated tree may result in a plan revision or project delay if approved plans require pruning that would not comply with crown preservation requirements.","numLines":27}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951862989,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WXSYfQK3M17WhPa5Q2SPtp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011ojPYrLAFipRdntTwc497d","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. ROW STREET TREES: Are there any trees shown in the public right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public streets?\n   - If so, identify their locations, species, and spacing\n   - Note if any planting zones, root barriers, or \"Street Tree Utility Gap\" areas are marked\n   - Describe the width and location of any designated utility exclusion zones or planting zone boundaries\n\n2. UTILITY INFRASTRUCTURE IN LANDSCAPE AREAS: Identify the locations of:\n   - Water (W) lines shown on the landscape plan\n   - Storm Drain (SD) lines\n   - Overhead Electric (OHE) lines\n   - Any notation about utilities routing through planting zones or landscape areas\n\n3. UTILITY EASEMENTS SHOWN: Identify and describe any utility easements depicted on the landscape plan:\n   - Location and width\n   - Whether they contain utilities\n   - Whether structures, paving, or landscaping are shown within easement boundaries\n\n4. TREE WELLS & ELECTRICAL OUTLETS: Look for any tree wells (circular areas with planting) shown on the plan:\n   - Are any electrical outlets or electrical conduit runs shown to tree well locations?\n   - Describe the location and proximity to other utilities\n\n5. LANDSCAPE FEATURES NEAR UTILITIES: Describe any landscaping, fencing, or structures shown within or near utility corridors or easements\n\nPlease provide specific building/zone references and measurements where visible on the drawing."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2097,"cache_read_input_tokens":69565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2097},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"78323ac2-ff16-4ca4-ac32-0288b2f7e7c8"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951862993,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. ROW STREET TREES: Are there any trees shown in the public right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public streets?\n   - If so, identify their locations, species, and spacing\n   - Note if any planting zones, root barriers, or \"Street Tree Utility Gap\" areas are marked\n   - Describe the width and location of any designated utility exclusion zones or planting zone boundaries\n\n2. UTILITY INFRASTRUCTURE IN LANDSCAPE AREAS: Identify the locations of:\n   - Water (W) lines shown on the landscape plan\n   - Storm Drain (SD) lines\n   - Overhead Electric (OHE) lines\n   - Any notation about utilities routing through planting zones or landscape areas\n\n3. UTILITY EASEMENTS SHOWN: Identify and describe any utility easements depicted on the landscape plan:\n   - Location and width\n   - Whether they contain utilities\n   - Whether structures, paving, or landscaping are shown within easement boundaries\n\n4. TREE WELLS & ELECTRICAL OUTLETS: Look for any tree wells (circular areas with planting) shown on the plan:\n   - Are any electrical outlets or electrical conduit runs shown to tree well locations?\n   - Describe the location and proximity to other utilities\n\n5. LANDSCAPE FEATURES NEAR UTILITIES: Describe any landscaping, fencing, or structures shown within or near utility corridors or easements\n\nPlease provide specific building/zone references and measurements where visible on the drawing.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951864198,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Examine the General Notes sheet and identify all notes related to Austin Energy and electrical utilities. Specifically:\n1. Are all four Standard Austin Energy Notes present and verbatim? (The four required notes are: (1) AE tree pruning rights; (2) owner/developer obligation to provide additional easements; (3) owner responsibility for erosion control, revegetation, tree protection within 10 feet of overhead electrical centerlines; (4) owner responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA/City/state clearances)\n2. Is there a note stating the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n3. Is there a note stating the developer is responsible for designing and constructing all conduit and related infrastructure to current Austin Energy Electric Service Standards?\n4. List all electric transmission notes present on the sheet.\n5. Provide the exact text of any electric or Austin Energy-related notes found.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided General Notes sheet, here are the findings regarding your specific questions about Austin Energy and electrical utility notes:\n\n**1. Are all four Standard Austin Energy Notes present and verbatim?**\nYes, all four standard notes are present. In fact, they are printed twice on this sheet: once under the heading \"**Electric Notes**\" (as numbered items 1 through 4) and a second time as unnumbered paragraphs at the bottom of the \"**Electric Transmission Notes**\" section. \n*   *(1) AE tree pruning rights:* Present. (See Electric Note 1)\n*   *(2) owner/developer obligation to provide additional easements:* Present. (See Electric Note 2)\n*   *(3) owner responsibility for erosion control, revegetation, tree protection within 10 feet of overhead electrical centerlines:* Present. (See Electric Note 3)\n*   *(4) owner responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA/City/state clearances:* Present. (See Electric Note 4)\n\n**2. Is there a note stating the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?**\nNo. After thoroughly scanning the entire document, there is no note specifically stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area.\n\n**3. Is there a note stating the developer is responsible for designing and constructing all conduit and related infrastructure to current Austin Energy Electric Service Standards?**\nNo. There is no note explicitly stating this requirement on this sheet.\n\n**4 & 5. List all electric transmission notes present on the sheet and provide the exact text.**\nBelow is the exact, character-by-character transcription of the two relevant sections found on the document: \"**Electric Notes**\" and \"**Electric Transmission Notes**\".\n\n***\n\n### Electric Notes\n1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n\n### Electric Transmission Notes\n1. **No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement.** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be inverted curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors). *(Note: transcribed exactly as printed, including the unbalanced trailing parenthesis)*\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n\n*(Directly following note 16, there are five unnumbered paragraphs under the same heading. They are duplicates of Electric Notes 1-5):*\n\nAustin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n\nThe owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n\nAny relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1494,"outputTokens":1849,"totalTokens":7495,"reasoningTokens":4152},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the General Notes sheet and identify all notes related to Austin Energy and electrical utilities. Specifically:\n1. Are all four Standard Austin Energy Notes present and verbatim? (The four required notes are: (1) AE tree pruning rights; (2) owner/developer obligation to provide additional easements; (3) owner responsibility for erosion control, revegetation, tree protection within 10 feet of overhead electrical centerlines; (4) owner responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA/City/state clearances)\n2. Is there a note stating the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n3. Is there a note stating the developer is responsible for designing and constructing all conduit and related infrastructure to current Austin Energy Electric Service Standards?\n4. List all electric transmission notes present on the sheet.\n5. Provide the exact text of any electric or Austin Energy-related notes found."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-sCh3hX6SCHcR9UoXHYgKmjAa","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:44:24 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-mat