{"level":30,"time":1776951865755,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Locate all transformer pads on the electrical site plan. For each transformer pad, document: (1) its location relative to buildings and parking areas, (2) the approximate distance from the nearest building structure or parking area, (3) whether any utility easement boundaries are shown, (4) any notation of Austin Energy or AE easements, (5) access paths to the pad.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" there are four designated electrical transformer pads. Here are the specific details requested for each:\n\n**Transformer Pad 1 (Top-Left / Northwest portion of the site)**\n*   **Location relative to buildings and parking areas:** Located on the western edge of the site, west of the northern end of Bldg. 2 and northwest of Bldg. 8. It sits in a landscaped area between the western property line and the paved drive aisle/parking spaces.\n*   **Approximate distance:** Visually estimated using the 1\" = 20' scale, the pad is approximately 5 to 10 feet west of the nearest parking space curb edge.\n*   **Utility easement boundaries:** The pad is enclosed within a dashed rectangular boundary. There is a text callout pointing directly to this boundary labeled exactly as `\"Vault Easement\"`. It is also located within a larger area denoted by dashed lines labeled `\"Sidewalk Easement\"`.\n*   **Notation of Austin Energy or AE easements:** There are no explicit notations mentioning \"Austin Energy\" or \"AE\" near this pad; the specific terminology used is \"Vault Easement.\"\n*   **Access paths to the pad:** The pad is situated immediately adjacent to the paved drive aisle/parking area, suggesting direct access from the paved surface, though no separate, distinct access pathway is drawn.\n\n**Transformer Pad 2 (Middle-Right / East-central portion of the site)**\n*   **Location relative to buildings and parking areas:** Located on the eastern side of the main central drive aisle, situated in the space between the parking spaces for Bldg. 4 (units 403/404) and the side facade of Bldg. 5 (units 503/504).\n*   **Approximate distance:** Visually estimated using the scale, the pad is situated very close to the pavement, approximately 2 to 5 feet east of the back-of-curb of the parking/drive aisle.\n*   **Utility easement boundaries:** There are no distinct dashed boundary lines or specific easement labels drawn directly enclosing this pad.\n*   **Notation of Austin Energy or AE easements:** None are visible.\n*   **Access paths to the pad:** The pad is immediately adjacent to the main paved drive aisle and parking area, implying direct access from the pavement.\n\n**Transformer Pad 3 (Bottom-Left / Southwest portion of the site)**\n*   **Location relative to buildings and parking areas:** Located on the western edge of the site, directly west of Bldg. 8 (units 801/802), between the building facade and the western property boundary.\n*   **Approximate distance:** Visually estimated using the scale, the pad is approximately 5 to 10 feet west of the western wall of Bldg. 8. It is not adjacent to vehicular parking areas.\n*   **Utility easement boundaries:** Similar to Pad 1, this pad is enclosed within a dashed rectangular boundary. There is a text callout pointing to this boundary labeled exactly as `\"Vault Easement\"`.\n*   **Notation of Austin Energy or AE easements:** There are no explicit notations mentioning \"Austin Energy\" or \"AE\"; it uses the term \"Vault Easement.\"\n*   **Access paths to the pad:** This pad is physically separated from the vehicular drive aisles by Bldg. 8. It is located adjacent to a dashed line labeled `\"Sidewalk Easement\"`, indicating pedestrian access path routing.\n\n**Transformer Pad 4 (Bottom-Center / Southeast-central portion of the site)**\n*   **Location relative to buildings and parking areas:** Located in a landscaped island area dividing the parking zones between Bldg. 7 (units 703/704) and Bldg. 6 (units 601/602).\n*   **Approximate distance:** Visually estimated using the scale, the pad is approximately 5 to 10 feet from the adjacent parking space curbs for both Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7.\n*   **Utility easement boundaries:** There are no distinct dashed boundary lines or specific easement labels drawn directly enclosing this pad.\n*   **Notation of Austin Energy or AE easements:** None are visible.\n*   **Access paths to the pad:** The pad is located immediately adjacent to the paved drive aisles and parking spaces serving buildings 6 and 7, implying direct access from the paved surfaces.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1388,"outputTokens":931,"totalTokens":4551,"reasoningTokens":2232},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does