{"level":30,"time":1776951872085,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":1,"prompt":"Examine the cover sheet carefully and identify:\n1. Is there an \"Additional Review Acknowledgement\" table that lists all applicable external reviews, approvals, or permits (TxDOT, railroad, gas, TCEQ, water districts, easement acquisition, county approval, MUD approval, Texas Department of Health, non-occupancy letter, service extension approval, Planning and Development Review Department approvals)?\n2. If the table exists, is it complete with all required external reviews and approvals for this 39-unit townhome development?\n3. Are there any blank spaces or unchecked items in the table?\nProvide the exact text or structure of any acknowledgement table found.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (1)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951874118,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 3 (General Notes) carefully and identify all notes related to Austin Energy or electric utilities. Specifically:\n\n1. Are there four Standard Austin Energy Notes present? If so, what is the exact text of each one? The four required notes are:\n   - (1) AE tree pruning rights in easements\n   - (2) Owner/developer obligation to provide additional easements or access for AE facilities\n   - (3) Owner responsibility for erosion control, revegetation, and tree protection within 10 feet of proposed overhead electrical facility centerlines\n   - (4) Owner responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA/City/state clearances near overhead power lines\n\n2. Is there a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n\n3. Is there a developer responsibility note about designing and constructing conduit and infrastructure to Austin Energy standards?\n\n4. Are there any other electric utility notes or transmission easement notes visible on this sheet?\n\nProvide the exact text of all electric-related notes found on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 3 - General Notes), here are the findings regarding Austin Energy and electric utility notes:\n\n### 1. Are the four Standard Austin Energy Notes present?\n**Yes.** The four required standard notes are present under the heading **\"Electric Notes\"** (located in the middle-left column of the sheet). They are also repeated verbatim as unnumbered paragraphs immediately below the \"Fire Department\" section. \n\nHere is the exact text of the four notes:\n\n*   **Note 1:** \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Note 2:** \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Note 3:** \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n### 2. Is there a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n**No.** There is no specific note on this sheet explicitly stating, \"This site lies within the Austin Energy service area\" (though it is strongly implied by the presence of the other required Austin Energy notes). \n\n### 3. Is there a developer responsibility note about designing and constructing conduit?\n**No.** There are no notes visible on this sheet regarding the developer's responsibility to design or construct conduit and infrastructure to Austin Energy standards.\n\n### 4. Are there any other electric utility notes or transmission easement notes?\n**Yes.** There is an additional electric note under the **\"Electric Notes\"** section, as well as a large section specifically titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** at the top middle of the page. \n\n**From the \"Electric Notes\" section:**\n*   **Note 5:** \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n**From the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:**\nHere is the exact transcription of the 16 notes provided in this section:\n\n1.  \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n2.  \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n3.  \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n4.  \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n5.  \"Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n6.  \"Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n7.  \"Fill/spoils, materials, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n8.  \"24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n9.  \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n10. \"Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n11. \"Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structure/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be rollover curbing.\"\n12. \"Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n13. \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n14. \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n15. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n16. \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    *   any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    *   any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, no\n    *   any structures, including, but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n*(Note: Typo ending in \"no\" on bullet 2 of note 16 is transcribed exactly as written on the document).*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1526,"outputTokens":1492,"totalTokens":7171,"reasoningTokens":4153},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 3 (General Notes) carefully and identify all notes related to Austin Energy or electric utilities. Specifically:\n\n1. Are there four Standard Austin Energy Notes present? If so, what is the exact text of each one? The four required notes are:\n   - (1) AE tree pruning rights in easements\n   - (2) Owner/developer obligation to provide additional easements or access for AE facilities\n   - (3) Owner responsibility for erosion control, revegetation, and tree protection within 10 feet of proposed overhead electrical facility centerlines\n   - (4) Owner responsibility for maintaining NESC/OSHA/City/state clearances near overhead power lines\n\n2. Is there a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n\n3. Is there a developer responsibility note about designing and constructing conduit and infrastructure to Austin Energy standards?\n\n4. Are there any other electric utility notes or transmission easement notes visible on this sheet?\n\nProvide the exact text of all electric-related notes found on this sheet."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-bYY5exrGHbbqljUliPA3R9JE","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:44:34 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::qntp7-1776951795233-c1ef296913e1"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 3 - General Notes), here are the findings regarding Austin Energy and electric utility notes:\n\n### 1. Are the four Standard Austin Energy Notes present?\n**Yes.** The four required standard notes are present under the heading **\"Electric Notes\"** (located in the middle-left column of the sheet). They are also repeated verbatim as unnumbered paragraphs immediately below the \"Fire Department\" section. \n\nHere is the exact text of the four notes:\n\n*   **Note 1:** \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Note 2:** \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   **Note 3:** \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n### 2. Is there a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area?\n**No.** There is no specific note on this sheet explicitly stating, \"This site lies within the Austin Energy service area\" (though it is strongly implied by the presence of the other required Austin Energy notes). \n\n### 3. Is there a developer responsibility note about designing and constructing conduit?\n**No.** There are no notes visible on this sheet regarding the developer's responsibility to design or construct conduit and infrastructure to Austin Energy standards.\n\n### 4. Are there any other electric utility notes or transmission easement notes?\n**Yes.** There is an additional electric note under the **\"Electric Notes\"** section, as well as a large section specifically titled **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"** at the top middle of the page. \n\n**From the \"Electric Notes\" section:**\n*   **Note 5:** \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n**From the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section:**\nHere is the exact transcription of the 16 notes provided in this section:\n\n1.  \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n2.  \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n3.  \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n4.  \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n5.  \"Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n6.  \"Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n7.  \"Fill/spoils, materials, equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n8.  \"24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n9.  \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n10. \"Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n11. \"Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structure/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be rollover curbing.\"\n12. \"Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n13. \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n14. \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n15. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n16. \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    *   any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    *   any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, no\n    *   any structures, including, but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n*(Note: Typo ending in \"no\" on bullet 2 of note 16 is transcribed exactly as written on the document).*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1526,"outputTokens":1492,"totalTokens":7171,"reasoningTokens":4153},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"