ransmission poles and structures.\"\n15. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n16. \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    *   any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    *   any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, no\n    *   any structures, including, but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n*(Note: Typo ending in \"no\" on bullet 2 of note 16 is transcribed exactly as written on the document).*"}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776951874562,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0124KhZ3vT8J7CgdKA1okiet","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see from the master comment report that:\n1. Austin Energy Design Criteria are listed but there's no mention of ESPA approval specifically\n2. The Electric Review section just links to preliminary design requirements\n3. The completeness check report showed \"AE completeness check complete\" but that's not the same as ESPA approval\n\nNow let me compile my final findings. Based on all my research, here are the deficiencies I can confidently identify:\n\n1. **EL-3.29 - Additional Review Acknowledgement table** - The comprehensive table required per UCM 2.5.1.F should be on the cover sheet or transmittal listing all external approvals (TxDOT, railroad, gas, water district, TCEQ, etc.). What IS present is only a partial Austin Water form on Sheet 18. This is a FAIL.\n\n2. **EL-3.1 - ESPA** - No evidence of ESPA submission/approval visible in materials. Austin Energy completeness check being complete does not constitute ESPA approval documentation. This is NOT VERIFIABLE.\n\n3. **EL-3.2 - AEU Clearance** - No separate AEU clearance letter visible. Completeness check alone is not sufficient documentation. This is NOT VERIFIABLE.\n\n4. **EL-3.31 - Addressing plan approval** - Sheet 29 shows addresses but no documentation that the addressing plan has been approved by 911 Addressing/Address Management Services. The grouping specifically states that an Address Validation Letter does not constitute approval. This is NOT VERIFIABLE unless I can find an approval letter.\n\n5. **EL-3.4, EL-3.5 - Service area note and developer responsibility note** - Need to verify these are actually present and verbatim. From Block 8, I can see Austin Energy notes, but need to verify the specific text matches requirement.\n\n6. **EL-3.32 - Transmission easement plat notes** - Need to verify all 8 required notes per AEDC 1.16.0(8) are present on Sheet 3, Block 20.\n\n\nBased on what I can definitively confirm, the clear failure is EL-3.29 due to the missing comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table on the cover sheet—only a partial water/wastewater table appears on Sheet 18. For EL-3.1, EL-3.2, and EL-3.31, I cannot verify the required documentation since ESPA approval, AEU clearance, and addressing plan approval letters are not present in the materials.\n\nSeveral items warrant N/A status: the serving utility is unambiguously within AE's service area, no new driveways are shown near guy anchors, demolition was already completed in 2022, and no street lights are proposed in the design. EL-3.13, EL-3.14, and EL-3.15 regarding moonlight towers require human review since they're unlikely in South Austin but need verification. The project falls outside the Great Streets boundary, eliminating EL-3.20 from consideration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3531,"cache_read_input_tokens":81717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3531},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca44c-cd40-46be-bd59-597db07f0864","uuid":"532a171e-75c9-4dca-92e9-bbe75d0b82ec"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951877421,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze this electrical design plan carefully. I need to know:\n\n1. Are underground electric lines shown routed through or directly under any parking spaces? If so, describe their location and routing path.\n\n2. What is the location of transformer pads relative to buildings and parking areas? Are they within the property or in the ROW?\n\n3. Are there any power poles or overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If so, where are they located relative to the buildings?\n\n4. Can you identify the routing of electrical service lines from the buildings to the property line? Are they underground or overhead?\n\n5. Are there any easement boundaries shown for electrical infrastructure? Are they properly labeled?\n\nPlease provide specific locations, building references, and any dimensions or measurements visible that are relevant to utility routing compliance.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are underground electric lines shown routed through or directly under any parking spaces? If so, describe their location and routing path.**\nYes, underground electric lines (denoted by the solid blue lines and explicitly labeled with a callout as \"Underground Electric Line\" on the western side of the site) are routed extensively beneath the paved drive aisles and parking areas.\n*   **Routing Path:** The main electrical conduit forms a perimeter loop around the development. It runs continuously under the southern drive aisle (south of Bldg 8, Bldg 7, and Bldg 6), up the eastern drive aisle (east of Bldg 6 and Bldg 5), across the northern drive aisle (north of Bldg 5, Bldg 3, and Bldg 1), and connects back through the main entrance drive aisle on the west side.\n*   While they primarily follow the center or edges of the drive aisles, they pass directly in front of and behind the parking spaces that line these aisles throughout the entire complex.\n\n**2. What is the location of transformer pads relative to buildings and parking areas? Are they within the property or in the ROW?**\nThere are three identified \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations. All of them are located **within the property boundary** (inside the heavy dashed property line), not in the Right-Of-Way (ROW). They are situated in landscape islands adjacent to the parking/drive aisles:\n*   **Pad 1:** Located on the west side of the property, directly west of **Bldg 2**, situated in an island near the main entrance drive.\n*   **Pad 2:** Located on the southwest corner of the property, directly west of **Bldg 8**.\n*   **Pad 3:** Located on the eastern side of the property, in an island situated between **Bldg 4** and **Bldg 6**, near the eastern perimeter drive aisle.\n\n**3. Are there any power poles or overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If so, where are they located relative to the buildings?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are present, but they are located **outside the property boundary**.\n*   A line designated by the standard overhead symbol (dashed line with text \"- OHE -\") runs north-to-south along the far western edge of the document, entirely within the Right-Of-Way (ROW) of Valley View Road.\n*   There are no overhead electric lines shown crossing over the property or the buildings; all on-site routing is shown as underground.\n\n**4. Can you identify the routing of electrical service lines from the buildings to the property line? Are they underground or overhead?**\n*   **Routing:** Each building (Bldg 1 through Bldg 8) has a blue rectangular box attached to it labeled \"Electrical Meters\". From these meters, solid blue lines route outwards to connect to the main electrical loop running under the drive aisles. The main loop then connects to the utility infrastructure in the western ROW (Valley View Road) via lines entering near the southwest corner (west of Bldg 8) and the main entrance (west of Bldg 2).\n*   **Type:** All service lines from the buildings to the main loop, and from the loop to the property line, are shown as **underground** (indicated by the solid blue lines and the corresponding \"Underground Electric Line\" label).\n\n**5. Are there any easement boundaries shown for electrical infrastructure? Are they properly labeled?**\nYes, utility and specific electrical easements are shown and labeled along the perimeter boundaries of the property:\n*   **Southern Boundary:** There is a clearly labeled dashed line noting a **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"** running along the southern property line.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** There is a general utility easement labeled **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) running along the northern property line.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** There is a labeled **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** running along the eastern property line.\n*   Specific, individualized cut-out easements dedicated solely to the internal transformer pads are not distinctly dimensioned or separately labeled in this specific site plan view, though the pads are positioned adjacent to or within the general setback/easement areas.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1473,"outputTokens":953,"totalTokens":5673,"reasoningTokens":3247},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Analyze this electrical design plan carefully. I need to know:\n\n1. Are underground electric lines shown routed through or directly under any parking spaces? If so, describe their location and routing path.\n\n2. What is the location of transformer pads relative to buildings and parking areas? Are they within the property or in the ROW?\n\n3. Are there any power poles or overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If so, where are they located relative to the buildings?\n\n4. Can you identify the routing of electrical service lines from the buildings to the property line? Are they underground or overhead?\n\n5. Are there any easement boundaries shown for electrical infrastructure? Are they properly labeled?\n\nPlease provide specific locations, building references, and any dimensions or measurements visible that are relevant to utility routing compliance."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-jgaivO7Akkbf97qxkSODnCcw","timestamp":{},"modelId