{"level":30,"time":1776951878294,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01J5fz5yo1Qnn3nAbZVUkq26","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the site demolition notes on Sheet 8 (Block 9):\n\n1. Install all tree protection fencing as per sheet 5.\n2. All demolition within the full critical root zone of preserved trees to be performed with hand tools only.\n3. A pre-construction meeting with the Environmental Inspector is required prior to any site disturbance.\n4. Contractor is responsible for locating and abandoning existing private water and wastewater lines. All abandoned piping is to be plugged.\n5. Existing trees on the site are to remain unless noted otherwise.\n6. Contractor is to remove all demolished materials from site, and to repair or replace any materials or items designated to remain.\n7. Demolition work should be completed prior to any commencement of work on the proposed building.\n8. Contractor to remove gas & water meters and return meters to respective utility companies.\n9. Contractor to use \"Sidewalk Closed\" signs during sidewalk closures.\n10. Notify contracting officer and arborist before commencement of work which may jeopardize the well-being of any trees to remain.\n\n**CRITICAL:** These demolition notes do NOT address transmission line safety requirements. According to the grouping EL-1.18:\n\n\"Demolition plan sequence notes do not address required safety clearances from transmission lines: pre-construction safety meeting ≥48 hours before work, barricades erected 10 ft from all transmission structures (including guys and anchors) within the construction area, warning signs under overhead facilities, and prohibition on materials or spoils storage within the transmission easement\"\n\nThe demolition notes include:\n- ✗ Pre-construction safety meeting (Item 3 mentions meeting with Environmental Inspector, but NOT with Austin Energy ≥48 hours before work)\n- ✗ Barricades 10 ft from transmission structures\n- ✗ Warning signs under overhead facilities\n- ✗ Prohibition on materials/spoils in transmission easement\n\n\n- ✗ **EL-1.18 appears to be a FAIL** - the demolition plan notes are missing all four transmission line safety requirements.\n\nI need to check if there's a staging or construction plan that addresses these items, and review what the master comment report indicates about these gaps.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2649,"cache_read_input_tokens":57935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2649},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"3c3ce56a-66bf-4cbd-b5aa-071a105bb2fd"}
