{"level":30,"time":1776951892529,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BK3nYwn7AsW6FScrku5Qgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This gives me crucial information:\n\n1. **Underground electric lines** are routed through/under parking spaces (throughout the entire complex in drive aisles and parking areas)\n2. **Transformer pads** are located within the property (not in ROW) - 3 pads identified\n3. **Overhead electric lines** are only in the ROW (western edge, Valley View Road)\n4. **Service lines from buildings** are underground\n5. **Easements shown**: Various utility easements along perimeters\n\nNow I need to check if this violates any of the EL-2 checklist items. The key regulatory framework check:\n\nFrom facts.md:\n- **Zoning:** MF-2 (not a CTC site)\n- **Regulating Plan:** None (not Plaza Saltillo TOD or NBG)\n- **Street:** Valley View Road is a \"Local Street\" (ASMP Level 1) — NOT a CTC or Urban Roadway\n- **Hill Country Roadway:** Not within 1,000 feet of the named corridors\n\nFrom the grouping (EL-2.md):\n- **EL-2.1 applies only to CTC or Urban Roadway sites under Subchapter E** — This site fronts a LOCAL STREET (Valley View Road), not a CTC or Urban Roadway. **NOT APPLICABLE**\n- **EL-2.2 applies only to Hill Country Roadway Corridors** — This site is NOT within 1,000 feet of Loop 360, RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway. **NOT APPLICABLE**\n- **EL-2.3, EL-2.4 apply only to CTC/Urban Roadway sites** — NOT APPLICABLE\n- **EL-2.5, EL-2.6, EL-2.7 apply only to Plaza Saltillo TOD** — NOT APPLICABLE\n\n\n- **EL-2.8 applies only to NBG district** — NOT APPLICABLE\n- **EL-2.9 applies only when overhead utilities remain on CTC/Urban/TOD/NBG frontages** — The overhead lines are in the ROW only, not crossing buildings. Need to verify building-to-property-line compliance.\n- **EL-2.10 applies when utilities are under detention ponds** — YES, this site has a biofiltration/detention pond. Need to check if utilities are routed underneath.\n- **EL-2.11, EL-2.12 apply to ROW** — Need to evaluate these for the overhead lines in the western ROW.\n- **EL-2.13 applies when transformers are in parkland** — The pads are on private property, not in parkland. Need to verify parkland boundaries.\n- **EL-2.14 applies to light rail proximity** — No light rail mentioned. Probably NOT APPLICABLE.\n- **EL-2.15 applies when easement boundaries encroach into proposed ROW** — Need to check if any easements conflict with ROW.\n- **EL-2.16 applies when items are placed within utility easements without licenses** — Need to check if structures/paving/landscaping are within easements without licenses.\n- **EL-2.17 applies to private utilities in public ROW** — The underground lines appear to be from the utility provider (AE\n\n), not private utilities. Need to verify.\n- **EL-2.18 applies to abandoned utilities with clearance conflicts** — Need to check demolition plans for abandoned utilities.\n- **EL-2.19 applies to existing public/franchise utilities in ROW not terminated** — Need to check demolition/ROW plans.\n- **EL-2.20 applies to underground storage tanks** — facts.md says none registered. **NOT APPLICABLE**\n- **EL-2.21 applies to power pole relocation** — Need to check if poles are relocated.\n- **EL-2.22 applies to transformer pads** — YES, I found 3 transformer pads. Need to verify they meet all UCM requirements.\n- **EL-2.23 applies to tree wells with electrical outlets** — Need to check landscape plan.\n- **EL-2.24 applies to utilities under parking on Table**\n\nThe site's MF-2 zoning with 39 units across 2.16 acres falls short of the ≥3 acre nonresidential threshold for Table B applicability, so this standard likely doesn't apply here. Priority areas to examine include utility routing beneath the biofiltration pond, transformer pad compliance with clearance and easement requirements, and the missing easement depictions noted in the facts.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1497,"cache_read_input_tokens":59519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1497},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"0a5d7a1f-e16e-4ac7-bf78-b6255ac6a932"}
