{"level":30,"time":1776951897417,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016YyfZjBWxhmyBcX3p4oqPG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 29 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This is an addressing plan showing the layout of multiple townhome buildings. It includes the lot lines, building footprints, unit numbers, unit square footages, finished floor elevations (FFE), and various easements. Key details include Building 1-8, units 101-104, 201-206, 301-305, 401-405, 501-504, 601-604, 701-705, and 801-806.\n     4→\n     5→This plan shows a site layout with multiple residential buildings and associated site features. \n     6→- Building footprints are shown with unit numbers, area (sf), and finished floor elevations (FFE).\n     7→- Patios are indicated for ground floor units.\n     8→- Various easements are shown, including drainage, water, and wastewater easements.\n     9→- Property lines and adjacent property zoning information are provided.\n    10→- Existing infrastructure like water manholes, fire hydrants, gas meters, and utility lines (water, wastewater, electric) are indicated.\n    11→- A scale bar indicates 1\" = 20'.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 2: notes — Notes regarding the installation of fences near trees and a disclaimer about the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans.\n    14→\n    15→**Fence Note**\n    16→Post holes that are to be installed near a trees Critical Root Zone (CRZ) will be dug by hand. No machinery is allowed in the CRZ and any work done in this area shall be done by hand. Add a 3-inch layer of hardwood mulch in the CRZ prior to commencing construction activities.\n    17→\n    18→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    19→\n    20→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    21→\n    22→## Block 3: notes — Information regarding the benchmarks used for elevation control on the project.\n    23→\n    24→**Benchmarks**\n    25→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    26→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    27→\n    28→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    29→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    30→\n    31→## Block 6: text_block — The legal description of the property being developed.\n    32→\n    33→**Legal Description**\n    34→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    35→\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"8c9d0c23-e1d7-462a-a302-29d0dde4c524","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 29 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This is an addressing plan showing the layout of multiple townhome buildings. It includes the lot lines, building footprints, unit numbers, unit square footages, finished floor elevations (FFE), and various easements. Key details include Building 1-8, units 101-104, 201-206, 301-305, 401-405, 501-504, 601-604, 701-705, and 801-806.\n\nThis plan shows a site layout with multiple residential buildings and associated site features. \n- Building footprints are shown with unit numbers, area (sf), and finished floor elevations (FFE).\n- Patios are indicated for ground floor units.\n- Various easements are shown, including drainage, water, and wastewater easements.\n- Property lines and adjacent property zoning information are provided.\n- Existing infrastructure like water manholes, fire hydrants, gas meters, and utility lines (water, wastewater, electric) are indicated.\n- A scale bar indicates 1\" = 20'.\n\n## Block 2: notes — Notes regarding the installation of fences near trees and a disclaimer about the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans.\n\n**Fence Note**\nPost holes that are to be installed near a trees Critical Root Zone (CRZ) will be dug by hand. No machinery is allowed in the CRZ and any work done in this area shall be done by hand. Add a 3-inch layer of hardwood mulch in the CRZ prior to commencing construction activities.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 3: notes — Information regarding the benchmarks used for elevation control on the project.\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 6: text_block — The legal description of the property being developed.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
