{"level":30,"time":1776951911599,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XgB2h6yyGVLWQkaCSjnvLy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Land Development Engineering Review\n     2→\n     3→*Informational requirements for License Agreements, Encroachment Agreements, Easement Releases, and ROW Vacations.*\n     4→\n     5→**CC Land Development Engineering** – Land Development Engineering\n     6→\n     7→Comments below are Informational (website). License Agreements, Encroachment Agreements and Easement Releases are separate applications which should run concurrent with your development application. Please note that License Agreements (LA) and Encroachment Agreement (EA) require an AULCC submittal and review prior to LA and EA application submittals\n     8→\n     9→A **License Agreement** is needed for items that will be temporarily placed within the City of Austin current or proposed Right of Way (ROW) or Easement(s) and shall be executed prior to issuance of the development permit. City Code Chapter 14-11 \n    10→➢ Contact LandManagement2@austintexas.gov for pre-submittal meetings as needed. Reference website for application requirements\n    11→➢ Current and proposed easements should be shown on all site plan sheets.\n    12→➢ Site Plan set is required to include License Agreement Plan Sheet and Landscape Sheets, and Irrigation Sheets if these appurtenances are proposed.\n    13→➢ Typical License Agreements include, but not limited to, awnings, canopies, benches, bike racks, trash receptacles, street trees, landscaping, irrigation, outdoor dining areas, and pedestrian lighting. (See website for list of most common appurtenance that we license.)\n    14→\n    15→An **Encroachment Agreement** is needed for items that will be permanently placed within the City of Austin Right of Way (ROW) and shall be executed prior to issuance of the development permit. Encroachment Agreements require approval by City Council. City Code Chapter 14-11 \n    16→➢ Contact LandManagementROW@austintexas.gov for pre-submittal meetings as needed.\n    17→➢ Reference website for application requirements\n    18→➢ Typical items include, but not limited to, Sky Bridges, Balconies, Underground Parking Garages, etc..\n    19→\n    20→For development applications needing City of Austin **Easement Releases** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\n    21→➢ Contact LandManagement@austintexas.gov for initial consultation as needed.\n    22→➢ Reference website for application requirements.\n    23→\n    24→For development applications needing City of Austin **ROW Vacations** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\n    25→➢ Contact LandManagementROW@austintexas.gov for initial consultation as needed.\n    26→➢ Reference website for application requirements.\n    27→➢ City Council approval is required.\n    28→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"5c4ec9a3-5601-4af5-a207-04fb16df7aef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/04-land-development-engineering-review.md","content":"# Land Development Engineering Review\n\n*Informational requirements for License Agreements, Encroachment Agreements, Easement Releases, and ROW Vacations.*\n\n**CC Land Development Engineering** – Land Development Engineering\n\nComments below are Informational (website). License Agreements, Encroachment Agreements and Easement Releases are separate applications which should run concurrent with your development application. Please note that License Agreements (LA) and Encroachment Agreement (EA) require an AULCC submittal and review prior to LA and EA application submittals\n\nA **License Agreement** is needed for items that will be temporarily placed within the City of Austin current or proposed Right of Way (ROW) or Easement(s) and shall be executed prior to issuance of the development permit. City Code Chapter 14-11 \n➢ Contact LandManagement2@austintexas.gov for pre-submittal meetings as needed. Reference website for application requirements\n➢ Current and proposed easements should be shown on all site plan sheets.\n➢ Site Plan set is required to include License Agreement Plan Sheet and Landscape Sheets, and Irrigation Sheets if these appurtenances are proposed.\n➢ Typical License Agreements include, but not limited to, awnings, canopies, benches, bike racks, trash receptacles, street trees, landscaping, irrigation, outdoor dining areas, and pedestrian lighting. (See website for list of most common appurtenance that we license.)\n\nAn **Encroachment Agreement** is needed for items that will be permanently placed within the City of Austin Right of Way (ROW) and shall be executed prior to issuance of the development permit. Encroachment Agreements require approval by City Council. City Code Chapter 14-11 \n➢ Contact LandManagementROW@austintexas.gov for pre-submittal meetings as needed.\n➢ Reference website for application requirements\n➢ Typical items include, but not limited to, Sky Bridges, Balconies, Underground Parking Garages, etc..\n\nFor development applications needing City of Austin **Easement Releases** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\n➢ Contact LandManagement@austintexas.gov for initial consultation as needed.\n➢ Reference website for application requirements.\n\nFor development applications needing City of Austin **ROW Vacations** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\n➢ Contact LandManagementROW@austintexas.gov for initial consultation as needed.\n➢ Reference website for application requirements.\n➢ City Council approval is required.\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776951914169,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the preliminary electrical design plan and report:\n1. What overhead electrical utilities or poles are shown on this sheet, if any? Where are they located relative to the buildings?\n2. What clearance dimensions or measurements are shown between electrical facilities (transformers, pull boxes, meters) and building structures?\n3. Are there any overhead conductor clearance zones or clearance envelope boundaries drawn or labeled on this sheet?\n4. Are there any utility poles shown near or adjacent to the site boundaries?\n5. What is the relationship between any shown utility infrastructure and the transmission easement mentioned in the general notes?\n\nReport what you actually see on the plan - specific locations, dimensions, and clearances depicted.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the answers to your questions:\n\n**1. What overhead electrical utilities or poles are shown on this sheet, if any? Where are they located relative to the buildings?**\nOverhead electrical utilities are indicated by a line labeled **\"- OHE -\"** located along the far western edge of the drawing (left side), running generally parallel to \"Valley View Road\". This overhead line is located entirely outside the primary building area, separated by a property boundary and a \"Sidewalk Easement\". There are no overhead electrical lines shown crossing over or located within the immediate vicinity of the proposed buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8). The electrical infrastructure servicing the buildings directly is depicted with blue lines, which are explicitly labeled in at least one instance as an **\"Underground Electric Line\"**.\n\n**2. What clearance dimensions or measurements are shown between electrical facilities (transformers, pull boxes, meters) and building structures?**\nThere are **no explicit clearance dimensions or measurements** (e.g., specific distance values with dimension lines) shown on this sheet between the electrical facilities (labeled as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\", \"Electrical Pull Box\", and \"Electrical Meters\") and the building structures. The drawing indicates general placement using blue symbols and callout text, but lacks dimensional specifications for required clearances.\n\n**3. Are there any overhead conductor clearance zones or clearance envelope boundaries drawn or labeled on this sheet?**\n**No**, there are no overhead conductor clearance zones, clearance envelope boundaries, or similar restrictive areas explicitly drawn or labeled anywhere on this sheet.\n\n**4. Are there any utility poles shown near or adjacent to the site boundaries?**\n**Yes**, the presence of utility poles is strongly implied adjacent to the western site boundary (along Valley View Road) by the line clearly labeled **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric). Standard line types for overhead utilities typically connect utility poles, although there are no distinct symbols specifically text-labeled as \"Utility Pole\" in that area.\n\n**5. What is the relationship between any shown utility infrastructure and the transmission easement mentioned in the general notes?**\nBased *strictly* on the text visible in this document, **there is no \"transmission easement\" mentioned in the general notes, utility notes, or any other visible text blocks on this sheet.** The visible notes refer to water/wastewater branches, utility verifications, and geologic inspections. Various other easements are visible on the plan (e.g., \"5' P.U.E\", \"Wastewater Easement\", \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\"), but none are designated as a \"transmission easement\". Therefore, a relationship cannot be established from this specific sheet.","provide