{"level":30,"time":1776951919398,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and report:\n1. Is a transmission easement or transmission facility shown on the site plan? If so, where is it located and how is it depicted (labeled line, hatched area, etc.)?\n2. Are there any transmission poles, transmission structures, or electric transmission facilities visible or labeled on the site plan?\n3. What easements are shown on the plan? List each one and its location on the site.\n4. Are there any graphic boundaries, clearance zones, or buffer areas shown around any utilities?\n5. Are there any overhead electric lines shown near or adjacent to buildings or other structures?\n6. What is shown in the northeast corner of the site (based on the general notes, there is drainage activity there)?\n\nProvide specific location references and what you actually see depicted on the plan.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (9)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776951919674,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. ROW STREET TREES: Are there any trees shown in the public right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road or other public streets?\n   - If so, identify their locations, species, and spacing\n   - Note if any planting zones, root barriers, or \"Street Tree Utility Gap\" areas are marked\n   - Describe the width and location of any designated utility exclusion zones or planting zone boundaries\n\n2. UTILITY INFRASTRUCTURE IN LANDSCAPE AREAS: Identify the locations of:\n   - Water (W) lines shown on the landscape plan\n   - Storm Drain (SD) lines\n   - Overhead Electric (OHE) lines\n   - Any notation about utilities routing through planting zones or landscape areas\n\n3. UTILITY EASEMENTS SHOWN: Identify and describe any utility easements depicted on the landscape plan:\n   - Location and width\n   - Whether they contain utilities\n   - Whether structures, paving, or landscaping are shown within easement boundaries\n\n4. TREE WELLS & ELECTRICAL OUTLETS: Look for any tree wells (circular areas with planting) shown on the plan:\n   - Are any electrical outlets or electrical conduit runs shown to tree well locations?\n   - Describe the location and proximity to other utilities\n\n5. LANDSCAPE FEATURES NEAR UTILITIES: Describe any landscaping, fencing, or structures shown within or near utility corridors or easements\n\nPlease provide specific building/zone references and measurements where visible on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (labeled Sheet 28 of 35, project Valley View Townhomes), here is the detailed information requested:\n\n**1. ROW STREET TREES**\n*   **Locations & Species:** There are no trees explicitly shown *outside* the property line within the public right-of-way (ROW) of Valley View Road. However, immediately adjacent to the ROW, on the property side, there is a designated \"STREET YARD\" (shaded area designated by Key Note 'H.2'). Within this area, several proposed trees are shown. They are labeled with the designations 'SY' (Street Yard Tree) and 'M' (Mitigation Tree).\n*   **Spacing:** There are no specific spacing dimensions or measurements provided between these trees on this plan.\n*   **Planting Zones/Barriers:** There are no notations indicating root barriers or \"Street Tree Utility Gap\" areas.\n*   **Utility Exclusion Zones:** No designated utility exclusion zones or planting zone boundaries with specific widths are marked in this area.\n\n**2. UTILITY INFRASTRUCTURE IN LANDSCAPE AREAS**\n*   **Water (W) lines:** A water line (marked '-W-') is shown entering the site from Valley View Road on the west, passing through the 'H.2' (Street Yard) landscape area. Another '-W-' line runs horizontally along the southern boundary of the site, within a landscaped strip containing trees and sod.\n*   **Storm Drain (SD) lines:** Storm drain lines (marked '-SD-') primarily run east-west through the central paved driveway/parking area. An additional '-SD-' line runs horizontally along the southern boundary, parallel to the water line, within the landscape area.\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE) lines:** An overhead electric line (marked '-OHE-') is shown running horizontally along the extreme southern boundary line of the property.\n*   **Notations:** There are no explicit text notations on this sheet discussing the routing of utilities through planting zones or landscape areas; the routing is only shown graphically via the linetypes.\n\n**3. UTILITY EASEMENTS SHOWN**\n*   No formally labeled utility easements (e.g., standard dashed lines labeled \"10' P.U.E.\" or \"W.W.E.\") are explicitly depicted or dimensioned on this specific landscape plan sheet. While utility lines (W, SD, OHE) are present, their corresponding legal easement boundaries are not marked here.\n\n**4. TREE WELLS & ELECTRICAL OUTLETS**\n*   **Tree Wells:** There are no isolated \"tree wells\" (small, circular planted areas wholly surrounded by paving) shown on this plan. Trees in the parking areas are located within larger landscape islands or peninsulas (designated by Key Note 'H.4' for \"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\").\n*   **Electrical Outlets/Conduit:** There are no electrical outlets, waterproof receptacles, or electrical conduit runs depicted in any of the landscape islands or near any proposed tree locations on this plan.\n\n**5. LANDSCAPE FEATURES NEAR UTILITIES**\n*   **Southern Boundary:** A \"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\" (Key Note 'H.6') runs along the southern property line, directly adjacent to the '-OHE-' (Overhead Electric) line. Immediately inside this fence line, there is a narrow landscape corridor containing 'SOD' (Key Note 'H.7') and several proposed trees. Both a '-W-' (Water) line and an '-SD-' (Storm Drain) line run parallel through this same narrow landscaped corridor, in very close proximity to the proposed trees and the fence.\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road frontage):** A '-W-' (Water) line crosses perpendicularly through the shaded 'H.2' (Street Yard) area. This area contains 'SOD' (Key Note 'H.7') and proposed 'SY' (Street Yard) and 'M' (Mitigation) trees. The water line routes closely past at least one of these proposed street yard trees.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1628,"outputTokens":845,"totalTokens":5015,"reasoningTokens":2542},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually an