{"level":30,"time":1776951921139,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 2 (Plat) carefully and identify:\n\n1. What easements are depicted on this plat? List each easement with:\n   - Description/type (e.g., drainage, utility, greenbelt, transmission)\n   - Width/dimensions if shown\n   - Location on the property\n\n2. Are there any notes on the plat about tree pruning, access, maintenance, or restrictions related to any easements, particularly transmission or drainage easements?\n\n3. What is the source of this plat? Is it the current subdivision plat for the project, or is it a historical plat?\n\n4. Are there any electrical easements shown? If so, describe their size, location, and any associated notes.\n\nProvide the exact location and description of each easement shown.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan document (\"Sheet 2 of 39\"), here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**1. Easements Depicted on the Plat**\nThere are three specific easements explicitly labeled on this plat:\n\n*   **Public Utility Easement (P.U.E.)**\n    *   **Description/Label:** \"5' P.U.E. (Exist)\"\n    *   **Width:** 5 feet\n    *   **Location:** Runs along the entire northern boundary line of both LOT 1 and LOT 2, adjacent to the \"CORTEZ HEIGHTS\" property line.\n*   **Drainage Easement**\n    *   **Description/Label:** \"26' Drainage Easement (Existing)\"\n    *   **Width:** 26 feet\n    *   **Location:** Located within the northern portion of LOT 2.\n*   **Wastewater Easement**\n    *   **Description/Label:** \"10' Wastewater Easement\" (Text is slightly blurry, but this is the most accurate reading)\n    *   **Width:** 10 feet\n    *   **Location:** Located within the southern half of LOT 2, extending westward from the eastern property line (Clawson Road).\n\n**2. Notes on Tree Pruning, Access, Maintenance, or Restrictions**\nThere are **no notes** anywhere on this plat regarding tree pruning, access restrictions, maintenance responsibilities, or specific restrictions related to the transmission or drainage easements. The only text pertaining to easements is in the standard owner's dedication block, which simply states: \"...and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.\"\n\n**3. Source of the Plat (Current vs. Historical)**\nThis is a **historical plat** that has been scanned and inserted into a modern site plan set for reference. \n*   **Evidence of Historical Nature:** The document itself is titled \"TRAVIS COUNTY PLAT VOLUME 73 PAGE 76\" for the \"MECEY SUBDIVISION\". All approval dates, filing dates, and surveyor certifications on the drawing are from the year **1975** (e.g., \"APPROVED FOR ACCEPTANCE Date: 12-11-75\", \"Surveyed Aug. 20, 1975\").\n*   **Evidence of Current Submission:** The historical 1975 scan is framed within a modern title block on the right side by \"Bleyl Engineering\" for a project named \"Valley View Townhomes\", identified as \"Plat\", \"Sheet: 2 of 39\".\n\n**4. Electrical Easements**\nThere are **no explicitly labeled \"electrical\" or \"transmission\" easements** on this plat. \nHowever, there is a **\"5' P.U.E. (Exist)\"** (Public Utility Easement) running along the northern boundary of the lots. Public Utility Easements typically encompass electrical lines along with other standard utilities (telecom, gas, etc.), though the plat does not feature any specific notes, restrictions, or details regarding electrical infrastructure for this 5-foot strip.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1470,"outputTokens":663,"totalTokens":4661,"reasoningTokens":2528},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg