{"level":30,"time":1776951935566,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KcdLNfobkreGnEqKwVLzCy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 12 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 2: drawing — This block contains the main site plan drawing for the project, showing existing and proposed features, contours, drainage details, and utility lines.\n     4→\n     5→Detailed site plan drawing showing building footprints, property lines, existing and proposed contours, storm drainage lines, utility easements, and various infrastructure elements like grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes. The plan includes dimensions, elevations, and specific details for various components.\n     6→\n     7→## Block 3: notes — This block provides the legal description for the property shown in the site plan.\n     8→\n     9→**Legal Description**\n    10→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    11→\n    12→## Block 4: notes — This block lists the benchmarks used for the site plan, including their locations and elevations.\n    13→\n    14→**Benchmarks**\n    15→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    16→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    17→\n    18→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    19→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    20→\n    21→## Block 6: notes — This block contains drainage notes for the site plan, detailing requirements for detention and filtration facilities, utility locations, and curb construction.\n    22→\n    23→**Drainage Notes**\n    24→1. Upon completion of the proposed site improvements, and prior to the release of the Certificate of Occupancy by the Watershed Protection and Development Review Department, the Design Engineer shall certify in writing that the proposed detention and filtration facilities were constructed in conformance with the approved plans.\n    25→2. Contractor shall call One Call Center (472-2822) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\n    26→\n    27→**Curb Note**\n    28→Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n    29→\n    30→## Block 7: notes — This block contains the legend for the site plan, explaining the symbols and line types used in the drawing.\n    31→\n    32→**Legend**\n    33→\n    34→| Symbol | Description |\n    35→|---|---|\n    36→| [solid line with \"700\"] | Existing Contour |\n    37→| [dashed line with \"700\"] | Proposed Contour |\n    38→| [dot with \"698.25\"] | Proposed Spot Elevation |\n    39→| [line with \"700.00\" and \"699.50\"] | Top of Curb / Bottom of Curb |\n    40→| [solid line with \"LOC\"] | Proposed Limits of Construction |\n    41→| [dashed line] | Proposed Storm Drain Line |\n    42→| [arrow pointing left with \"Level Landing\"] | Level Landing (Not to exceed 2% in any Direction) |\n    43→| [arrow pointing down with \"Down\"] | ADA Ramp (Not to exceed 8.33%) |\n    44→\n    45→## Block 8: notes — This block refers to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n    46→\n    47→**Tree List**\n    48→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    49→\n    50→## Block 13: text_block — This block contains a disclaimer about the location of existing utilities and the contractor's responsibility to verify them.\n    51→\n    52→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    53→\n    54→## Block 14: text_block — This block provides the scale for the site plan drawing.\n    55→\n    56→[Scale bar showing 0, 20', 40']\n    57→**Scale 1\" = 20'**\n    58→\n    59→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"b62fc27f-16f3-418f-ad2f-0dee62755e1b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 12 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 2: drawing — This block contains the main site plan drawing for the project, showing existing and proposed features, contours, drainage details, and utility lines.\n\nDetailed site plan drawing showing building footprints, property lines, existing and proposed contours, storm drainage lines, utility easements, and various infrastructure elements like grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes. The plan includes dimensions, elevations, and specific details for various components.\n\n## Block 3: notes — This block provides the legal description for the property shown in the site plan.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 4: notes — This block lists the benchmarks used for the site plan, including their locations and elevations.\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 6: notes — This block contains drainage notes for the site plan, detailing requirements for detention and filtration facilities, utility locations, and curb construction.\n\n**Drainage Notes**\n1. Upon completion of the proposed site improvements, and prior to the release of the Certificate of Occupancy by the Watershed Protection and Development Review Department, the Design Engineer shall certify in writing that the proposed detention and filtration facilities were constructed in conformance with the approved plans.\n2. Contractor shall call One Call Center (472-2822) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\n\n**Curb Note**\nGrading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n\n## Block 7: notes — This block contains the legend for the site plan, explaining the symbols and line types used in the drawing.\n\n**Legend**\n\n| Symbol | Description |\n|---|---|\n| [solid line with \"700\"] | Existing Contour |\n| [dashed line with \"700\"] | Proposed Contour |\n| [dot with \"698.25\"] | Proposed Spot Elevation |\n| [line with \"700.00\" and \"699.50\"] | Top of Curb / Bottom of Curb |\n| [solid line with \"LOC\"] | Proposed Limits of Construction |\n| [dashed line] | Proposed Storm Drain Line |\n| [arrow pointing left with \"Level Landing\"] | Level Landing (Not to exceed 2% in any Direction) |\n| [arrow pointing down with \"Down\"] | ADA Ramp (Not to exceed 8.33%) |\n\n## Block 8: notes — This block refers to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n\n**Tree List**\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — This block contains a disclaimer about the location of existing utilities and the contractor's responsibility to verify them.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — This block provides the scale for the site plan drawing.\n\n[Scale bar showing 0, 20', 40']\n**Scale 1\" = 20'**\n\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
