trol and tree protection\n  4. Owner responsibility for clearance maintenance\n- Status: PASS\n\n**3. Developer Responsibility Note (EL-3.5)**\n- ✗ NOT FOUND: No note about developer responsibility for conduit/infrastructure to AE standards\n- This is a deficiency\n\n**4. Transmission Easement Notes (EL-3.32)**\n- The plat shows a 5' P.U.E. on northern boundary but no specific transmission easement\n- Sheet 3 shows 16 Electric Transmission Notes with detailed restrictions\n- However, need to verify if these notes adequately address transmission easement requirements\n\n. The vision report lists 16 notes total, but I need to cross-reference against the 8 mandatory notes required by AEDC 1.16.0(8): AE tree pruning rights, additional easement/access provision, erosion control and tree protection responsibilities, clearance maintenance, NESC compliance restrictions, 24-hour AE access, road/driveway capacity requirements (48,000 lb tandem), and 48-hour notice before construction/grading. The notes shown appear to cover these core topics with supplementary provisions.\n\nFor ESPA approval, the Master Comment Report documents Austin Energy's review, but I don't see a formal ESPA approval letter—only a completeness check notation. The clearance requirement may be satisfied by the AE completeness check result, though I should confirm whether this differs from an actual AEU clearance. The Service Availability Letter appears absent from the reviewed documents, though this may not apply if Austin's location within the established Austin Energy service area exempts it from this requirement.\n\nThe Cover Sheet's \"Reviewed By\" section looks incomplete, and I need to verify whether a comprehensive external review acknowledgement table exists covering all relevant agencies like TxDOT, railroad, gas, and TCEQ. Street lighting hasn't appeared in any of the project sheets reviewed so far, so I should determine if this is even part of the scope. For AULCC coordination, since the project involves new electrical infrastructure, I need to check whether the ROW work linear footage triggers AULCC requirements and locate any coordination documentation.\n\nAddressing Plan on Sheet 29 requires verification that it's been approved and all street names are properly reserved. The preconstruction meeting note appears in the transmission documents mentioning a 48-hour safety meeting with the AE, but I should confirm this is properly documented in the project requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1290,"cache_read_input_tokens":64753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1290},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60bcd99d-409f-4cd6-a909-b056cb4b2c38","uuid":"3beb2f1f-bfdd-4980-b5a2-5d93e6fd0a20"}
