st corner reads exactly: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 882 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**(3) Spatial relationships between these areas:**\nNone of the staging, storage, or concrete cleanout areas appear to be located within the boundaries of the identified electrical easements.\n*   The **\"Staging and Storage Area\"** and **\"Concrete Truck Cleanout\"** are positioned exclusively on the far **western** boundary of the project site.\n*   The identified **electrical easements** run exclusively along the **eastern** and **southern** boundaries of the project site.\n*   Therefore, they are physically separated by the entire width/depth of the proposed townhome development footprint (Buildings 2, 4, 3, 5, and 6) and do not overlap."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"648d0ebf-683f-4479-9626-137a793c9299","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan, here are the findings addressing your specific questions:\n\n**(1) Location of staging areas, storage areas, concrete truck cleanout areas, or spoils areas:**\n*   **\"Staging and Storage Area\"**: There is a hatched rectangular area labeled exactly as \"Staging and Storage Area\". It is located on the western side of the site, near the western property boundary, directly west of proposed \"Bldg. 2\" (specifically adjacent to Unit 201).\n*   **\"Concrete Truck Cleanout\"**: There is a small square area labeled exactly as \"Concrete Truck Cleanout\". It is located immediately north of the Staging and Storage Area, also on the western edge of the site, west of proposed \"Bldg. 2\" (specifically adjacent to Unit 202).\n*   No areas labeled as \"spoils\" areas were identified on this plan.\n\n**(2) Boundaries or location of the transmission easement:**\nWhile the specific phrase \"transmission easement\" does not appear on this sheet, there are several labeled electrical easements located along the property boundaries:\n*   **Eastern Boundary**: Running parallel to the eastern property line (right side of the page), there is a boundary line with a label reading exactly: **\"25' Electric and Telephone Easement\"**. Further up along the eastern edge (near Unit 603), another label reads: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 93, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Southern Boundary**: Running along the lower edge of the site plan, there are labels pointing to a dashed line. One reads exactly: **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 & Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** Another label near the southeast corner reads exactly: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 882 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**(3) Spatial relationships between these areas:**\nNone of the staging, storage, or concrete cleanout areas appear to be located within the boundaries of the identified electrical easements.\n*   The **\"Staging and Storage Area\"** and **\"Concrete Truck Cleanout\"** are positioned exclusively on the far **western** boundary of the project site.\n*   The identified **electrical easements** run exclusively along the **eastern** and **southern** boundaries of the project site.\n*   Therefore, they are physically separated by the entire width/depth of the proposed townhome development footprint (Buildings 2, 4, 3, 5, and 6) and do not overlap."}]}
