{"level":30,"time":1776951959426,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012GbDCagB6oiFVfbRReHVfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so block 8 has the Electric Notes (the 5 notes about tree pruning, easements, etc.), and block 19 is the Austin Water letter confirming suitable and sufficient service. Neither of these mention ESPA.\n\nNow, the grouping instructions state:\n- \"ESPA submission normally occurs AFTER DSD site plan approval, not before\" (Exception listed in Common Exception Patterns)\n- \"ESPA must be resubmitted after receiving an Electric Permit number (AEDC 1.4.2.7.A)\"\n\nSo it's expected that ESPA might not be submitted YET (since the site plan hasn't been approved yet - it's still in review). However, the checklist item EL-3.1 says \"Electric Service Planning Application (ESPA) not submitted to Austin Energy for review and approval, OR ESPA approval not documented in the plan set\" and the applicability is \"Only when new or modified electrical service is required.\"\n\nLooking at Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design), there clearly IS new electrical service being proposed (transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground lines). So EL-3.1 is applicable.\n\nThe question is: has ESPA been submitted and approved? The Master Comment Report shows \"AE completeness check complete\" but doesn't say whether ESPA has been submitted.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The grouping says ESPA submission \"normally occurs AFTER DSD approves the site plan\" - so at this stage (site plan still in review), ESPA may not yet be submitted. But the checklist says the deficiency is \"not submitted to Austin Energy for review and approval, or ESPA approval not documented.\" \n\nSo the question is: should ESPA be documented in the plan set or elsewhere at this stage? Let me re-read the requirement more carefully.\n\nThe checklist applicability says \"Only when new or modified electrical service is required\" and the code citation is AEDC 1.4.2.1 which requires submission of ESPA.\n\n\nSince the project is still in site plan review and ESPA typically comes after DSD approval, submitting it now would be premature. The grouping's exception clarifies that ESPA submission follows site plan approval, not the reverse. The applicant hasn't submitted ESPA yet, which aligns with the normal sequence of the approval process.\n\nI'll mark this as not-verifiable since the site plan hasn't been approved and there's no indication of whether ESPA submission is required or planned at this stage. Now checking EL-3.2 for any AEU clearance documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":73112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"89e605af-8f57-44a0-806f-828d22c14385"}
