{"level":30,"time":1776951976775,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and report:\n1. Is a transmission easement or transmission facility shown on the site plan? If so, where is it located and how is it depicted (labeled line, hatched area, etc.)?\n2. Are there any transmission poles, transmission structures, or electric transmission facilities visible or labeled on the site plan?\n3. What easements are shown on the plan? List each one and its location on the site.\n4. Are there any graphic boundaries, clearance zones, or buffer areas shown around any utilities?\n5. Are there any overhead electric lines shown near or adjacent to buildings or other structures?\n6. What is shown in the northeast corner of the site (based on the general notes, there is drainage activity there)?\n\nProvide specific location references and what you actually see depicted on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the detailed findings to answer your questions:\n\n**1. Is a transmission easement or transmission facility shown on the site plan? If so, where is it located and how is it depicted?**\nThere is no easement or facility explicitly labeled with the word \"Transmission\" on this site plan. However, there are local public utility and electric easements shown along the perimeter of the property, depicted primarily with dashed lines outlining the easement areas. (See Question 3 for the specific list of electric-related easements).\n\n**2. Are there any transmission poles, transmission structures, or electric transmission facilities visible or labeled on the site plan?**\nWhile the word \"transmission\" is not used, there are electric structures and overhead lines visible and labeled on the plan:\n*   **\"Power Pole\"**: There are two structures explicitly labeled \"Power Pole\" located along the western property line. One is located in the northwest corner near the upper driveway entrance (\"Construct Type II Driveway\"). The second is located near the southwest corner of the property.\n*   **Overhead Electric Lines**: A line style marked with **\"- OHE -\"** connects these power poles along the western boundary and continues along the southern property boundary.\n*   **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"**: A rectangular pad with this label is shown on the western side of the site, situated in the island area between the upper and lower driveways, directly west of Bldg. 1.\n\n**3. What easements are shown on the plan? List each one and its location on the site.**\nThe following easements are depicted and labeled with text and dashed boundary lines:\n\n*   **West Property Line / Entrance Area:**\n    *   `Wastewater Easement Doc#` (Document number is cut off/illegible) - Located near the northernmost driveway entrance.\n    *   `Sidewalk Easement Doc#` (Document number is cut off/illegible) - Located just south of the northernmost driveway.\n    *   `Sidewalk Easement Doc#` (Document number is cut off/illegible) - Located near the southernmost driveway entrance.\n*   **North Property Line:**\n    *   `5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Runs horizontally along the top (northern) boundary of the site.\n*   **East Property Line:**\n    *   `25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Located in the northeast corner overlapping the detention pond area.\n    *   `25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2010021137 O.P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Located roughly midway down the eastern property boundary.\n    *   `15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Located slightly south of the midway point on the eastern boundary, directly east of Bldg 6.\n    *   `3' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Located slightly south of the midway point on the eastern boundary.\n    *   `5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5168, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.` - Located in the southeast corner.\n*   **South Property Line:**\n    *   `5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.` - Runs horizontally along the bottom (southern) boundary of the site.\n\n**4. Are there any graphic boundaries, clearance zones, or buffer areas shown around any utilities?**\nNo explicit graphic boundaries, clearance zones, drop zones, or buffer areas (such as concentric circles or shaded \"no-build\" zones) are drawn or labeled around the overhead electric lines (\"- OHE -\"), power poles, or the transformer pad. The utility easements themselves represent a legal boundary, but no separate physical safety clearance zones are depicted.\n\n**5. Are there any overhead electric lines shown near or adjacent to buildings or other structures?**\nYes, overhead electric lines labeled **\"- OHE -\"** are shown running along the western and southern perimeter property lines.\n*   **Western boundary:** The \"- OHE -\" line runs outside the new sidewalks and driveways. Building 1 and Building 8 are separated from these lines by the driveways and parking aisles.\n*   **Southern boundary:** The \"- OHE -\" line runs along the southern property line. Building 8 is the closest structure to this line. The line does not appear to cross over any residential buildings, as it is confined to the outer edge of the property boundary, separated from Building 8 by a driveway and a \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n\n**6. What is shown in the northeast corner of the site (based on the general notes, there is drainage activity there)?**\nThe northeast corner of the site plan explicitly shows drainage infrastructure. It contains a large rectangular area featuring the following labels:\n*   **\"Biofiltration Detention Pond\"** (located in the center of the rectangular feature).\n*   **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** (pointing to the boundary of the pond).\n*   **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** (surrounding portions of the pond).\n*   This area is situated entirely within the boundaries of the labeled **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   Underground storm drainage lines (labeled **\"- SD -\"**) are shown routing into this pond area from the main site.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1482,"outputTokens":1259,"totalTokens":4971,"reasoningTokens":2230},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan and report:\n1. Is a transmission easement or transmission facility shown on the site plan? If so, where is it located and how is it depicted 