{"level":30,"time":1776951985936,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan for Valley View Road frontage. Identify: (1) Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road? (2) Are there any root barrier boundaries or planting zone delineations marked? (3) Are any utility lines (especially Austin Water, water mains, or water services) shown crossing through or adjacent to any designated planting zones? (4) Is there any indication of utility exclusion zones? Describe the location and nature of any utilities relative to the street frontage.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 28 of 35 (\"LANDSCAPE PLAN\"), focusing specifically on the left side of the drawing along the Valley View Road frontage, here are the findings corresponding to your questions:\n\n**(1) Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road?**\nWhile the exact boundary line demarcating the public right-of-way versus private property is not explicitly labeled with text in that specific area, there are trees shown planted immediately adjacent to the Valley View Road street edge.\n*   These trees are located within a shaded gray boundary that runs parallel to the street.\n*   There are callout tags pointing to this shaded area labeled **\"H.2\"**. According to the KEY NOTES legend, \"H.2\" designates a **\"STREET YARD\"**.\n*   Within this shaded H.2 area along the frontage, there are four large tree symbols shown. Adjacent to several of these specific tree symbols is the text **\"SY\"** and **\"M\"**. According to the unnumbered legend text below the Key Notes:\n    *   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n    *   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**(2) Are there any root barrier boundaries or planting zone delineations marked?**\n*   **Root Barriers:** There are no lines, symbols, or text labels indicating \"root barriers\" anywhere along the Valley View Road frontage or in the legend on this sheet.\n*   **Planting Zone Delineations:** Yes, planting zones are clearly delineated using shading and hatching. The primary planting zone along the Valley View Road frontage is delineated by a solid gray shaded area. This shaded area is identified by leader lines pointing to it with the tag **\"H.2\"**, which the legend defines as **\"STREET YARD\"**. Other adjacent planting zones are denoted with different hatch patterns, such as the area tagged **\"H.4\"** (\"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\").\n\n**(3) Are any utility lines (especially Austin Water, water mains, or water services) shown crossing through or adjacent to any designated planting zones?**\nYes, utility lines are shown intersecting the designated planting zones.\n*   In the lower-left portion of the site plan, intersecting the lower section of the shaded \"STREET YARD\" (H.2) frontage area, there are horizontal lines indicating utilities entering/crossing the site.\n*   One line passing horizontally through the lower part of the H.2 shaded area is labeled **\"--- SD ---\"** (typically indicating Storm Drain).\n*   Directly below that, another line passes horizontally through the lower extent of the H.2 shaded area and is labeled **\"--- W ---\"** (typically indicating a Water line).\n*   A line labeled **\"--- OHE ---\"** (Overhead Electric) runs horizontally along the bottom edge of the site plan, near the property boundary, but appears to be just outside or on the edge of the delineated landscape zones.\n\n**(4) Is there any indication of utility exclusion zones? Describe the location and nature of any utilities relative to the street frontage.**\n*   **Exclusion Zones:** There are no explicit labels, hatched areas, or boundary lines denoting \"utility exclusion zones\" or minimum planting clearances around the utility lines on this landscape plan sheet.\n*   **Location/Nature relative to frontage:** The utilities described above (**\"--- SD ---\"** and **\"--- W ---\"**) run perpendicular to the Valley View Road frontage. They cross horizontally from the street/ROW area on the left, directly through the lower portion of the shaded \"STREET YARD\" (H.2) planting zone, and into the site. Tree symbols are shown planted in the H.2 zone in relatively close proximity to where these lines cross, but no visual exclusion radius is drawn around the utility lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1418,"outputTokens":825,"totalTokens":4400,"reasoningTokens":2157},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan for Valley View Road frontage. Identify: (1) Are there any street trees shown in the public right-of-way along Valley View Road? (2) Are there any root barrier boundaries or planting zone delineations marked? (3) Are any utility lines (especially Austin Water, water mains, or water services) shown crossing through or adjacent to any designated planting zones? (4) Is there any indication of utility exclusion zones? Describe the location and nature of any utilities relative to the street frontage."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-sEHJ8zQtdva1jruHAEyKjKFj","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:46:25 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::nfc9t-1776951934992-ef0e36326578"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 28 of 35 (\"LANDSCAPE PLAN\"), focusing specifically on the left side of the drawing along the Valley Vie