e parallel pipes connect to horizontal connector lines labeled: `\"0.42 ft 6\" PVC @ 1.00%\"`.\n    *   They lead to a central outlet labeled: `\"6\" PVC Riser Outlet Pipe See Detail 1.6.7.C-3 FL In 6\": 669.31\"`.\n    *   There are cleanouts for this system labeled `\"Cleanout (Typ) FL 6\": 669.75\"` and `\"Cleanout FL 6\": 669.36\"`.\n*   **Storm Drain (SD) Lines:**\n    *   A solid line denoted with `\"SD\"` enters the `\"Sedimentation\"` basin from the west (left).\n    *   A solid line denoted with `\"SD\"` runs parallel to the biofiltration media bed on the north (top) side, turning south to connect into the pond area.\n*   **Routing Relative to Features:** The 6\" perforated underdrain pipes run lengthwise inside the biofiltration area, bounded entirely within the `\"Concrete Structural Retaining Wall w/ Fall Protection Railing (By Others)\"`.\n\n### 2. POND BOUNDARIES AND LOCATION\n*   **Associated Unit/Building:** The pond is located immediately adjacent to and north/northwest of an area designated in large text as `\"Unit 501\"`.\n*   **Dimensions:** While overall external dimensions are not specified with a single leader line, internal dimensions are provided:\n    *   The `\"Sedimentation\"` basin has internal dimension lines marking `\"18'\"` (width) and `\"47'\"` (length).\n    *   The Biofiltration area has an internal width dimension line of `\"36.25'\"`.\n*   **Orientation and Setting:**\n    *   The pond structure is oriented horizontally across the plan sheet.\n    *   To the south (bottom of drawing) is `\"Unit 501\"`.\n    *   To the east (right of drawing) is a `\"Fire\"` lane and an area labeled `\"Sto Pav\"` (likely Stone Paving, text partially cut off).\n    *   To the west (left of drawing) is an `\"8' Wide Concrete Maintenance Path\"`.\n\n### 3. UTILITY CONNECTIONS TO THE POND\n*   **Inflow Pipes:**\n    *   Stormwater enters the `\"Sedimentation\"` basin from the west via a `\"24\" Pipe Through Pond Wall FL In 24\": 672.34\"`.\n    *   T