{"level":30,"time":1776952003269,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKbnZcUxCk9TE6EtL4eyrY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 12 — Storm Sewer Plan\n     2→\n     3→Displays the proposed storm sewer layout and drainage infrastructure details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the proposed Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12 of 39) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's surface and subsurface drainage infrastructure, including the layout of storm sewer pipes, grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes overlaid on the site grading and building footprints. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   **Benchmarks**: BM #1 Elevation = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 Elevation = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    12→*   **ADA Specifications**: ADA Ramp maximum slope = 8.33%; Level Landing maximum slope = 2.00%\n    13→*   **Storm Sewer Pipes**: Drawing indicates extensive use of 12\", 18\", and 24\" HDPE pipe. Examples include:\n    14→    *   24\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 1.35% (e.g., lengths of 53.28 lf, 47.98 lf, 26.71 lf, 20.98 lf)\n    15→    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 0.50% (e.g., lengths of 71.10 lf, 63.17 lf, 61.27 lf)\n    16→    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 4.00% (e.g., lengths of 49.02 lf, 25.60 lf, 19.84 lf)\n    17→*   **Key Structures**:\n    18→    *   4'x4' Junction Box: Rim = 684.80, FL 24\" = 673.90\n    19→    *   SD Manhole (near Bldg 2): Rim = 684.71, FL 24\" = 675.47, FL 18\" = 675.57\n    20→    *   Multiple 18\" and 2'x2' Grate Inlets throughout the site (e.g., 2'x2' Grate Inlet Rim = 684.34, FL 24\" = 675.19)\n    21→*   **Building Sizes**: Examples include Bldg 2 (4,830 sf, FFE=685.50), Bldg 7 (4,144 sf, FFE=685.0), Bldg 8 (4,997 sf, FFE=685.50)\n    22→\n    23→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    24→\n    25→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan Drawing**\n    26→    Contains the detailed layout of the storm sewer system, including pipe alignments, structure locations, existing/proposed contours, building footprints (Buildings 1-8), and property boundaries.\n    27→    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\n    28→\n    29→*   **Block 10: seal — Title Block**\n    30→    Provides primary project identification (Valley View Townhomes, Austin, TX) and the engineering firm's information (Bleyl Engineering).\n    31→    *READ for project context and location.*\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    34→    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\n    35→    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\n    36→\n    37→*   **Block 4: notes — Legend**\n    38→    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\n    39→    *READ for ADA constraints and symbol definitions, VISION to map these symbols onto the main drawing.*\n    40→\n    41→*   **Block 5: notes — Drainage & Curb Notes**\n    42→    Provides construction directions for curbs (catch vs. spill curbs) and administrative requirements for detention/filtration facility certification prior to obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy.\n    43→    *READ for compliance and curb grading requirements.*\n    44→\n    45→*   **Blocks 6, 7: notes — References & Legal Description**\n    46→    Provides the legal plat description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) and points to Sheet 32 for the site's tree list.\n    47→    *READ to cross-reference property bounds or tree data.*\n    48→\n    49→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14: various — Boilerplate, Scale & Administrative**\n    50→    Contains the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), Texas 811 utility contact information, standard utility verification disclaimers, city review disclaimers, the drawing scale (1\" = 20'), project tracking numbers, and the sheet index (Sheet 12 of 39).\n    51→    *READ Block 12 to confirm the drawing scale; skip the rest unless auditing standard design metadata or disclaimers.*\n    52→\n    53→---\n    54→\n    55→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    56→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"a40bce80-99d0-4517-8ad8-7297fb5aeb65","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 12 — Storm Sewer Plan\n\nDisplays the proposed storm sewer layout and drainage infrastructure details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the proposed Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12 of 39) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's surface and subsurface drainage infrastructure, including the layout of storm sewer pipes, grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes overlaid on the site grading and building footprints. \n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmarks**: BM #1 Elevation = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 Elevation = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n*   **ADA Specifications**: ADA Ramp maximum slope = 8.33%; Level Landing maximum slope = 2.00%\n*   **Storm Sewer Pipes**: Drawing indicates extensive use of 12\", 18\", and 24\" HDPE pipe. Examples include:\n    *   24\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 1.35% (e.g., lengths of 53.28 lf, 47.98 lf, 26.71 lf, 20.98 lf)\n    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 0.50% (e.g., lengths of 71.10 lf, 63.17 lf, 61.27 lf)\n    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 4.00% (e.g., lengths of 49.02 lf, 25.60 lf, 19.84 lf)\n*   **Key Structures**:\n    *   4'x4' Junction Box: Rim = 684.80, FL 24\" = 673.90\n    *   SD Manhole (near Bldg 2): Rim = 684.71, FL 24\" = 675.47, FL 18\" = 675.57\n    *   Multiple 18\" and 2'x2' Grate Inlets throughout the site (e.g., 2'x2' Grate Inlet Rim = 684.34, FL 24\" = 675.19)\n*   **Building Sizes**: Examples include Bldg 2 (4,830 sf, FFE=685.50), Bldg 7 (4,144 sf, FFE=685.0), Bldg 8 (4,997 sf, FFE=685.50)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan Drawing**\n    Contains the detailed layout of the storm sewer system, including pipe alignments, structure locations, existing/proposed contours, building footprints (Buildings 1-8), and property boundaries.\n    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\n\n*   **Block 10: seal — Title Block**\n    Provides primary project identification (Valley View Townhomes, Austin, TX) and the engineering firm's information (Bleyl Engineering).\n    *READ for project context and location.*\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\n    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Legend**\n    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\n    *READ for ADA constraints and symbol definitions, VISION to map these symbols onto the main drawing.*\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Drainage & Curb Notes**\n    Provides construction directions for curbs (catch vs. spill curbs) and administrative requirements for detention/filtration facility certification prior to obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy.\n    *READ for compliance and curb grading requirements.*\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7: notes — References & Legal Description**\n    Provides the legal plat description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) and points to Sheet 32 for the site's tree list.\n    *READ to cross-reference property bounds or tree data.*\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14: various — Boilerplate, Scale & Administrative**\n    Contains the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), Texas 811 utility contact information, standard utility verification disclaimers, city review disclaimers, the drawing scale (1\" = 20'), project tracking numbers, and the sheet index (Sheet 12 of 39).\n    *READ Block 12 to confirm the drawing scale; skip the rest unless auditing standard design metadata or disclaimers.*\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776952005580,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017BvCu1VTMs73rAr5snvytY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The landscape blocks show:\n- H.2: STREET YARD\n- H.3: STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n- SY = Street Yard Tree (>1.5 cal inch)\n- Various planting areas\n\nLet me use vision to examine the landscape plan (Sheet 31) to see if there are street trees with planting zones in the ROW along Valley View Road, which would trigger the UCM § 2.9.1.C planting zone prohibition for Austin Water utilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":67498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1809},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"87367942-9ed2-46b5-9fe5-6fe6e3c2122a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952007642,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) and identify:\n1. Is there a proposed Austin Energy electrical service to the buildings? \n2. Are electrical transformers shown on the plan for new service?\n3. Is this new service or modification to existing service?\n4. What is the approximate electrical load or service capacity indicated?\n5. Are there any notes about the electrical service design or requirements?\nProvide the key details visible on this sheet regarding the proposed electrical infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here are the details regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Is there a proposed Austin Energy electrical service to the buildings?**\nYes, there is proposed underground electrical service routed to all eight buildings on the site. While the words \"Austin Energy\" do not explicitly appear on this sheet, the title block indicates the project is in \"Austin, Texas 78704.\" The service is depicted by solid blue lines traversing the site, with one specific segment explicitly labeled as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** near the western boundary.\n\n**2. Are electrical transformers shown on the plan for new service?**\nYes. There are four distinct rectangular areas outlined with dashed blue lines, each explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. They are located:\n*   West of Bldg. 1\n*   West of Bldg. 2 (near the Sidewalk Easement)\n*   Between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5\n*   Between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7\n\n**3. Is this new service or modification to existing service?**\nBased on the visual evidence, this represents new service infrastructure for a newly proposed development. The drawing is titled \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for \"Valley View Townhomes.\" The blue lines route newly proposed electrical infrastructure to newly proposed building footprints (labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8).\n\n**4. What is the approximate electrical load or service capacity indicated?**\nThere is **no** indication of electrical load, voltage, amperage, or transformer capacity (e.g., kVA) anywhere on this specific sheet.\n\n**5. Are there any notes about the electrical service design or requirements?**\nThere are no specific electrical design notes or specifications on this sheet. However, there are general notes that apply to all utilities, including electrical trenching:\n*   Under **\"Utility Notes\"**:\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n    *(Note: Notes 3 and 4 in this block specifically pertain only to Domestic Water and Wastewater).*\n*   Under the **\"Note\"** block (bottom left):\n    *   \"This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM); provided that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\"\n\n**Other Key Details Visible:**\n*   **Meters:** Every building block (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) has a designated location along the building perimeter explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"**.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** The underground routing network includes numerous points explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** located at turning points and junctions along the blue lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1413,"outputTokens":647,"totalTokens":4246,"reasoningTokens":2186},"warnings":[],"request":{"b