 Between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5\n*   Between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7\n\n**3. Is this new service or modification to existing service?**\nBased on the visual evidence, this represents new service infrastructure for a newly proposed development. The drawing is titled \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for \"Valley View Townhomes.\" The blue lines route newly proposed electrical infrastructure to newly proposed building footprints (labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8).\n\n**4. What is the approximate electrical load or service capacity indicated?**\nThere is **no** indication of electrical load, voltage, amperage, or transformer capacity (e.g., kVA) anywhere on this specific sheet.\n\n**5. Are there any notes about the electrical service design or requirements?**\nThere are no specific electrical design notes or specifications on this sheet. However, there are general notes that apply to all utilities, including electrical trenching:\n*   Under **\"Utility Notes\"**:\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n    *(Note: Notes 3 and 4 in this block specifically pertain only to Domestic Water and Wastewater).*\n*   Under the **\"Note\"** block (bottom left):\n    *   \"This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM); provided that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\"\n\n**Other Key Details Visible:**\n*   **Meters:** Every building block (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) has a designated location along the building perimeter explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"**.\n*   **Pull Boxes:** The underground routing network includes numerous points explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** located at turning points and junctions along the blue lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1413,"outputTokens":647,"totalTokens":4246,"reasoningTokens":2186},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":3045072.944176,"endTime":3071952.257334,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"rSLqaZHIA6enqOYPk9T1-Ao"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.036822","marketCost":"0.036822","inferenceCost":"0.036822","inputInferenceCost":"0.002826","outputInferenceCost":"0.033996","generationId":"gen_01KPX9EWPSR2F077VXR37M25ZR"}}},"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here are the details regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Is there a proposed Austin Energy electrical service to the buildings?**\nYes, there is proposed underground electrical service routed to all eight buildings on the site. While the words \"Austin Energy\" do not explicitly appear on this sheet, the title block indicates the project is in \"Austin, Texas 78704.\" The service is