 this sheet, no utilities, easements, or transmission easement boundaries are drawn or labeled. \n\n*(Note: There is a \"Legend\" in the top right corner that defines symbols for various utility and easement features—such as \"Existing Easement,\" \"Existing Power Pole & Down Guy,\" and \"Overhead Electric Line\"—but these symbols are merely definitions and are not applied to any drawing on this specific page.)*\n\n**3. Where are the \"Electric Transmission Notes\" located on the page and what do they apply to - are they keyed to specific features shown on a diagram, or are they general project-wide notes?**\nThe \"Electric Transmission Notes\" are located in the top middle-right section of the page, positioned to the left of the \"Legend\" and above the two \"Austin Water\" letters. \n\nBecause there is no diagram on this sheet, these are **general project-wide notes**. They are not keyed to specific graphical features on this page. They consist of a numbered list (items 1 through 17) detailing overarching safety, clearance, and operational requirements (e.g., *\"1. No construction is permitted within the transmission easement...\"* and *\"2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\"*).\n\n**4. Is there any visual indication of where transmission facilities are located on the property, or are these notes referring to transmission facilities that may be off-site or in proximity to the site?**\nThere is **no visual indication** on this sheet showing where transmission facilities are physically located on or near the property. The notes provide mandatory guidelines and restrictions regarding electric facilities and easements, implying that transmission facilities are present within the project's scope or proximity, but the actual geographical location of these facilities would have to be found on a different sheet within the plan set that contains the physical site drawing.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtS