{"level":30,"time":1776952019069,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_016SY1AUvyrBUpuwkMuEpYbW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. So there IS new Austin Energy service being proposed (transformers, meters, pull boxes, underground lines). This means EL-3.1 applicability is confirmed - new electrical service IS required.\n\nNow let me finalize my findings. Let me also double-check if there's anything about moonlight towers since that's a downtown-specific requirement. The project is at 3759 Valley View Road, which is in South Austin (south of Lady Bird Lake), so it's not in the downtown area where moonlight towers are concentrated. However, I should still flag this appropriately.\n\nLet me now prepare my final list of deficiencies. Let me be conservative and focus on items I can definitively mark as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE based on the evidence I've gathered:\n\n**DEFINITE FAILS (not found on plans):**\n1. EL-3.4 - No note that site is within Austin Energy service area (VISION confirmed MISSING)\n2. EL-3.5 - No note about developer responsibility for conduit/infrastructure to AE standards (VISION confirmed MISSING)\n3. EL-3.29 - No Additional Review Acknowledgement table on cover sheet (VISION confirmed MISSING)\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (not found in submitted documents):**\n1. EL-3.1 - ESPA not documented in plan set (new service IS proposed, but ESPA normally submitted after site plan approval - cannot verify status)\n2. EL-3.2 - AEU clearance not found in supplementary documents (required but not located in submittal)\n3. EL-3.30 - Street names not shown as reserved with 911 Addressing (project shows unit addresses on Sheet 29 but no evidence of reservation)\n4. EL-3.31 - Addressing plan not shown as approved (Sheet 29 shows addressing plan but no evidence of Address Management Services approval separate from AVL)\n\n\n5. EL-3.6 - Four Standard Austin Energy Notes appear present and match verbatim requirements. EL-3.3 regarding Electric Service Availability Letter doesn't apply since facts.md shows no ambiguity about which utility serves the location. EL-3.23 on AULCC requirements doesn't trigger—only approximately 72 LF of water main work shown versus the 300+ LF threshold, project isn't in DAPCZ, and no pole relocations evident. Moonlight tower requirements (EL-3.13, 3.14, 3.15) don't apply to this South Austin location outside the downtown district.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":76289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"d69b5993-a1f2-4bef-ba9c-c9183ecdbd08"}
