{"level":30,"time":1776952031233,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KBnVaXytCxgbbMYEPMNcVz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I've submitted my findings. Let me now provide a summary to the user of what I found and what the status is.\n\nLet me briefly summarize:\n- 32 checklist items total in this grouping\n- 7 items flagged as fail or not-verifiable (5 fail, 2 not-verifiable)\n- 25 items passed or were not applicable\n\nThe main issues are:\n1. Two missing required Austin Energy plan notes (EL-3.4 and EL-3.5)\n2. Missing Additional Review Acknowledgement table on cover sheet (EL-3.29)\n3. Unverifiable: AEU clearance, ESPA, addressing approvals","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":77795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2044},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"be4df1ab-84ca-4dff-ae4c-244ee70de783"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952034207,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CrKJus6BDL7Vj5pM7rWJFj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The storm sewer plan has storm drain pipes, grate inlets, and manholes. I need to check if any of these are near Austin Energy poles. However, from the vision analysis of Sheet 5, the electrical easements are on the eastern and southern boundaries, while the main site development is in the central and western portions. I should check if any of the storm drain components are near those easement boundaries.\n\nBut more importantly, I need to assess all applicable checklist items. Let me now create a comprehensive assessment. Based on my research:\n\n**ITEMS THAT DO NOT APPLY:**\n1. **EL-1.1** - Overhead utility zone (10-ft CTC/Urban Roadway requirement) - Valley View Road is a Local Street, NOT a CTC or Urban Roadway, so EL-1.1 does NOT apply.\n\n2. **EL-1.2, EL-1.3, EL-1.4, EL-1.5** - Horizontal/radial clearances from AE overhead conductors, vault clearances - No overhead distribution conductors visible on the plans. Only mention of \"proposed overhead electric facilities\" for service drops, but no dimensions or clearances provided in documents.\n\n3. **EL-1.6** - Customer service entrance facilities clearance from AE poles - No specific service entrance facilities (service equipment, FDCs, meter vaults) shown with clearances to poles.\n\n4. **EL-1.7** - Service drop clearances over truck traffic - No overhead service drops shown with vertical clearance dimensions for truck traffic areas.\n\n5. **EL-1.8** - Texas Gas Service crossings - No mention of TGS lines in the plans.\n\n6. **EL-1.9, EL-1.10** - AE underground crossings/joint trenches - No specific crossing details shown with clearance dimensions, and no joint-trench agreements referenced.\n\n7. **EL-1.11** - Utilities within 24 inches of ROW facilities - The site does connect to existing water/wastewater public utilities at the boundary, but no specific close-proximity utilities within ROW are identified in the documents.\n   \nWater and wastewater crossings lack detailed specifications for crossing methods and encasement requirements at the public mains. The wastewater service line is 6\" PVC rather than the 8\"-12\" diameter that would trigger large-diameter cleanout requirements. Storm drain components need verification for proximity to AE infrastructure.\n\nThe 5' electric easements along property boundaries require confirmation that no utilities are running parallel within them. Utility poles don't appear to be proposed in water easements. Since the SCM is privately maintained for the multi-family development rather than single-family or community association-maintained, staging area and maintenance drive clearance standards don't apply. No overhead utilities are identified above work zones that would create vertical clearance concerns.\n\nFor overhead electrical clearance zones, there are no visible overhead distribution conductors to delineate, and determining the transmission clearance envelope would need AE engineering input. The demolition plan on Sheet 8 falls short of transmission line safety requirements—it's missing the mandatory pre-construction safety meeting (48+ hours before work), 10-foot barricades from transmission structures, warning signs under overhead facilities, and prohibition on materials or spoils in the transmission easement. The transmission right-of-way access corridor also needs further review. notes on multiple sheets require the contractor to field verify utility crossing locations before construction begins, with Sheet 20 Block 6 explicitly documenting this requirement. The staging areas shown on Sheet 5 occupy the western portion of the site while electrical easements are positioned along the eastern and southern boundaries, but the transmission easement isn't clearly marked on the plans, making it impossible to confirm whether staging zones overlap with transmission infrastructure. My assessment shows EL-1.18 as a failure due to missing transmission line safety requirements in the demolition plan, EL-1.19 as not-verifiable because the transmission ROW access corridor dimensions cannot be confirmed from the available plans, EL-1.20 as a failure for lacking a specific caution note about at-grade utility appurtenances despite other utility-related notes being present, EL-1.21 as passing since field verification requirements are documented, and EL-1.25 as not-verifiable due to the transmission easement not being clearly delineated.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":78470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1759},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"500b8364-2f4d-4045-972d-1a44b26c5016"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952037300,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KBnVaXytCxgbbMYEPMNcVz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the review of grouping **EL-3 (Austin Energy Service and ROW Utility Coordination)** for the Valley View Townhomes project. \n\n### Research Findings\n\n**Project Context:**\n- 39-unit townhome development with 8 buildings\n- Located at 3759 Valley View Road in South Austin (outside downtown)\n- Project includes new Austin Energy electrical infrastructure (transformers, meters, pull boxes, underground service lines)\n- Water/wastewater connections to existing mains\n\n**Documents Examined:**\n- Site plan sheets 1, 3, 21, 29 (Cover, General Notes, Electrical Design, Addressing)\n- Utility tap plans (Sheets 19-20) and storm sewer plan (Sheet 12)\n- Multiple supplementary documents including Master Comment Report, completeness check results\n\n### Deficiencies Identified\n\nI found **7 deficiencies** across the 32 checklist items:\n\n**3 FAIL items** (missing required content on plan sheets):\n1. **EL-3.4** – No plan note stating site is within Austin Energy service area\n2. **EL-3.5** – No developer responsibility note for electric conduit/infrastructure design per AE standards  \n3. **EL-3.29** – Additional Review Acknowledgement table missing from cover sheet\n\n**4 NOT-VERIFIABLE items** (required documents not found in submittal):\n1. **EL-3.1** – ESPA approval not documented (though normally submitted after site plan approval)\n2. **EL-3.2** – Austin Energy Utility clearance not located in documents\n3. **EL-3.30** – Street name reservations with 911 Addressing not verified\n4. **EL-3.31** – Approved addressing plan not documented separately from any AVL\n\n**Items Passing or Not Applicable:**\n- Four Standard Austin Energy Notes ARE present and verbatim (EL-3.6)\n- AULCC clearance appears not required (~72 LF of water main work, not 300+ LF threshold; project not in DAPCZ; no pole relocations)\n- Moonlight tower provisions not applicable (project outside downtown/central Austin)\n\nThe findings have been returned in the structured format specified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2044,"cache_read_input_tokens":77795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2044},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9a1b17-16ac-4098-9a13-aa52e9d6aac3","uuid":"4f022e83-7992-4ff0-b6ce-85e4e9fa914e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952037346,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"3.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":308513,"duration_api_ms":180779,"num_turns":39,"result":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the review of grouping **EL-3 (Austin Energy Service and ROW Utility Coordination)** for the Valley View Townhomes project. \n\n### Research Findings\n\n**Project Context:**\n- 39-unit townhome development with 8 buildings\n- Located at 3759 Valley View Road in South Austin (outside downtown)\n- Project includes new Austin Energy electrical infrastructure (transformers, meters, pull boxes, underground service lines)\n- Water/wastewater connections to existing mains\n\n**Documents Examined:**\n- Site plan sheets 1, 3, 21, 29 (Cover, General Notes, Electrical Design, Addressing)\n- Utility tap plans (Sheets 19-20) and storm sewer plan (Sheet 12)\n- Multiple supplementary documents including Master Comment Report, completeness check results\n\n### Deficiencies Identified\n\nI found **7 deficiencies** across the 32 checklist items:\n\n**3 FAIL items** (missing required content on plan sheets):\n1. **EL-3.4** – No plan note stating site is within Austin Energy service area\n2. **EL-3.5** – No developer responsibility note for electric conduit/infrastructure design per AE standards  \n3. **EL-3.29** – Additional Review Acknowledgement table missing from cover sheet\n\n**4 NOT-VERIFIABLE items** (required documents not found in submittal):\n1. **EL-3.1** – ESPA approval not documented (though normally submitted after site plan approval)\n2. **EL-3.2** – Austin Energy Utility clearance not located in documents\n3. **EL-3.30** – Street name reservations with 911 Addressing not verified\n4. **EL-3.31** – Approved addressing plan not documented separately from any AVL\n\n**Items Passing or Not Applicable:**\n- Four Standard Austin Energy Notes ARE present and verbatim (EL-3.6)\n