{"level":30,"time":1776952038738,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CrKJus6BDL7Vj5pM7rWJFj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough review of the site plan documents and the grouping requirements, I've analyzed all 28 checklist items. Let me document my findings.\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Applicability Determination:**\n\nThe site has:\n- **Transmission easement and structures** (confirmed from Sheet 3 general notes with extensive transmission-related safety requirements)\n- **Demolition activities planned** (Sheet 8 - Tree Removal & Demolition Plan)\n- **Proposed utilities** (water, wastewater, underground electric; Sheet 19-21)\n- **Stormwater SCM** (private, multi-family - does NOT trigger EL-1.22/1.23 staging area clearance requirements)\n- **Valley View Road classification**: Local Street (NOT a Core Transit Corridor or Urban Roadway - therefore EL-1.1 does NOT apply)\n\n**Critical Findings - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n\n1. **Transmission easement boundaries NOT clearly delineated** on any site plan sheets (Sheet 2 plat, Sheet 5 ESC, Sheet 9-12)\n2. **Transmission clearance envelope NOT shown** with specific horizontal/vertical dimensions (required by EL-1.26)\n3. **Demolition sequence notes lacking transmission line safety requirements** (Sheet 8)\n4. **No contractor caution notes** for at-grade utility appurtenances in demolition plan (Sheet 8)\n5. **Transmission ROW access corridor dimensions NOT demonstrated** on construction/staging plans\n\n---\n\nNow let me generate the structured findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":78470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1759},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24aa3565-6e12-4421-aab9-b461d3b546f4","uuid":"43c28814-cd75-4e64-bd5d-3d1dcb37a1ca"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952043770,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 3 and look for:\n\n1. General construction notes or contractor requirements regarding utility field verification or separation verification during construction\n2. Any notes about contractor caution or safety near at-grade utility appurtenances\n3. Any requirement for field verification of clearances or separations\n4. Notes about the transmission easement and its delineation on plans\n\nProvide the exact text of any such notes found on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 3 (\"General Notes\"), here are the findings for your specific requirements. The text has been transcribed exactly as it appears on the document.\n\n### 1 & 3. Utility Field Verification, Clearances, and Separation Verification\nThe most explicit requirement for the contractor to field verify utilities and their crossings is located in the bottom right corner of the sheet (in the box next to the \"Texas 811 / Call Before You Dig!!\" logo). Additional requirements are found in the General Construction Notes and Electric Transmission Notes.\n\n**Bottom Right Corner Note:**\n> \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"\n\n**General Construction Notes:**\n> **2.** \"Contractor shall call Texas 811 (811 or 1-800-344-8377) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\"\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes:**\n> **3.** \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505 7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n### 2. Contractor Caution or Safety Near At-Grade Utility Appurtenances\nWhile the exact phrase *\"at-grade utility appurtenances\"* is not explicitly used, the document contains several strict safety, clearance, and caution mandates regarding utility equipment, structures, and lines.\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes:**\n> **2.** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n> **4.** \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n> **7.** \"Heavy equipment, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n> **15.** \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors\"\n\n**Electric Notes:**\n> **4.** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas State laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n### 4. Transmission Easement and Its Delineation on Plans\nThe document addresses rules for the transmission easement extensively in the **Electric Transmission Notes** section. While it does not include a specific textual note detailing *how* it is graphically delineated (other than standard linetypes in the Legend for \"Existing Easement\" and \"PUE\"), it sets strict parameters for what can happen within its boundaries:\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes:**\n> **1.** \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n> **9.** \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n> **11.** \"Property owner is responsible for any damage to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be machine laid/slip.\"\n> **16.** \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n> - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as frames, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n> - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n> - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1395,"outputTokens":1073,"totalTokens":6960,"reasoningTokens":4492},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 3 and look for:\n\n1. General construction notes or contractor requirements regarding utility field verification or separation verification during construction\n2. Any notes about contractor caution or safety near at-grade utility appurtenances\n3. Any requirement for field verification of clearances or separations\n4. Notes about the t