{"level":30,"time":1776952048067,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017KycmuNH6eLzJZ7ZRq3tvv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good information. Block 7 from Sheet 9 notes: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\" This is interesting — it suggests that electric easements may not be fully shown or secured yet.\n\nNow let me compile my findings and prepare the structured output. Based on all my research, here are the items I've flagged as fail or not-verifiable:\n\n**DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:**\n\n1. **EL-2.15 (Easement encroachment into ROW)** - **NOT-VERIFIABLE**: The facts state that two critical easements (Greenbelt Access & Use, Instrument 2010070731; City of Austin Drainage, Instrument 2011021137) and several others are NOT DEPICTED on the submitted site plan, even though they are recorded and perpetual. The easement boundaries cannot be verified against the proposed ROW without these easements being shown on the plans.\n\n2. **EL-2.16 (Easement licensing)** - **NOT-VERIFIABLE**: The submitted plans do not show any dedicated AE easement for the transformer pads, and there is no notation of a License Agreement from AE Public Involvement per UCM § 1.10.10.3 or a City Manager license per § 14-11-41 for any items within recorded utility easements. Cannot verify without proper documentation.\n\n3. **EL-2.22 (Transformer pad clearances and easement)** - **FAIL**: \n   - The vision analysis of Sheet 21 clearly shows that Transformer Pad 3 (located west of Unit 801) is positioned less than 5 feet (nearly flush) against the exterior wall of Unit 801. This violates UCM § 1.10.4, which requires 10 feet minimum clearance from the padlocked (hot-stick) side of the pad to any adjacent building or structure.\n   - Transformer Pad 2 sits in the narrow space between Units 404 and 504, positioned less than 10 feet from both exterior walls, which also breaches the clearance standard. Additionally, Sheet 21 lacks any dedicated AE easement notation for the transformer pad locations, which is required for utility facility protection.\n\n4. **EL-2.2 (Hill Country Roadway Corridor)** - Need to verify applicability. Valley View Road is in south Austin (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704). The group defines Hill Country Roadway Corridors as being within 1,000 feet of Loop 360 (US 290W to US 183), RM 620, RM 2222, RM 2244, or Southwest Parkway. The address is in south Austin, and I'm not aware of the specific proximity to these roads. However, the facts don't mention Hill Country Roadway corridor status, and the cover sheet would likely note this if applicable. Without explicit confirmation, I cannot definitively mark this as fail or not-verifiable. Let me be conservative and not include this unless I can verify it applies.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The grouping file states that Hill Country Roadway status should be \"Check: Hill Country Roadway corridor maps or applicability notation on site cover sheet; measure or verify site distance from named roadway ROW.\" The facts do not mention Hill Country Roadway Corridor at all, and the cover sheet guide doesn't mention it as a requirement. Without explicit evidence that the site is within a Hill Country Roadway Corridor, I cannot flag this as a deficiency.\n\nNow reviewing other elements: EL-2.1 through EL-2.9 apply only to CTC, Urban Roadway, Plaza Saltillo TOD, or NBG frontages. Since Valley View Road is classified as a LOCAL STREET with no regulating plans, these requirements don't apply. The same logic eliminates EL-2.3, EL-2.4, EL-2.5 through EL-2.8, and EL-2.9's overhead utility zone requirement for CTC and Urban Roadway contexts. The vision confirms all electrical lines are underground.\n\nFor EL-2.10 regarding utilities under ponds, Sheet 15's analysis shows no external domestic water, sanitary sewer, or electrical lines crossing beneath the pond footprint. The pond has its own underdrain system with no external utilities routed underneath, so this should be marked PASS. However, I need to verify whether utilities shown on other sheets like the overall site plan or utility tap details might contradict this. The standard requires checking both grading/drainage and utility site plan overlays, and Sheet 15 specifically addresses the pond area itself.\n\nEL-2.11 and EL-2.12 address planting restrictions in right-of-way zones. Sheet 31 confirms no trees are explicitly positioned within the ROW, though a designated street yard exists on the property side. Since the restriction applies only to public right-of-way planting, and the trees shown are on private property within the street yard, these items are NOT APPLICABLE.\n\nEL-2.13 concerns transformers in parkland. The site notes indicate a parkland deficiency triggering fees rather than existing parkland on the property, making this requirement unlikely to apply.\n\nFor EL-2.14 regarding light rail corridors, there's no reference in the project documentation, so this is NOT APPLICABLE.\n\nEL-2.17 involves private utilities routed through the ROW. While Sheet 19 shows utilities entering from the west, there's no explicit evidence that private utilities are positioned within the public right-of-way itself. Given the project is developing the site rather than installing new utilities in existing ROW, this appears NOT APPLICABLE.\n\nEL-2.18 addresses abandoned utilities. Sheet 8 identifies existing utilities scheduled for removal, including a 6\" DI water line and fire hydrant, with the contractor required to verify locations and notify the engineer of any conflicts before proceeding. of work which may jeopardize the well-being of any trees to remain\" and mentions coordination, but no pole relocation shown. Likely NOT APPLICABLE unless poles are being relocated.\n\n**EL-2.23**: Tree well electrical outlets. Vision analysis of Sheet 31 states \"There are no isolated 'tree wells'...shown on this plan.\" NOT APPLICABLE.\n\n**EL-2.24**: Table B utility routing. Site is residential MF-2 zoning (<3 acres in residential), and parking is not between building and principal street. NOT APPLICABLE.\n\nThe key deficiencies emerging from this review are: EL-2.15 has multiple recorded easements that aren't depicted on the plans (NOT-VERIFIABLE); EL-2.16 lacks an AE easement for transformers and supporting documentation (NOT-VERIFIABLE); and EL-2.22 shows Transformer Pad 3 and possibly Pad 2 violating the required 10-foot clearance with no AE easement provided (FAIL). Now I need to compile these findings into the final structured output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5875,"cache_read_input_tokens":78333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5875},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"0230ed9a-9b8d-488b-b093-c314ef28d4d3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952048095,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017KycmuNH6eLzJZ7ZRq3tvv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents, I have identified the key issues. Let me now prepare my findings in the required structured format.\n\n## Research Summary\n\nI have reviewed all relevant site plan sheets and documents for this grouping:\n\n**Sheets Examined:**\n- Sheet 1 (Cover): No regulating plans, Valley View Road is a LOCAL STREET (not CTC/Urban Roadway)\n- Sheet 2 (Plat): Existing easements shown; facts note two critical easements NOT depicted\n- Sheet 8 (Demolition): Existing utilities (6\" DI water line, fire hydrant) being removed  \n- Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Note states \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date\"\n- Sheet 15 (Pond Plan): No external utilities shown crossing under the pond\n- Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan): Water/wastewater connections detailed\n- Sheet 20 (Public Utility Tap): AC to DI conversion, new fire demand meter\n- Sheet 21 (Electrical Design): **Four transformer pads shown with critical clearance issues**\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): No trees explicitly in public ROW; street yard trees on private property\n\n**Key Regulatory Applicability Analysis:**\n\nThis site (Valley View Road = LOCAL STREET, MF-2 zoning, no regulating plans) is NOT subject to:\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.9 (CTC/Urban Roadway/Plaza Saltillo/NBG requirements)\n- EL-2.11, EL-2.12 (ROW planting zone restrictions — no trees in ROW)\n- EL-2.13 (Parkland — no evidence of adjacent parkland)\n- EL-2.23, EL-2.24 (Tree wells, Table B routing — not applicable)\n\n**Critical Issues Found:**\n\n1. **Easement Depiction Deficiency (EL-2.15):** Facts.md explicitly documents that two perpetual recorded easements are NOT DEPICTED on submitted site plan: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres), plus four additional GIS-confirmed easements not verified on plans. Cannot assess whether these encroach into proposed ROW without their boundaries being shown.\n\n2. **Transformer Pad Clearance Violations (EL-2.22):** Vision analysis of Sheet 21 reveals:\n   - **Pad 3** (west of Unit 801): Located <5 feet (nearly flush) against building exterior — **VIOLATES 10-foot minimum clearance** per UCM § 1.10.4\n   - **Pad 2** (between Units 404/504): Positioned in tight corridor <10 feet from both buildings — **VIOLATES 10-foot minimum**\n   - No dedicated AE easement shown encumbering any transformer pad locations\n\n3. **Utility Easement Licensing (EL-2.16):** No AE easement shown on Sheet 21 for transformer pads; no License Agreement notation visible; no notation of City Manager license per § 14-11-41 for items within recorded utility easements.\n\n---"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5875,"cache_read_input_tokens":78333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5875},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15b83afc-0aa4-4376-b427-846989125e55","uuid":"85cfdf19-c01d-43a5-b095-8cd8dae64e48"}
