{"level":30,"time":1776952051813,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"I need to determine if there are Austin Water planting zone conflicts on this landscape plan. Please examine this drawing carefully and answer:\n\n1. Are there any street trees (SY - Street Yard Trees) shown along the Valley View Road frontage in the public right-of-way? If so, how many and where are they located?\n\n2. Are any planting zones, root barrier areas, or utility gap designations shown in the ROW along Valley View Road? If so, describe their locations and dimensions.\n\n3. Are there any Austin Water (W) utility lines shown on this landscape plan? If so, do they route through or near any planting zones in the ROW?\n\n4. Are there water service connections to the buildings shown? If so, where do they connect from and how do they route?\n\n5. Are there any landscape areas (H.2 street yard, H.3 street yard landscaping, or other planting designations) marked in the right-of-way area along Valley View Road?\n\nPlease provide specific measurements, tree locations (distances from curb or property line), and utility line routing relative to any planting zones.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35, Valley View Townhomes), here are the answers to your questions regarding potential Austin Water planting zone conflicts:\n\n**1. Are there any street trees (SY - Street Yard Trees) shown along the Valley View Road frontage in the public right-of-way? If so, how many and where are they located?**\n\n*   **No.** There are no trees planted within the public right-of-way (ROW) along Valley View Road on this plan.\n*   While there are trees located along the Valley View Road frontage (on the left side of the drawing), the center planting points (crosshairs) for all trees labeled with \"SY\" (specifically \"SY(M)\") are located *inside* the heavy dashed property line. Only the canopy circles extend over the property line into the ROW.\n\n**2. Are any planting zones, root barrier areas, or utility gap designations shown in the ROW along Valley View Road? If so, describe their locations and dimensions.**\n\n*   **No.** The area between the curb of Valley View Road and the property line (the ROW) does not contain any markings, hatching, or text indicating designated planting zones, root barrier lines, or utility gaps on this sheet.\n\n**3. Are there any Austin Water (W) utility lines shown on this landscape plan? If so, do they route through or near any planting zones in the ROW?**\n\n*   **No.** There are no Austin Water utility lines (typically denoted by a line with a \"W\") visible anywhere on this landscape plan sheet.\n*   The only utility-type lines explicitly labeled on this sheet are \"SD\" (Storm Drain) running horizontally through the site and \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric) running along the bottom property line. Because no water lines are shown, no routing conflicts in the ROW can be determined from this document.\n\n**4. Are there water service connections to the buildings shown? If so, where do they connect from and how do they route?**\n\n*   **No.** There are no water service connection lines, meters, or routing paths shown connecting to the buildings on this landscape plan. This information is typically reserved for Civil Utility plans.\n\n**5. Are there any landscape areas (H.2 street yard, H.3 street yard landscaping, or other planting designations) marked in the right-of-way area along Valley View Road?**\n\n*   **No.** While the Key Notes \"H.2\" (STREET YARD) and \"H.3\" (STREET YARD LANDSCAPING) are utilized on the plan near Valley View Road, they do not extend into the ROW.\n*   The leader lines for the \"H.2\" and \"H.3\" bubbles point to specific shaded/hatched areas. These designated shaded areas are contained entirely *inside* the heavy dashed property line, on the private property side, not in the right-of-way.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1541,"outputTokens":625,"totalTokens":3833,"reasoningTokens":1667},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"I need to determine if there are Austin Water planting zone conflicts on this landscape plan. Please examine this drawing carefully and answer:\n\n1. Are there any street trees (SY - Street Yard Trees) shown along the Valley View Road frontage in the public right-of-way? If so, how many and where are they located?\n\n2. Ar