{"level":30,"time":1776952059002,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01J1APBY4MNSdgARKR2R3jZ1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for the **Underground Utility Routing and Placement (EL-2)** grouping. \n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Not Applicable Items** (based on site characteristics):\n- EL-2.1 through EL-2.9: Valley View Road is a LOCAL STREET (not CTC/Urban Roadway); site has no regulating plans\n- EL-2.2: Hill Country Roadway status not indicated; insufficient evidence of applicability\n- EL-2.11, EL-2.12: No trees shown in public ROW (only on private property street yard areas)\n- EL-2.13, EL-2.14: No parkland or light rail corridor adjacency identified\n- EL-2.20, EL-2.23, EL-2.24: No underground storage tanks; no tree wells; residential zoning (not Table B subject)\n\n**Deficiencies Identified** (3 total):\n\n1. **EL-2.15 (Easement Encroachment)** — **NOT-VERIFIABLE**  \n   Two critical perpetual easements plus four additional GIS-confirmed easements are not depicted on the submitted site plan, preventing verification of compliance with easement boundary requirements.\n\n2. **EL-2.16 (Easement Licensing)** — **NOT-VERIFIABLE**  \n   No AE easement or license agreement documentation shown for transformer pad locations; cannot verify required licensing per UCM regulations.\n\n3. **EL-2.22 (Transformer Pad Clearances)** — **FAIL**  \n   Transformer Pad 3 is positioned less than 5 feet against Unit 801 (violates 10-foot minimum per UCM § 1.10.4); Transformer Pad 2 also appears to violate 10-foot clearance. No dedicated AE easement shown.\n\nAll findings have been output in the required structured format."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_