{"level":30,"time":1776952060303,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MXLamKZvcfdts2Uto9BFPs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have very detailed information. Key points:\n\n1. **Field Verification Required**: The plans STATE that \"Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction\" (bottom right of Sheet 3)\n2. **Contractor Caution Language**: While not explicitly about \"at-grade utility appurtenances,\" the transmission notes contain extensive caution and safety language, but I need to check if the DEMOLITION PLAN includes this language\n3. **Transmission Easement**: The plans reference the transmission easement extensively in the Electric Transmission Notes, but I need to verify if it's actually delineated on the plans (vision tool said it's NOT clearly shown on Sheets 5 and 9)\n\nNow let me compile my findings for each checklist item. I'll work through them systematically.\n\nLet me create my evaluation now based on all the evidence I've gathered:\n\n**EL-1.1**: Building or structure located within 10-ft radius of energized overhead conductors, or overhead utility zone not graphically delineated\n- Applicability: Only when overhead utilities remain on site AND the site fronts a Core Transit Corridor or Urban Roadway\n- Valley View Road = LOCAL STREET (not CTC or Urban Roadway)\n- Status: **N/A** - Not applicable due to street classification\n\n**EL-1.2**: Customer facilities not maintaining minimum 7-ft 6-in horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from AE overhead distribution conductors\n- Applicability: Only when overhead distribution utilities are present\n- Vision shows overhead lines (OHE) along south and east property boundaries, but Sheet 21 (electrical plan) shows underground service\n- The overhead 