{"level":30,"time":1776952070888,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DjMwmZzEWNRvTdCs4E7hfm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Sheet 20 shows public utility connections with water tap to existing 6\" water line. Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings so far before evaluating each checklist item.\n\n## RESEARCH FINDINGS SUMMARY:\n\n### Site Context:\n- **Zoning:** MF-2 (Multi-Family, Medium Density)\n- **Street Classification:** Valley View Road = Local Street (ASMP Level 1) — NOT a CTC, Urban Roadway, Hill Country Roadway, or regulating plan district\n- **No Regulating Plans Apply** (not Plaza Saltillo TOD, NBG)\n- **Utilities:** Biofiltration/detention pond, water service (public tap), wastewater, storm drain, electrical\n- **No Hill Country Roadway Corridor applicability**\n\n### CRITICAL DEFICIENCY IDENTIFIED:\n\n**EL-2.10 - Utilities routed under detention pond:**\n- Sheet 15 (Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan) clearly shows:\n  - **Electrical (E) line** crosses completely through the pond, through sedimentation basin and biofiltration media\n  - **Wastewater (WW) line** crosses underneath southern boundary into biofiltration media\n- This violates the Reviewer Convention requirement that utilities should NOT be routed under detention/retention ponds\n- Status: **FAIL**\n\n### Other Findings:\n\n**Easements Not Depicted (General Compliance Issue):**\n- facts.md identified multiple recorded easements NOT shown on the site plan:\n  - Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 ac, Instrument 2010070731) - perpetual no-build zone - **NOT DEPICTED**\n  - City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 ac, Instrument 2011021137) - **NOT DEPICTED**\n  - Various plat-dedicated easements not verified on site plan\n\n\n- This relates to EL-2.15 (easement boundaries encroaching into ROW) and general compliance\n\n**Street Trees & Planting Zones:**\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows no street trees within the ROW—all plantings are on private property. No planting zones or utility gaps exist in the right-of-way, and Austin Water lines don't create conflicts with landscape design. EL-2.11 and EL-2.12 don't apply here.\n\n**Transformer Pads:**\n- Sheet 21 shows 3 transformer pads all within private property. Need to verify UCM § 1.10.4 clearance requirements (EL-2.22). Underground electric lines run through drive aisles and around parking areas, but EL-2.24 doesn't apply—the site has only 39 residential units on 2.16 acres in MF-2 zoning, which doesn't meet Table B's thresholds for nonresidential zoning or surface parking requirements.\n\n**Building-to-Property-Line Undergrounding:**\n- Valley View Road is a local street, not a CTC or Urban Roadway, so EL-2.1 doesn't apply.\n- Water, wastewater, and electrical routing underground from buildings to the property line isn't mandated by the EL-2.1 framework for this street classification.\n\n**Utilities in ROW:**\n- Need to check for conflicts with ROW improvements. Sheet 20 indicates a public water tap being made, likely in the ROW.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":70476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"eb7bf420-277f-419d-b56a-8306c0cf41d5"}
