{"level":30,"time":1776952074234,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DjMwmZzEWNRvTdCs4E7hfm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UY7eiT9bdM1Lu2M8AAwyVE","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"I need to verify transformer pad placement and clearances against UCM § 1.10.4 requirements. Please examine this electrical plan and provide specific information about each transformer pad:\n\nFor EACH transformer pad visible on this plan, please provide:\n1. **Pad Location** - Which building is it nearest to, and what is its distance from any building wall or structure? (Need to verify 10-foot clearance from buildings on hot-stick side)\n2. **Pad to Parking/Traffic Area** - What is the distance from the pad to the nearest parking space or traffic area? (Need to verify within 6 feet for AE truck access per UCM § 1.10.4)\n3. **Easement Encumbrance** - Is there a dedicated AE easement boundary shown around each pad? If so, what are the dimensions?\n4. **Fence/Clearance Areas** - Are there any fences or barriers shown near the pads? What clearances are noted?\n5. **Are pads on customer's property** - Confirm each pad is NOT in public ROW or dedicated parkland\n\nPlease measure or estimate distances where visible on the plan and identify the specific pad locations by building reference."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":70476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"aa8e1055-840c-428f-9500-d0c7dc91f34f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952074236,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"I need to verify transformer pad placement and clearances against UCM § 1.10.4 requirements. Please examine this electrical plan and provide specific information about each transformer pad:\n\nFor EACH transformer pad visible on this plan, please provide:\n1. **Pad Location** - Which building is it nearest to, and what is its distance from any building wall or structure? (Need to verify 10-foot clearance from buildings on hot-stick side)\n2. **Pad to Parking/Traffic Area** - What is the distance from the pad to the nearest parking space or traffic area? (Need to verify within 6 feet for AE truck access per UCM § 1.10.4)\n3. **Easement Encumbrance** - Is there a dedicated AE easement boundary shown around each pad? If so, what are the dimensions?\n4. **Fence/Clearance Areas** - Are there any fences or barriers shown near the pads? What clearances are noted?\n5. **Are pads on customer's property** - Confirm each pad is NOT in public ROW or dedicated parkland\n\nPlease measure or estimate distances where visible on the plan and identify the specific pad locations by building reference.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952096058,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"Examine the plat sheet and specifically look for:\n1. All recorded easements shown on the plat - list each one with its width and location\n2. Is there a transmission easement shown? If so, describe its location, width, and how it's labeled\n3. Are there any electric easements shown? Describe them\n4. Are there any utility poles or utility structures shown on the plat?\n5. In the legend or title block, is there any reference to transmission facilities?\n\nReport exactly what you see labeled on the plat.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided plat sheet for the \"MECEY SUBDIVISION,\" here are the findings in response to your specific questions:\n\n**1. All recorded easements shown on the plat:**\nThe plat shows dashed lines indicating several easements, labeled exactly as follows:\n*   **North boundary of LOT 1:** A dashed line is shown along the inside of the northern boundary line, labeled **`5' P.U.E. (Exist.)`**.\n*   **South boundary of LOT 1:** A dashed line is shown along the inside of the southern boundary line. It has a stacked label that reads:\n    **`Exist 5' Elec. Ease. &`**\n    **`5' P.U.E.`**\n*   **North boundary of LOT 2:** A dashed line is shown along the inside of the northern boundary line, labeled **`5' P.U.E.`**.\n*   **South boundary of LOT 2:** A dashed line is shown along the inside of the southern boundary line, labeled **`5' P.U.E.`**.\n*   **Interior of LOT 2 (Drainage):** A 26-foot wide area bounded by dashed lines traverses the eastern portion of Lot 2. It is labeled:\n    **`26' Drainage`**\n    **`Easement (Existing)`**\n*   **Interior of LOT 2 (Utility line):** A dashed line runs generally east-to-west across the middle/lower portion of Lot 2. It is labeled **`10' [text unclear, appears to be \"Watermain\" or \"Wastewater\"] Ease. Existing`**. Due to image resolution, the exact type of utility in this 10-foot easement is difficult to read with absolute certainty.\n\n*(Note: Dashed lines also appear along the road frontages of Valley View Road and Clawson Road, but they do not have specific independent text labels pointing directly to them, other than the general P.U.E. labels mentioned above near the corners.)*\n\n**2. Transmission easement presence:**\n*   There are **no** transmission easements shown or labeled anywhere on this plat.\n\n**3. Electric easements shown:**\n*   Yes, there is one explicitly labeled electric easement. It is located along the southern boundary of **LOT 1**.\n*   It is described by the label: **`Exist 5' Elec. Ease. & 5' P.U.E.`** indicating a 5-foot width.\n\n**4. Utility poles or utility structures shown:**\n*   There are **no** utility poles, towers, guy wires, or utility structures drawn, symbolized, or labeled on this plat.\n\n**5. Legend or title block references to transmission facilities:**\n*   There is **no** reference to transmission facilities in the legend or the title blocks.\n*   The \"LEGEND\" solely contains:\n    *   `Iron Stake Set`\n    *   `Iron Stake Found`\n    *   `Travis County Deed Records` (with a circle symbol)\n    *   `Scale 1\" = 100 Feet`","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1422,"outputTokens":668,"totalTokens":5690,"reasoningTokens":3600},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1618032]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do n