{"level":30,"time":1776952100205,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":8,"prompt":"Examine the demolition plan. Identify all utility lines shown as existing (to be demolished or removed). Note: (1) Are there existing water lines in the ROW? (2) Are there existing wastewater lines? (3) Are there fire hydrants or other utility appurtenances? (4) Does the plan show these utilities being removed, abandoned, or retained? (5) Are there any abandonment notes indicating how removed utilities are capped, plugged, or terminated?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided demolition plan, here is the analysis regarding utility lines and appurtenances:\n\n**(1) Are there existing water lines in the ROW?**\nYes, there are existing water lines shown in the Right-Of-Way (Valley View Road). \n*   The main plan shows a line marked with `-W-` running along the left side.\n*   The inset plan in the bottom left corner, titled \"CITY OF AUSTIN WATER INTERSECTION\" for \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\", explicitly identifies an existing **\"8\\\" PVC WATER LINE\"** and points out a **\"6\\\" DI Water Line\"**.\n\n**(2) Are there existing wastewater lines?**\nYes, there are existing wastewater lines shown.\n*   A line marked with `-WW-` runs along the ROW on the top left.\n*   It connects to an appurtenance labeled **\"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\"** in the top left corner.\n\n**(3) Are there fire hydrants or other utility appurtenances?**\nYes, several utility appurtenances are identified on the plan:\n*   **Fire Hydrants**: There is a callout for **\"Existing Fire Hydrant to be Removed\"** (main plan, bottom left) and **\"Remove Existing Fire Hydrant 172943 and Replace with new Fire Hydrant\"** (inset plan).\n*   **Valves & Tees**: The inset plan contains a callout to **\"Remove Existing Valve and Tee\"**.\n*   **Backflow Preventer**: A callout on the center-left side indicates a **\"Backflow Preventer to be Removed\"**.\n*   **Meters**: A **\"Gas Meter\"** is shown near the top-left curve, and a **\"Water Meter\"** is indicated (with notes about a 2\" water meter return).\n*   **Manholes & Vaults**: **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**, **\"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\"**, and an **\"AT&T Vault\"** are located near the top left corner. Another **\"Existing Manhole\"** is shown centrally.\n*   **Grease Trap**: A callout in the center points to an **\"Abandon and Remove Grease Trap\"**.\n*   **Power/Electric**: There are multiple callouts stating **\"Coordinate with City of Austin for the removal of power poles and electric lines\"**.\n\n**(4) Does the plan show these utilities being removed, abandoned, or retained?**\nThe plan indicates a mix of removals and abandonments:\n*   **Removed**: Fire hydrants (**\"Existing Fire Hydrant to be Removed\"**), valves/tees (**\"Remove Existing Valve and Tee\"**), the backflow preventer (**\"Backflow Preventer to be Removed\"**), power poles/electric lines (**\"removal of power poles and electric lines\"**), and the grease trap (**\"Abandon and Remove Grease Trap\"**). \n*   **Abandoned**: The fire service line has a callout stating **\"Existing Fire Service to be Abandoned per Intersection Map Below\"**. Private water and wastewater lines are also to be abandoned per the site notes.\n\n**(5) Are there any abandonment notes indicating how removed utilities are capped, plugged, or terminated?**\nYes, there are explicit abandonment instructions:\n*   **Site Demolition Notes, Item #4** states: **\"Contractor is responsible for locating and abandoning existing private water and wastewater lines. All abandoned piping is to be plugged.\"**\n*   **Site Demolition Notes, Item #9** states: **\"Contractor to remove gas & water meters and return meters to respective utility companies.\"**\n*   A callout box on the left side (referencing the fire service) provides specific termination instructions for the meter: **\"Existing Fire Service to be Abandoned per Intersection Map Below. Return 2\\\" water meter #24327671 to Austin Water Inspector for Credit.\"**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1406,"outputTokens":840,"totalTokens":4339,"reasoningTokens":2093},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2303940]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the demolition plan. Identify all utility lines shown as existing (to be demolished or removed). Note: (1) Are there existing water lines in the ROW? (2) Are there existing wastewater lines? (3) Are there fire hydrants or other utility appurtenances? (4) Does the plan show these utilities being removed, abandoned, or retained? (5) Are there any abandonment notes indicating how removed utilities are capped, plugged, or terminated?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Jk3RuWMv4Phk1iI7AJ4ZiChz","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:48:20 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::6mtbm-1776952073827-00fbfc51f2ff"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided demolition plan, here is the analysis regarding utility lines and appurtenances:\n\n**(1) Are there existing water lines in the ROW?**\nYes, there are existing water lines shown in the Right-Of-Way (Valley View Road). \n*   The main plan shows a line marked with `-W-` running along the left side.\n*   The inset plan in the bottom left corner, titled \"CITY OF AUSTIN WATER INTERSECTION\" for \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\", explicitly identifies an existing **\"8\\\" PVC WATER LINE\"** and points out a **\"6\\\" DI Water Line\"**.\n\n**(2) Are there existing wastewater lines?**\nYes, there are existing wastewater lines shown.\n*   A line marked with `-WW-` runs along the ROW on the top left.\n*   It connects to an appurtenance labeled **\"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\"** in the top left corner.\n\n**(3) Are there fire hydrants or other utility appurtenances?**\nYes, several utility appurtenances are identified on the plan:\n*   **Fire Hydrants**: There is a callout for **\"Existing Fire Hydrant to be Removed\"** (main plan, bottom left) and **\"Remove Existing Fire Hydrant 172943 and Replace with new Fire Hydrant\"** (inset plan).\n*   **Valves & Tees**: The inset plan contains a callout to **\"Remove Existing Valve and Tee\"**.\n*   **Backflow Preventer**: A callout on the center-left side indicates a **\"Backflow Preventer to be Removed\"**.\n*   **Meters**: A **\"Gas Meter\"** is shown near the top-left curve, and a **\"Water Meter\"** is indicated (with notes about a 2\" water meter return).\n*   **Manholes & Vaults**: **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**, **\"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\"**, and an **\"AT&T Vault\"** are located near the top left corner. Another **\"Existing Manhole\"** is shown centrally.\n*   **Grease Trap**: A callout in the center points to an **\"Abandon and Remove Grease Trap\"**.\n*   **Power/Electric**: There are multiple callouts stating **\"Coordinate with City of Austin for the removal of power poles and electric lines\"**.\n\n**(4) Does the plan show these utilities being removed, abandoned, or retained?**\nThe plan indicates a mix of removals and abandonments:\n*   **Removed**: Fire hydrants (**\"Existing Fire Hydrant to be Removed\"**), valves/tees (**\"Remove Existing Valve and Tee\"**), the backflow preventer (**\"Backflow Preventer to be Removed\"**), power poles/electric lines (**\"removal of power poles and electric lines\"**), and the grease trap (**\"Abandon and Remove Grease Trap\"**). \n*   **Abandoned**: The fire service line has a callout stating **\"Existing Fire Service to be Abandoned per Intersection Map Below\"**. Private water and wastewater lines are also to be abandoned per the site notes.\n\n**(5) Are there any abandonment notes indicating how removed utilities are capped, plugged, or terminated?**\nYes, there are explicit abandonment instructions:\n*   **Site Demolition Notes, Item #4** states: **\"Contractor is responsible for locating and abandoning existing private water and wastewater lines. All abandoned piping is to be plugged.\"**\n*   **Site Demolition Notes, Item #9** states: **\"Contractor to remove gas & water meters and return meters to respective utility companies.\"**\n*   A callout box on the left side (referencing the fire service) provides specific termination instructions for the meter: **\"Existing Fire Service to be Abandoned per Intersection Map Below. Return 2\\\" water meter #24327671 to Austin Water Inspector for Credit.\"**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1406,"outputTokens":840,"totalTokens":4339,"reasoningTokens":2093},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":3145661.145446,"endTime":3171635.006065,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"CiP