{"level":30,"time":1776952107065,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"I need to verify transformer pad placement and clearances against UCM § 1.10.4 requirements. Please examine this electrical plan and provide specific information about each transformer pad:\n\nFor EACH transformer pad visible on this plan, please provide:\n1. **Pad Location** - Which building is it nearest to, and what is its distance from any building wall or structure? (Need to verify 10-foot clearance from buildings on hot-stick side)\n2. **Pad to Parking/Traffic Area** - What is the distance from the pad to the nearest parking space or traffic area? (Need to verify within 6 feet for AE truck access per UCM § 1.10.4)\n3. **Easement Encumbrance** - Is there a dedicated AE easement boundary shown around each pad? If so, what are the dimensions?\n4. **Fence/Clearance Areas** - Are there any fences or barriers shown near the pads? What clearances are noted?\n5. **Are pads on customer's property** - Confirm each pad is NOT in public ROW or dedicated parkland\n\nPlease measure or estimate distances where visible on the plan and identify the specific pad locations by building reference.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the \"Valley View Townhomes,\" here is the detailed information regarding the transformer pads. \n\n*Note: All distance measurements provided below are visual estimates based on the graphic scale provided in the top right corner of the document, which reads exactly: **Scale 1\" = 20'**. The plan does not explicitly label the \"hot-stick\" side of the pads.*\n\nThere are two transformer pads explicitly labeled on this site plan. They are identified by a solid dark blue square symbol with a leader line labeled exactly: **Electrical Transformer Pad**.\n\n### Transformer Pad 1 (West side of property)\n**1. Pad Location**\n*   **Nearest Buildings:** This pad is located between **Bldg. 1** to the north and **Bldg. 8** to the south.\n*   **Distance to Buildings:** Based on the visual scale, the pad appears to be approximately **10 to 15 feet** from the nearest wall of Bldg. 1 (near Unit 201/202). It appears to be approximately **15 to 20 feet** from the nearest wall of Bldg. 8 (near Unit 801).\n\n**2. Pad to Parking/Traffic Area**\n*   **Distance:** The pad is situated immediately adjacent to the curb of the internal looped driveway. Based on the scale, the distance from the pad symbol to the curb line appears to be **less than 5 feet**, suggesting it meets the criteria for being within 6 feet for AE truck access.\n\n**3. Easement Encumbrance**\n*   **Boundary:** There is a dashed rectangular boundary drawn immediately surrounding the solid blue pad symbol. \n*   **Dimensions:** There are **no specific dimensions** labeled for this dashed boundary. Nearby, pointing toward an area slightly south of the pad, there is text that reads **\"Vault Easement\"**, but it does not point directly to the box around the transformer pad itself.\n\n**4. Fence/Clearance Areas**\n*   **Fences:** There are **no fences or physical barriers** drawn around the pad.\n*   **Clearances:** While the dashed rectangular box likely denotes a clearance or easement area, there are **no specific clearance dimensions** (e.g., 10x10) noted in text near this pad.\n\n**5. Property Status**\n*   **Customer Property:** Yes, the pad is located inside the heavy dashed-dotted line marking the development's property boundary. It is not located in the public Right-of-Way (which is shown west of the property line) and there is no indication of dedicated parkland.\n\n---\n\n### Transformer Pad 2 (East side of property)\n**1. Pad Location**\n*   **Nearest Buildings:** This pad is located south of **Bldg. 4** and east of **Bldg. 6**.\n*   **Distance to Buildings:** Based on the visual scale, the pad appears to be approximately **20 to 25 feet** south of the nearest wall of Bldg. 4. It appears to be approximately **20 to 30 feet** east of the nearest wall of Bldg. 6.\n\n**2. Pad to Parking/Traffic Area**\n*   **Distance:** The pad is located immediately adjacent to the outer curve of the internal driveway. Based on the scale, the distance from the pad symbol to the curb line appears to be **less than 5 feet**, suggesting it meets the criteria for being within 6 feet for AE truck access.\n\n**3. Easement Encumbrance**\n*   **Boundary:** Similar to Pad 1, there is a dashed rectangular boundary drawn immediately surrounding the solid blue pad symbol.\n*   **Dimensions:** There are **no specific dimensions** or explicit easement labels pointing to this specific dashed boundary on the plan.\n\n**4. Fence/Clearance Areas**\n*   **Fences:** There are **no fences or physical barriers** drawn enclosing the pad. (A \"Wood Fence\" is indicated further east on the property boundary, but it does not enclose the pad).\n*   **Clearances:** There are **no specific clearance dimensions** noted in text near this pad.\n\n**5. Property Status**\n*   **Customer Property:** Yes, the pad is located inside the heavy dashed-dotted line marking the development's property boundary. It is not located in the public Right-of-Way or dedicated parkland.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1561,"outputTokens":950,"totalTokens":4809,"reasoningTokens":2298},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"I need to verify transformer pad placement and clearances against UCM § 1.10.4 requirements. Please examine this electrical plan and provide specific information about each transformer pad:\n\nFor EACH transformer pad visible on this plan, please provide:\n1. **Pad Location** - Which building is it nearest to, and what is its distance from any building wall or structure? (Need to verify 10-foot clearance from buildings on hot-stick side)\n2. **Pad to Parking/Traffic Area** - What is the distance from the pad to the nearest parking space or traffic area? (Need to verify within 6 feet for AE truck access per UCM § 1.10.4)\n3. **Easement Encumbrance** - Is there a dedicated AE easement boundary shown around each pad? If so, what are the dimensions?\n4. **Fence/Clearance Areas** - Are there any fences or barriers shown near the pads? What clearances are noted?\n5. **Are pads on customer's property** - Confirm each pad is NOT in public ROW or dedicated parkland\n\nPlease measure or estimate distances where visible on the plan and identify the specific pad locations by building reference."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-UxL9jIWPD7eezBIWQBw98PTG","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:48:27 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::dc2rt-1776952074837-2dcb76f626d8"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the \"Valley View Townhomes,\" here is the detailed information regarding the transformer pads. \n\n*Note: All distance measurements provided below are visual estimates based on the graphic scale provided in the top right corner of the document, which reads exactly: **Scale 1\" = 20'**. The plan does not explicitly label the \"hot-stick\" side of the pads.*\n\nThere are two transformer pads explicitly labeled on this site plan. They are identified by a solid dark blue square symbol with a leader line labeled exactly: **Electrical Transformer Pad**.\n\n### Transformer Pad 1 (West side of property)\n**1. Pad Location**\n*   **Nearest Buildings:** This pad is located 