{"level":30,"time":1776952111454,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":20,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 20 (Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile) and identify:\n\n1. All utilities shown in the ROW (right-of-way) area near Valley View Road\n2. Distances between proposed utilities and existing ROW facilities (water lines, gas lines, sewer lines, etc.)\n3. Whether distances of 24 inches or less are shown for any utility positioning\n4. Any notes about existing utility clearances or conflicts\n5. Any evidence of AULCC (Austin Utility Location and Coordination Commission) coordination\n\nPlease provide specific measurements and locations shown on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 20 (Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile) from the provided site plan document, here are the details regarding your requests:\n\n**1. All utilities shown in the ROW (right-of-way) area near Valley View Road**\nBased on the plan view (top half of the sheet) and the Legend provided, the following utilities and related infrastructure are shown in or near the indicated ROW area:\n*   **Existing Water Line:** Identified by the line type `- W -` and a callout stating \"Replace AC pipe with DI Pipe per Note this Sheet Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction\". There is also a callout to \"Install 8\" Gate Valve on Existing 8\" Water Line\".\n*   **Existing Wastewater Line:** Identified by the line type `- WW -` crossing the proposed alignment.\n*   **Existing Gas Line:** Identified by a line labeled `- G -` crossing the proposed alignment (Note: 'G' is not explicitly in the legend but is standard notation).\n*   **Proposed Water Line:** Shown via thick solid lines connecting to the existing main, and thick dashed lines (labeled with `W` inside the line per legend).\n*   **Existing Fire Hydrant:** Callout states \"Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant\".\n*   **Proposed Fire Demand Meter/Vault:** Callout for \"8\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault See Detail S12-AW-02\".\n*   **Proposed Storm Drain:** Identified by the line type `- SD -` near the vault area.\n\n**2. Distances between proposed utilities and existing ROW facilities**\n*   **No specific clearance distances (dimensions) are shown** on this sheet between the proposed water line and the existing crossing utilities.\n*   The Profile View (bottom half) shows visual crossings of the proposed water line (\"Wtr-Ln-A\") beneath an existing wastewater line (labeled \"-WW-\") and an existing gas line (labeled \"-G-\"). However, there are no vertical dimension lines or numerical text indicating the exact clearance distance between the outside diameters of these pipes at the crossing points.\n\n**3. Whether distances of 24 inches or less are shown for any utility positioning**\n*   Because specific numerical clearance dimensions are omitted at the utility crossing points in both the plan and profile views, **there are no distances of 24 inches or less explicitly shown or confirmed** on this sheet.\n\n**4. Any notes about existing utility clearances or conflicts**\nThe sheet contains several notes directing the contractor regarding existing utilities and potential conflicts. They are quoted exactly as they appear:\n\n*   **Under \"Utility Notes\":**\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n*   **Under \"Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends\" (second paragraph):**\n    *   \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"\n*   **Callout pointing to the existing water line in the plan view:**\n    *   \"Replace AC pipe with DI Pipe per Note this Sheet Contractor to Verify Location and Depth Prior to Construction\"\n\n**5. Any evidence of AULCC (Austin Utility Location and Coordination Commission) coordination**\n*   **No evidence found.** There are no stamps, signatures, or specific notes on this sheet explicitly mentioning AULCC or indicating AULCC coordination. There is a logo for \"Texas 811 - Call Before You Dig!!\", but no direct reference to AULCC.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1432,"outputTokens":839,"totalTokens":4350,"reasoningTokens":2079},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1220588]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 20 (Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile) and identify:\n\n1. All utilities shown in the ROW (right-of-way) area near Valley View Road\n2. Distances between proposed utilities and existing ROW facilities (water lines, gas lines, sewer lines, etc.)\n3. Whether distances of 24 inches or less are shown for any utility positioning\n4. Any notes about existing utility clearances or conflicts\n5. Any evidence of AULCC (Austin Utility Location and Coordination Commission) coordination\n\nPlease provide specific measurements and locations shown on this sheet."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Dcrt9epjXYlGhIgHXF2FizHh","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:48:31 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","