{"level":30,"time":1776952124961,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QxqTwCQDURA2EmJ319P6GK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\n     4→\n     5→Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     6→\n     7→The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     8→\n     9→The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n    10→\n    11→The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n    12→\n    13→Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\n    14→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"ec727771-29c8-4453-8c17-273fa81dc314","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-14.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 14\n\n## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\n\nAustin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n\nThe owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n\nThe owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n\nAny relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776952125008,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PVaLoqvprRjirZFd9zgSV7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014xMyDfYSmWNGbNSD9wB6Ts","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-20.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":68149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":598},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"54c954e5-7dc9-41e5-af72-0ee86ece5075"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952125047,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014xMyDfYSmWNGbNSD9wB6Ts","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 20\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Transmission Notes\n     6→1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n     7→2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n     8→3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n     9→4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    11→6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n    12→7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n    13→8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n    14→9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n    15→10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n    16→11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n    17→12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n    18→13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n    19→14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n    20→15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n    21→16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    22→  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    23→  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    24→  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"4691c6a8-cfdd-4f9b-8f80-e59f02229f34","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-20.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 20\n\n## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\n\nElectric Transmission Notes\n1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n  · any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776952135948,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RMAwTHFLoDSrhyZTZLqnUx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NLhEeq13XqUVQ7h6ASz32K","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Water line crossings with existing utilities in ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water utility crossing shown on Sheet 20 crossing existing wastewater and gas lines, but no crossing detail identifies AE underground facility proximity or demonstrates 12-inch clearance. Verify that water line crossings do not impact AE underground conduit; if AE underground is present at these crossing locations, clearance dimensions must be labeled."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Underground electrical infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electrical infrastructure shown on Sheet 21; water and wastewater utilities shown on Sheet 19. The plans do not clearly identify whether any non-AE utilities are proposed in joint trenches with AE underground conduit, or indicate if a written joint-trench agreement with Austin Energy is on file."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM 2.9.2.B.17","UCM 2.9.1.B.3"],"applicableAreas":["Water utility tap in ROW crossing existing wastewater and gas lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 20 profile shows water line (Wtr-Ln-A) crossing existing wastewater and gas lines, but the crossing method (trenchless vs. open-cut) is not identified on the plan or profile. Vertical separation distances are not labeled. Without crossing method designation and labeled clearance dimensions, the applicable separation standard cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM 1.14.9"],"applicableAreas":["Demolition activities adjacent to transmission easement and transmission structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":8},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Demolition plan (Sheet 8) Site Demolition Notes do not address required transmission line safety clearances detailed in Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes. Missing: (1) pre-construction safety meeting requirement with Austin Energy 48 hours before work commencement, (2) barricade requirement 10 feet from transmission structures, (3) warning signs under overhead transmission facilities, and (4) prohibition on materials or spoils storage within transmission easement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM 1.14.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transmission ROW access corridor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction plans do not demonstrate maintenance of a 25-foot-wide access corridor with minimum 16-foot vertical clearance along the transmission ROW. Transmission easement boundaries and access corridor requirements are not graphically delineated on the site plan or erosion control plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["DCM 1.2.4.E.2.e"],"applicableAreas":["SCM staging area on western side of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 5 shows a 'Staging and Storage Area' on the western side of the site, but no vertical clearance dimensions or annotations are provided. The plan does not demonstrate the 14-foot minimum vertical clearance from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects above the staging area."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM 1.14.9"],"applicableAreas":["Staging and storage areas relative to transmission easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes prohibit staging, spoils, and dumpsters within 25 feet of transmission structures. However, the transmission easement boundaries are not delineated on Sheet 5 (Erosion Control Plan) or Sheet 9 (Site Plan), making it impossible to verify that the shown staging area does not overlap transmission easement or violate 25-foot clearance from transmission structures."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM 1.10.3","UCM 1.14.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site with transmission lines and distribution utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electrical clearance zones or envelopes are graphically delineated on any plan sheets. Transmission line safety buffers (including the 25-foot no-dig zone and transmission easement boundaries referenced in Sheet 3 General Notes) are not shown. Distribution overhead conductor clearance envelopes are not graphically represented."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2441,"cache_read_input_tokens":71759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2441},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4a1fc80-d233-40ef-93cf-fcf0c529f6de","uuid":"2ee9d4bf-a667-4b75-90b0-0169de478482"}
