{"level":30,"time":1776952182902,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JVJVAoW9vT4MSMxxFQiBfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I found it. In Block 8, Section 1.6.3.B.4 states:\n\n\"4. In all cases, trees shall be preserved according to the requirements of Section 3 of the Environmental Criteria Manual. The access drive and staging area shall be designed to preserve trees 8\" in diameter and greater to the maximum extent possible. Trees 8\" in diameter and larger shall be surveyed and shown for the proposed access easement at the time of construction plan permitting.\"\n\nThis mentions \"access drive and staging area\" but does NOT specify the 14-ft vertical clearance requirement from DCM 1.2.4.E.\n\nThe block discusses tree preservation in the access drive and staging area design, but doesn't mention the specific 14-foot vertical clearance from vegetation and other objects that is required by DCM 1.2.4.E.\n\nThis is actually a deficiency - the 14-ft clearance is not documented in the maintenance requirements shown on Sheet 16.\n\nLet me now summarize all my findings and compile the final output. Based on my research:\n\n## APPLICABLE STATUS DETERMINATIONS:\n\n1. **EL-1.1** - N/A (Valley View Road is a local street, not a CTC or Urban Roadway)\n2. **EL-1.2** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Overhead utilities present but no clearance dimensions shown)\n3. **EL-1.3** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Overhead utilities present but no clearance dimensions shown)\n4. **EL-1.4** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Vault proximity to overhead utilities unclear; no AE approval evident)\n5. **EL-1.5** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (No clearance dimensions shown to verify)\n6. **EL-1.6** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Service entrance equipment shown but no clearance dimensions)\n7. **EL-1.7** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Service drop identification and clearance heights not documented)\n\n\n8. **EL-1.8** - N/A (No TGS lines identified on site plan)\n9. **EL-1.9** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Underground utility crossings proposed but clearance dimensions not labeled)\n10. **EL-1.10** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (No joint trench agreements documented)\n11. **EL-1.11** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Utility tap shown but AULCC approval documentation not evident)\n12. **EL-1.12** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Utility crossing method not clearly identified)\n13. **EL-1.13** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Encasement specifications not documented)\n14. **EL-1.14** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Conduit sizing and protection details missing from plans)\n15. **EL-1.15** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Storm drain manhole clearances from AE poles not documented)\n16. **EL-1.16** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Utility routing relative to easement boundaries not clearly documented)\n17. **EL-1.17** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Transmission structures not shown/located on site plan)\n18. **EL-1.18** - FAIL (Demolition plan missing required transmission safety notes)\n19. **EL-1.19** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Transmission ROW access corridor not depicted)\n20. **EL-1.20** - FAIL (Demolition plan missing required caution note for at-grade utility appurtenances)\n21. **EL-1.21** - PASS (Field verification language present in utility notes on Sheet 21)\n22. **EL-1.22** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (SCM staging area vertical clearances not documented)\n23. **EL-1.23** - FAIL (SCM maintenance access drive 14-ft vertical clearance not documented)\n24. **EL-1.24** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Work zone vertical clearances below overhead utilities not documented)\n25. **EL-1.25** - NOT-VERIFIABLE (Staging plans not examined in detail; cannot confirm overlap avoidance)\n26. **EL-1.26** - FAIL (No overhead electrical clearance zones graphically delineated)\n27. **EL-1.27** - FAIL (No horizontal height limit lines shown for overhead utilities)\n28. **EL-1.28** - FAIL (No sloped/stepped height limit lines depicted for overhead utilities on graded areas)\n\nI need to distinguish between actual deficiencies versus items where compliance simply can't be verified. A FAIL means the required element is demonstrably absent from the plans, while NOT-VERIFIABLE indicates insufficient documentation to assess compliance. For instance, EL-1.18 is a FAIL because the demolition plan omits the mandatory transmission safety notes covering the 48-hour meeting, barricades, and warning signage. Similarly, EL-1.20 fails because the caution notation for at-grade utility appurtenances is missing from the demolition notes. EL-1.23 also constitutes a FAIL since the maintenance requirements don't specify the required 14-ft vertical clearance for the access drive.\n\nThe graphic elements present additional clear failures: no clearance envelope boundaries appear anywhere on the sheets (EL-1.26), no horizontal height limit lines are shown (EL-1.27), and no sloped or stepped height limit lines are depicted (EL-1.28). In contrast, NOT-VERIFIABLE conditions exist where utilities or equipment are present but lack proper dimensioning—such as clearance measurements for the utilities themselves (EL-1.2, EL-1.3), service equipment clearances (EL-1.6), and underground utility crossing dimensions (EL-1.9). The transmission facility references also fall into this category since the notes exist but don't provide sufficient detail to confirm all clearance requirements are met.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2950,"cache_read_input_tokens":77479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2950},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a849ead6-fbef-4e89-ab5d-465127c74861","uuid":"82d0cff7-974a-45e2-aeeb-39fbbb066591"}
