{"level":30,"time":1776952183690,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the grading plan and report:\n1. Are there any horizontal dashed height limit lines shown to delineate overhead utility clearance envelopes?\n2. Are there any sloped or stepped height limit lines shown to account for grade changes beneath overhead utilities?\n3. Where is the overhead electric line (OHE) shown relative to the site grading, and are clearances to the grade documented?\n\nDescribe what clearance-related graphics you see on the grading plan.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (11)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952193942,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PzGXtoGw8dFduA2VZLyQHM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important! The 1975 Mecey Subdivision plat DOES show some easements:\n- 15' P.U.E. (northern boundary)\n- 5' Electric Easement (southern boundary - Lot 1)\n- 5' Electric Easement (northern boundary - Lot 2)\n- 25' Drainage Easement (crossing Lot 2 interior, west-east)\n- 10' Water & WW Easement (crossing Lot 2 interior, south)\n\nBUT facts.md says there are ADDITIONAL easements that are NOT shown on the submitted site plan:\n- **Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 ac, NE interior, Instrument 2010070731, 2010)** - NOT on 1975 plat, NOT on current site plan\n- **City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 ac, NE corner, Instrument 2011021137, 2011)** - NOT on 1975 plat, NOT on current site plan\n- Additional easements from other plats (Cortez Heights Vol 64/13, Trico Vol 69/14) - NOT verified on site plan\n\nSo the issue is:\n1. The 1975 Mecey plat shows SOME easements\n2. But the CURRENT site plan (Sheet 9 and others) should show ALL current easements, including the 2010 and 2011 recorded easements\n\nThe fact that facts.md says these recent easements \"NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and NOT in the COA GIS easement layer\" means they MUST be added to the site plan.\n\nThis is a **FAIL** for EL-2.15 (and general compliance) - the site plan does not depict all recorded easements, particularly the critical no-build Greenbelt easement and City Drainage easement.\n\nNow let me finalize my findings and prepare the structured output.\n\n\n- **EL-2.10 - Utilities routed under detention pond:** Sheet 15 shows electrical and wastewater lines crossing through the biofiltration/detention pond footprint in the NE corner (Unit 501 pond area), including the sedimentation basin and biofiltration media. This violates reviewer convention—utilities cannot be placed underneath detention facilities.\n\n- **EL-2.15 - Easement boundaries encroaching into ROW / Easements not depicted:** Two recorded easements are missing from the site plan: the perpetual Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres in the NE interior) and another easement affecting Lot 1. Sheet 2, Sheet 9, and Sheet 21 do not show these easements, which are documented in county clerk records and violate UCM § 2.9.1.A.1.\n\n- **EL-2.22 - Transformer pad deficiencies:** Transformer Pad 1 (positioned between Buildings 1 and 8 on the west side) and Transformer Pad 2 (between Buildings 4 on the east side) fail to meet UCM § 1.5.2.6 and UCM § 1.10.4 requirements.\n\nThe preliminary electrical design plan depicts transformer pads as dashed boundary boxes but lacks critical specifications: pad dimensions must align with AE Design standards rather than using a generic dimension, and each pad requires either a dedicated AE easement boundary or a recorded AE License Agreement per UCM § 1.10.10.3 and § 1.10.4. Need to coordinate with Austin Energy to finalize pad dimensions from the customer's AutoCAD drawings and secure recorded utility easements for both pads before moving forward.\n\nUtility easement boundaries are shown across the site on the plat and electrical plan, but the submission is missing License Agreements from AE Public Involvement for items within private AE easements and City Manager licenses for items in public utility easements or public ROW per UCM § 1.10.10.3 and § 14-11-41. Compliance cannot be confirmed without these licensing documents. All required License Agreements and City Manager licenses for any structures, paving, or landscaping within recorded easement boundaries must be provided.\n\nThe previous assisted living facility (demolished June 2022 under Permit 2022-096813 BP) may have left abandoned utilities on site or in the right-of-way. The demolition plan needs to explicitly document removal of all abandoned utilities that conflict with the proposed biofiltration/detention pond, new building locations, and utility routing, including evidence of caps, plugs, and abandonments. This documentation is required before construction can proceed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3724,"cache_read_input_tokens":74294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3724},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"33ce60fc-f4d5-4139-bd7e-ac6c28acc305"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952198482,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PzGXtoGw8dFduA2VZLyQHM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research and analysis of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, I have identified the key deficiencies within the Underground Utility Routing and Placement grouping. Let me now prepare my structured findings.\n\n## FINAL RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**Applicability Assessment:**\nThe site fronts **Valley View Road**, a **Local Street (ASMP Level 1)** — NOT a CTC, Urban Roadway, or Hill Country Roadway Corridor. The property is zoned **MF-2 (Multi-Family)** with **NO regulating plans** (not Plaza Saltillo TOD or NBG). Therefore, most Subchapter E utility undergrounding requirements (EL-2.1 through EL-2.4, EL-2.9) and regulating plan provisions (EL-2.5 through EL-2.8) are **NOT APPLICABLE** to this site.\n\n**Critical Findings:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (Utilities Under Detention Pond)** — **CRITICAL DEFICIENCY FOUND**\n   - Sheet 15 (Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan) clearly depicts electrical (E) and wastewater (WW) utility lines routed directly through the pond footprint, crossing through sedimentation basin and biofiltration media.\n\n2. **EL-2.15 (Easement Deficiency)** — **CRITICAL DEFICIENCY FOUND**  \n   - facts.md identifies two perpetual recorded easements NOT depicted on the submitted site plan:\n     - Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 ac, NE interior, perpetual no-build zone)\n     - City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 ac, NE corner)\n   - Together these encumber ~19% of the property but are completely absent from submitted plans.\n\n3. **EL-2.22 (Transformer Pad Deficiency)** — **DEFICIENCY FOUND**\n   - Two transformer pads shown on Sheet 21 but NOT dimensioned per AE Design specifications\n   - NO dedicated AE easement boundaries explicitly labeled or recorded\n   - Missing License Agreement documentation from AE Public Involvement\n\n4. **Other Items Not Applicable:**\n   - EL-2.11, EL-2.12: NO street trees in ROW (landscape plan confirms trees are on private property only)\n   - EL-2.13: Transformer pads on private property (not in parkland)\n   - EL-2.24: NOT a Table B site (MF-2 zoning, <3 acres, residential)\n   - EL-2.20: NO underground storage tanks on site\n\nNow let me prepare the structured output with only the fail and not-verifiable items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3724,"cache_read_input_tokens":74294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3724},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8937ea6-a85f-452c-ba14-5b8849922a4d","uuid":"5ba86c86-973b-41c9-ac55-6f5b9cc34947"}
