{"level":30,"time":1776952209345,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the grading plan and report:\n1. Are there any horizontal dashed height limit lines shown to delineate overhead utility clearance envelopes?\n2. Are there any sloped or stepped height limit lines shown to account for grade changes beneath overhead utilities?\n3. Where is the overhead electric line (OHE) shown relative to the site grading, and are clearances to the grade documented?\n\nDescribe what clearance-related graphics you see on the grading plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there any horizontal dashed height limit lines shown to delineate overhead utility clearance envelopes?**\nNo. There are no horizontal dashed lines or markings labeled as height limits or clearance envelopes for overhead utilities. The dashed lines present on the plan generally represent existing grading contours, proposed storm drain lines, or property/easement boundaries (as indicated in the Legend).\n\n**2. Are there any sloped or stepped height limit lines shown to account for grade changes beneath overhead utilities?**\nNo. This document is a top-down plan view. It does not contain any sloped or stepped height limit lines, nor does it provide profile or section views that would typically depict vertical clearance accounting for grade changes beneath overhead utilities. \n\n**3. Where is the overhead electric line (OHE) shown relative to the site grading, and are clearances to the grade documented?**\nAn overhead electric line, denoted by standard linework with text reading \"- OH E -\", is shown running approximately north-south along the western boundary of the site, adjacent to and partially within the right-of-way for \"Valley View Road\". \n\nWhile site grading is shown beneath and adjacent to this line (via existing dashed contours, proposed solid contours, and ground spot elevations like \"+681.41\" and \"+679.98\"), **there are no clearances to the grade documented**. There are no annotations, dimensions, or specific callouts indicating the vertical distance between the proposed/existing ground and the overhead electric wires.\n\n**Summary of clearance-related graphics:**\nThere are **no clearance-related graphics** depicted on this grading plan. The plan solely illustrates ground-level features such as existing and proposed ground contours, spot elevations, building footprints (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8), retaining walls, and utility easements (e.g., \"7.5' P.U.E.\", \"25' Building Setback\").","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1403,"outputTokens":419,"totalTokens":3373,"reasoningTokens":1551},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the grading plan and report:\n1. Are there any horizontal dashed height limit lines shown to delineate overhead utility clearance envelopes?\n2. Are there any sloped or stepped height limit lines shown to account for grade changes beneath overhead utilities?\n3. Where is the overhead electric line (OHE) shown relative to the site grading, and are clearances to the grade documented?\n\nDescribe what clearance-related graphics you see on the grading plan."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-3UAA6stTLf0zDKvFI597BvDC","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:50:09 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::rmlrs-1776952184528-5167d023ef2a"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text