{"level":30,"time":1776952219398,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019meEBcqwzZ3QHBsMAFCMv1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, I have evaluated all 28 checklist items in the Overhead and Vertical Electrical Clearances grouping. Here are my findings:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**Site Context:**\n- Valley View Road is a LOCAL STREET (not a CTC or Urban Roadway) per ASMP street classification\n- The site contains overhead electric lines (OHE) along the western and southern boundaries\n- The site plan includes utility tap connections to public 8\" water and wastewater mains\n- Biofiltration/detention pond is located in the northeast portion of the site\n- Sheet 3 (General Notes) contains 16 detailed Electric Transmission Notes referencing transmission easements, structures, and clearance requirements\n- HOWEVER: No transmission easements or transmission structures are depicted on any site plan sheets, the plat, or in the property facts\n\n**Critical Gap Identified:**\nSheet 3 includes comprehensive transmission facility requirements (25-ft clearances from structures, 48-hr pre-construction safety meetings, barricades, warning signs, etc.), but **no transmission facilities are graphically shown or located on the site plans**. This creates ambiguity about whether transmission facilities actually exist on or adjacent to the site.\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Overhead utility clearance envelope boundaries (7.5-ft horizontal and 15-ft radial zones from outside conductors)\n- Horizontal or sloped height limit lines indicating clearance limits\n- Clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to buildings, structures, service equipment, or other facilities\n- Transmission structure location and ROW access 