partment dependencies and low-confidence flags populated appropriately."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16479,"cache_read_input_tokens":31534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16479},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64beaaef-ed0b-4b8f-aa9d-17e754791a84","uuid":"6b07df86-0ad2-4c48-b10b-6bd80690d505"}
{"level":30,"time":1776952425712,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":158791,"duration_api_ms":158743,"num_turns":2,"result":"I've synthesized your 23 utility infrastructure findings into **7 structured comments** at a 3.3:1 consolidation ratio.\n\n## Output Summary\n\nThe grouping covers **electrical and water utility coordination** issues across transmission easement management, overhead/underground clearances, appurtenance spacing, and crossing specifications. All findings were **Tier 1 (within utility scope)** and are preserved in full detail.\n\n**Comments produced:**\n1. **Demolition plan safety notes** — Missing transmission clearance requirements and general utility caution language (2 findings, all high-confidence)\n2. **Transmission easement documentation** — Access corridor dimensions, easement boundaries, and structure locations not shown (3 findings, all high-confidence + 1 single-run)\n3. **Overhead clearance envelopes** — No height limit lines, clearance dimensions, or envelope delineation for distribution/transmission (5 findings: 2 high-confidence, 3 single-run)\n4. **Utility appurtenance clearances** — Vault, meter, cleanout, manhole spacing from poles/conductors undocumented (5 findings, all single-run)\n5. **Water utility tap crossing** — Crossing method, clearance, and encasement specifications missing (3 findings, all medium-confidence)\n6. **Underground coordination** — Joint-trench agreements and AULCC ROW approval documentation missing (2 findings, both single-run)\n7. **Staging/work zone verticals** — SCM staging and construction access vertical clearances undocumented (3 findings: 1 medium-confidence, 2 single-run)\n\nAll 23 input findings appear exactly once via `sourceId`. Per-run comments preserved verbatim in `runComments[]`. Cross-department dependencies and low-confidence flags populated appropriately.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"64beaaef-ed0b-4b8f-aa9d-17e754791a84","total_cost_usd":0.15476065,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48013,"cache_read_input_tokens":31534,"output_tokens":18315,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48013,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":18315,"cacheReadInputTokens":31534,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48013,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.15476065,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Demolition plan missing critical utility safety notes","summary":"Sheet 8 demolition notes lack required transmission line safety requirements and general utility caution language, increasing risk to field personnel and utility infrastructure.","sheets":[8],"applicableArea":"Demolition plan; Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Safety/contractor management; Austin Energy coordination","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Missing transmission line safety clearances from demolition notes: 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy, 10-foot barricade from transmission structures, warning signs, and prohibition on materials/spoils storage within transmission easement.","citation":"UCM 1.14.9","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Demolition plan sequence notes (Sheet 8, Block 9) do not address required safety clearances from transmission lines. Missing: (1) pre-construction safety meeting requirement ≥48 hours before commencement with Austin Energy; (2) barricade requirement 10 feet from all transmission structures, including guys and anchors; (3) warning signs under overhead transmission facilities; (4) prohibition on materials and spoils storage within the transmission easement. Current notes only reference Environmental Inspector meeting and utility abandonment."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Demolition plan (Sheet 8) Site Demolition Notes do not address required transmission line safety clearances detailed in Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes. Missing: (1) pre-construction safety meeting requirement with Austin Energy 48 hours before work commencement, (2) barricade requirement 10 feet from transmission structures, (3) warning signs under overhead transmission facilities, and (4) prohibition on materials or spoils storage within transmission easement."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Demolition plan notes do not address required safety clearances from transmission lines: pre-construction safety meeting with Austin Energy 48 hours before work commencement, barricades erected 10 feet from transmission structures, warning signs under overhead facilities, and prohibition on materials or spoils storage within transmission easement. Sheet 3 (General Notes) specifies transmission facility requirements but Sheet 8 demolition notes (Block 9, 10 items) do not reference or incorporate these safety requirements."}]},{"text":"Missing contractor caution note requiring extreme care when working near at-grade utility appurtenances (meter boxes, cleanouts, valve boxes, pump stations, service pedestals, etc.).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.20","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Demolition plan general notes do not include a requirement for contractor to use extreme caution when working near at-grade utility appurtenances. While the demolition notes address tree protection, utility abandonment, and safety meetings, there is no specific caution language warning the contractor about the electrical utility infrastructure present on the site."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Demolition plan general notes (Sheet 8, Block 9) do not include a note requiring contractor to exercise extreme caution when working near at-grade utility appurtenances (meter boxes, cleanouts, valve boxes, pump stations, service pedestals, etc.). This standard precaution is required on all demolition plans with proposed utility infrastructure."}]}]},{"headline":"Transmission easement boundaries and access requirements not graphically shown","summary":"Transmission easement location, ROW access corridor dimensions, and transmission structure positions are not depicted on site plan or construction plans, preventing verification of staging separation, access corridor maintenance, and utility pole placement compliance.","sheets":[3,5,9],"applicableArea":"Transmission easement; Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Transmission facility operator coordination for structure and easement location confirmation","attn":"Detail 3 flagged by single run; verify transmission facility locations with applicable utility operator before plan approval","details":[{"text":"25-foot-wide transmission ROW access corridor with minimum 16-foot vertical clearance dimensions not graphically shown on site plan (Sheet 9) or erosion control plan (Sheet 5) to verify compliance with required corridor maintenance.","citation":"UCM 1.14.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Construction and staging plans do not demonstrate maintenance of a 25-foot-wide access corridor with minimum 16-foot vertical clearance along the full transmission ROW length. The transmission easement location is not clearly delineated on the Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan (Sheet 5), and no construction plan explicitly shows the transmission access corridor dimensions required by UCM 1.14.4."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Construction plans do not demonstrate maintenance of a 25-foot-wide access corridor with minimum 16-foot vertical clearance along the transmission ROW. Transmission easement boundaries and access corridor requirements are not graphically delineated on the site plan or erosion control plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Maintenance of 25-foot-wide transmission ROW access corridor with 16-foot minimum vertical clearance cannot be verified. Although Sheet 3 contains detailed transmission facility requirements, no transmission ROW or access corridor is graphically depicted or dimensioned on site plan (Sheet 9) or construction/staging plans to demonstrate the required 25-foot width and 16-foot vertical clearance for its full length."}]},{"text":"Staging and temporary spoils areas' separation from transmission easement cannot be verified; easement boundaries not graphically delineated on construction or erosion control plans, despite Sheet 3 prohibiting materials storage within the easement.","citation":"UCM 1.14.9; Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot verify that staging and temporary spoils areas are not overlapping with transmission easement because the transmission easement boundary is not clearly delineated on the Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan. While Sheet 5 identifies a 'Staging and Storage Area' and 'Concrete Truck Cleanout' on the western side of the site, and Sheet 3 notes explicitly prohibit materials storage within the transmission easement, the transmission easement location is not graphically shown to verify compliance with the separation requirement."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes prohibit staging, spoils, and dumpsters within 25 feet of transmission structures. However, the transmission easement boundaries are not delineated on Sheet 5 (Erosion Control Plan) or Sheet 9 (Site Plan), making it impossible to verify that the shown staging area does not overlap transmission easement or violate 25-foot clearance from transmission structures."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Staging or temporary spoils areas overlapping utility line alignments or transmission easement cannot be verified. Although Sheet 3 specifies transmission easement restrictions (no spoils within 25 feet of transmission structures), a detailed staging/construction plan layout is not available in the reviewed sheets to confirm that staging areas avoid utility alignments and transmission easement encroachment."}]},{"text":"Electric utility poles proposed within water easements or within 10 feet of large transmission structures cannot be verified because transmission structure locations are not depicted on any site plan sheet, despite 16 detailed transmission facility notes on Sheet 3.","citation":"Requires human verification","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric utility poles proposed within water easements or within 10 feet of large electric transmission structures cannot be verified because transmission structures are not depicted on any site plan sheet or plat, despite Sheet 3 containing 16 detailed Electric Transmission Notes referencing transmission easements and structures. Applicability and compliance cannot be determined without clear identification of transmission facility location."}]}]},{"headline":"Overhead utility clearance zones lack graphical delineation and dimensioning","summary":"No distribution or transmission overhead conductor clearance envelopes, height limit lines, or clearance dimensions are shown on site plan or utility sheets, preventing verification of minimum sky-to-ground and radial separation requirements across varying site grades.","sheets":[5,9,11,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure; Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy for clearance envelope verification and site-specific analysis approval","attn":"Details 3–5 based on single-run findings; request AE-provided clearance envelope analysis and certified dimensions before final plan approval","details":[{"text":"No electrical clearance zones, transmission easement boundaries, or distribution conductor clearance envelopes are graphically delineated on any plan sheets (site plan, erosion control, electrical plan).","citation":"UCM 1.10.3; UCM 1.14.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.26","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No electrical clearance zones or envelopes are graphically delineated on any plan sheets. Transmission line safety buffers (including the 25-foot no-dig zone and transmission easement boundaries referenced in Sheet 3 General Notes) are not shown. Distribution overhead conductor clearance envelopes are not graphically represented."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electrical clearance zones are not graphically delineated on plans. Distribution clearance envelope boundaries (7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance and 15-foot radial zone from outside conductor) are not shown on site plan or utility plan sheets. No transmission clearance envelope (which requires AE-provided site-specific analysis) is shown despite Sheet 3 referencing transmission facilities."}]},{"text":"No horizontal dashed height limit lines depicted on site plan or erosion control plan to show transmission or distribution overhead conductor clearance envelope boundaries, despite Sheet 3 referencing transmission facilities.","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No horizontal dashed height limit lines are shown on the site plan or erosion control plan to delineate the overhead transmission conductor clearance envelope boundaries. Transmission structures and easement are referenced in Sheet 3 General Notes but are not graphically depicted with height limit annotations on site plan sheets."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Horizontal dashed height limit lines are not shown on plans to delineate AE overhead conductor clearance envelope boundaries. Site plan, grading plan, and utility plan sheets lack the required height limit line annotations that establish the vertical boundary of the overhead utility clearance zones."}]},{"text":"Minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from AE overhead primary, neutral, and secondary conductors along western and southern site boundaries cannot be verified; no clearance dimensions or measurement lines provided on electrical or site plans.","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from AE overhead primary, neutral, or secondary conductors cannot be verified. Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the electrical plan and site plan along Valley View Road boundary, but no clearance dimension lines or measurements are provided from the outermost conductor to any customer facility edge, building, transformer pad, or other structure."}]},{"text":"Minimum 15-foot radial clearance from AE overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified; no radial clearance envelopes or dimension arcs shown on utility plan (Sheet 21) or site plan (Sheet 9).","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Minimum 15-foot radial clearance from AE overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified. No radial clearance envelopes, dimension arcs, or measurements are shown on utility plan or site plan sheets from the outside conductor to any proposed customer facility."}]},{"text":"Sloped or stepped dashed height limit lines not shown on grading plan (Sheet 11) or utility profile sheets to reflect grade-dependent conductor clearance boundaries; site elevation range 678.5' to 681'.","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Sloped or stepped dashed height limit lines are not shown on plans where overhead utilities are present on sites with non-uniform grade conditions. The site has sloped terrain (elevations ranging from ~678.5' to ~681' per benchmarks), but no profile-view height limit lines reflecting grade changes beneath overhead conductor spans are depicted on grading plan or utility profile sheets."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility appurtenance clearances from poles and conductors undocumented","summary":"Clearance dimensions from customer service facilities, cleanouts, manhole, vault, and transformer locations to AE overhead poles, guy wires, and conductors are not dimensioned on any plan sheets, preventing verification of minimum separation requirements.","sheets":[12,20,21,26],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure; Site-wide","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Energy for clearance review and written approval of appurtenance locations","attn":"All details based on single-run findings; request comprehensive clearance dimension review from Austin Energy for all customer facilities, appurtenances, and utility structures shown on plans","details":[{"text":"Fire demand meter vault vertical clearance from overhead line sag not labeled on Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 20); no Austin Energy clearance approval letter evident in project documentation.","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.4","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Vault vertical clearance from top of proposed structure to sag of lowest overhead power line is not labeled on plans. Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 20) indicates a fire demand meter vault connection but does not show or dimension its vertical proximity to the overhead electric line shown along Valley View Road. No Austin Energy written clearance approval letter is evident in the project file documentation reviewed."}]},{"text":"Clearance dimension lines lack proper anchoring to outermost conductor (not utility pole centerline) on electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9).","citation":"UCM 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearance dimension lines cannot be verified as anchored to outermost conductor rather than utility pole centerline. No clearance dimensions are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) or site plan (Sheet 9) to verify proper measurement reference points."}]},{"text":"Customer service entrance facilities (transformer pads and electrical meters on Sheet 21) lack documented minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from AE poles and overhead lines other than service drop.","citation":"UCM 1.10.6.1; UCM 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Customer service entrance facilities and electrical appurtenances are not documented with minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from AE poles and overhead lines other than service drop. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations and electrical meter locations but provides no horizontal clearance dimension lines from these facilities to the OHE line or power poles shown along the property boundary."}]},{"text":"Large-diameter wastewater cleanout horizontal clearance from AE utility poles and guy wires cannot be verified; Construction Details Sheet 26 shows specifications but no clearance dimensions provided.","citation":"UCM 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Large-diameter cleanout horizontal clearance from utility poles and guy wires cannot be verified. Construction Details Sheet 26 shows wastewater cleanout specifications but does not provide horizontal clearance dimensions from proposed cleanout locations to existing AE utility poles or guy wires on the site."}]},{"text":"Storm drain manhole locations (Sheet 12) lack documented 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from AE power poles on western and southern property boundaries.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.15","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain manhole horizontal clearance from Austin Energy overhead electric poles cannot be verified with the required 5-foot minimum. Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) depicts multiple storm drain manholes across the site but does not provide horizontal clearance dimension lines from manhole locations to the AE power poles shown along the western and southern property boundaries."}]}]},{"headline":"Water utility tap crossing details incomplete and undimensioned","summary":"Sheet 20 water utility tap crossing under Valley View Road and existing water main lacks crossing method identification, clearance dimensions, and encasement specifications required to verify compliance with utility separation and roadway protection standards.","sheets":[20],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure; Valley View Road Frontage","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Water for clearance and encasement specification verification; Austin Energy for underground facility coordination","attn":"","details":[{"text":"AE underground facility clearance from water line at perpendicular crossings cannot be verified with required 12-inch minimum; Sheet 20 utility tap profile does not label horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions between water line and any AE underground electrical conduit.","citation":"UCM 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water utility crossing shown on Sheet 20 crossing existing wastewater and gas lines, but no crossing detail identifies AE underground facility proximity or demonstrates 12-inch clearance. Verify that water line crossings do not impact AE underground conduit; if AE underground is present at these crossing locations, clearance dimensions must be labeled."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"AE underground facility clearance from other utilities at perpendicular crossings cannot be verified with the required 12-inch minimum. Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile (Sheet 20) shows the proposed water line tap connection but does not label horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions between the water line and any AE underground electrical conduit at crossing points."}]},{"text":"Water utility tap crossing method (trenchless vs. open-cut) not identified on Sheet 20 plan or profile; vertical separation distances not labeled; applicable standard (trenchless: 36\" or 2× diameter per UCM 2.9.2.B.17 vs. open-cut: 12–18\" per UCM 2.9.1.B.3) cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM 2.9.2.B.17; UCM 2.9.1.B.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.12","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 20 profile shows water line (Wtr-Ln-A) crossing existing wastewater and gas lines, but the crossing method (trenchless vs. open-cut) is not identified on the plan or profile. Vertical separation distances are not labeled. Without crossing method designation and labeled clearance dimensions, the applicable separation standard cannot be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility crossing method (trenchless vs. open-cut) cannot be clearly identified on plans, preventing verification of applicable separation standard. Sheet 20 utility tap profile does not explicitly state whether the proposed water line tap crossing under Valley View Road or existing water main is trenchless or open-cut, which determines whether UCM 2.9.2.B.17 (trenchless: 36 in or 2× diameter) or UCM 2.9.1.B.3 (open-cut: 12-18 in) applies."}]},{"text":"Utility encasement specifications (piping material type, diameter, longitudinal extent) not provided on Sheet 20 Utility Tap Plan & Profile for water line crossing under Valley View Road per UCM 2.9.1.D.","citation":"UCM 2.9.1.D","sourceId":"1:EL-1.13","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 20 profile shows water line crossing under Valley View Road (public roadway), but encasement specifications (material type, diameter, extent) are not provided on the crossing detail sheets. Confirm encasement piping specifications for utilities crossing under the roadway per UCM 2.9.1.D."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Encasement specifications are not provided for utilities crossing under roadways or structures. Utility Tap Plan & Profile (Sheet 20) does not reference or detail encasement material type, dimensions, or longitudinal extent specifications for the proposed utility tap crossing under Valley View Road."}]}]},{"headline":"Underground utility coordination agreements and ROW documentation missing","summary":"Plans do not identify joint-trench arrangements with Austin Energy, provide required joint-trench agreements, or document AULCC ROW assignment change approvals for utilities located within 24 inches of existing ROW facilities.","sheets":[19,20,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Energy for joint-trench coordination; Austin Utility Location Coordination Commission (AULCC) for ROW assignment change approval; Public Works for ROW authorization","attn":"Both details based on single-run findings; verify documentation status with AULCC and Austin Energy before plan approval","details":[{"text":"Underground infrastructure layout does not identify whether non-AE utilities (water, wastewater on Sheets 19) are proposed in joint trenches with AE underground conduit (Sheet 21), and no written joint-trench agreement with Austin Energy is evident.","citation":"UCM 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground electrical infrastructure shown on Sheet 21; water and wastewater utilities shown on Sheet 19. The plans do not clearly identify whether any non-AE utilities are proposed in joint trenches with AE underground conduit, or indicate if a written joint-trench agreement with Austin Energy is on file."}]},{"text":"Utility tap located within 24 inches of existing ROW facility (Sheet 20) lacks documented AULCC Completeness Letter or formal ROW assignment change approval required by § 14-11-180(C).","citation":"§ 14-11-180(C)","sourceId":"1:EL-1.11","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Proposed utility located within 24 inches of existing ROW facility cannot be verified with AULCC ROW assignment change approval documentation. Sheet 20 shows utility tap proximity to existing water main but does not reference AULCC Completeness Letter (ROW assignment change approval) or other formal AULCC authorization in the plan notes or project documentation reviewed."}]}]},{"headline":"Staging and work zone vertical clearances not documented on plans","summary":"Vertical clearance documentation is missing for SCM staging and maintenance access areas (14-foot minimum from vegetation) and construction driveways passing beneath overhead electric lines, preventing verification of access compliance and utility safety.","sheets":[5,9,15,16],"applicableArea":"Drainage & Detention; Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Landscape/Environmental for SCM access drive requirements; Austin Energy for overhead line clearance verification","attn":"Details 2–3 based on single-run findings; coordinate with Austin Energy on final work zone clearance requirements","details":[{"text":"SCM staging area (Sheet 5, western site) vertical clearance minimum 14 feet from existing and proposed vegetation and all overhead objects not demonstrated; Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan (Sheet 15) does not specify designated staging area with labeled clearances.","citation":"DCM 1.2.4.E.2.e","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 5 shows a 'Staging and Storage Area' on the western side of the site, but no vertical clearance dimensions or annotations are provided. The plan does not demonstrate the 14-foot minimum vertical clearance from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects above the staging area."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"SCM staging area vertical clearance minimum 14 feet from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects cannot be verified. Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan (Sheet 15) addresses pond design and storage volumes but does not specify a designated staging area with labeled 14-foot vertical clearance dimensions from overhead vegetation and other objects."}]},{"text":"SCM maintenance access drive vertical clearance minimum 14 feet from existing and proposed vegetation and all other overhead obstructions not documented on Sheet 16 maintenance and construction requirements.","citation":"DCM 1.2.4.E.1.e.ii","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"SCM maintenance access drive vertical clearance is not documented at minimum 14 feet from existing and proposed vegetation and all other objects. Sheet 16 maintenance and construction requirements (Block 8) address tree preservation in the access drive design but do not specify the 14-foot minimum vertical clearance requirement from vegetation at maturity and all other overhead obstructions."}]},{"text":"Construction access driveway and work zone vertical clearance below overhead electric lines (OHE shown along western and southern boundaries on site plan) not documented with clearance dimensions at internal access points.","citation":"UCM 1.10.6.2; UCM 1.3.16","sourceId":"1:EL-1.24","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Work zone or construction access driveway vertical clearance below overhead utilities cannot be verified. Overhead electric line (OHE) is shown along the western and southern site boundaries on the site plan, but no vertical clearance dimensions are documented at internal driveway access points or work zones that may pass beneath overhead conductor spans."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d42d4ce8-1446-4a14-90cf-fc1780e82f45"}
