{"level":30,"time":1776952434441,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"2.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":167526,"duration_api_ms":167475,"num_turns":2,"result":"## Summary\n\nI've synthesized your **9 utility infrastructure findings** into **3 consolidated comments** using aggressive merging by theme:\n\n### Comment Structure:\n\n**Comment 1 — Easement & Transformer Pad Documentation** (3 details)\n- Missing recorded easements encumbering 19% of property (Greenbelt & Drainage, by instrument)\n- Transformer pads lack AE easement docs and License Agreements\n- Clearance violations and AE Design spec gaps for Pads 2 & 3\n- **Severity 3** (critical — blocks approval)\n\n**Comment 2 — Utility Routing Conflicts** (3 details)\n- Electrical/wastewater under detention pond (Sheet 15)\n- Water utility through street tree planting zone without root barriers\n- New private utility routing undefined (through ROW vs. private property)\n- **Severity 2** (medium — fixable with rerouting)\n\n**Comment 3 — Demolition & Removal Documentation** (3 details)\n- Abandoned utilities from prior assisted living facility not documented\n- Public utility termination procedures at ROW boundary undefined\n- Power pole removal coordination letters/permits missing\n- **Severity 2** (medium — fixable with revised demolition plan)\n\n### Coverage:\n✓ All 9 findings accounted for (each appears in exactly one comment's `details` array)\n✓ All atomic data points preserved: instrument numbers, acreage, specific building units, sheet numbers, codes\n✓ Cross-department flags set (Austin Energy, Public Works, Arborist, Watershed)\n✓ Attention flags set for low-confidence details and items requiring coordination\n\nThe output is ready for review.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"39c5f380-3d88-429b-94f6-ab67ab3f0560","total_cost_usd":0.1650001,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47342,"cache_read_input_tokens":27866,"output_tokens":20604,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":47342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":20604,"cacheReadInputTokens":27866,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47342,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1650001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Recorded easements and transformer pad documentation missing","summary":"Two perpetual recorded easements encumbering approximately 19% of the property are not depicted on the site plan. Transformer pad locations lack AE easement encumbrances, required License Agreements, compliance with clearance requirements, and AE Design coordination.","sheets":[2,9,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (transformer pad specifications and AE easement requirements); Public Works (easement verification and licensing requirements)","attn":"Coordinate with Austin Energy regarding final transformer pad locations and specifications before approval. Verify that proposed pad locations can satisfy minimum 10-foot clearance from all adjacent structures. Obtain copies of all recorded easement instruments from county records.","details":[{"text":"Two perpetual recorded easements encumber approximately 19% of the property but are not depicted on the site plan: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres, NE interior, no-build zone) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres, NE corner).","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.A.1","sourceId":"2:EL-2.15","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Two critical recorded easements (Greenbelt Access & Use Easement Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres; City of Austin Drainage Easement Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres) and four additional GIS-confirmed easements (10' Wastewater, 25' Drainage, 7.5' Public Utility, 10' Drainage) are not depicted on submitted site plan, preventing verification that utility easement boundaries do not encroach into proposed public right-of-way. Applicant must add all recorded easement boundaries to site plan before compliance can be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Two perpetual recorded easements are not depicted on the submitted site plan: (1) Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres, NE interior, no-build zone, perpetual), and (2) City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres, NE corner, perpetual). These recorded easements encumber approximately 19% of the property. All recorded easements must be depicted on the site plan, plat, and all relevant working drawings before approval. Current site plan compliance cannot be verified without these critical easements shown and building layout verified against them."}]},{"text":"Transformer pad locations lack dedicated AE easement encumbrances and required License Agreements from AE Public Involvement. Pads 1 and 3 show only 'Vault Easement' (not AE easement); Pads 2 and 4 have no easement notation. Required License Agreements per UCM § 1.10.10.3 or City Manager licenses per § 14-11-41 are not documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.3; § 14-11-41","sourceId":"2:EL-2.16","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Two critical recorded easements required by law are not depicted on site plan: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (2010070731, 0.31 acres, NE no-build zone) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (2011021137, 0.130 acres, NE corner). Additionally, transformer pads lack required AE easement documentation: Pads 1 & 3 show only 'Vault Easement' (not AE easement); Pads 2 & 4 have no easement notation. No dedicated AE easements visible encumbering transformer locations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Submitted site plan does not show a dedicated AE easement encumbering transformer pad locations, nor is there notation of a License Agreement from AE Public Involvement per UCM § 1.10.10.3 or a City Manager license per § 14-11-41 for items within recorded utility easements. Utility easement status and licensing compliance cannot be verified from submitted documents. Provide AE easement plat or evidence of required license agreements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The site plan identifies utility easements but does not include copies of required License Agreements or City Manager licenses. Items placed within private AE easements require a License Agreement from AE Public Involvement per UCM § 1.10.10.3. Items within public utility easements or public ROW require a City Manager license per § 14-11-41. Submit copies of all required licensing documentation for any structures, paving, or landscaping proposed within recorded easement boundaries before approval."}]},{"text":"Transformer Pad 3 is positioned less than 5 feet from Unit 801 exterior wall and Pad 2 is less than 10 feet from Units 404 and 504, both violating UCM § 1.10.4 minimum 10-foot clearance from adjacent structures. All pads lack AE Design sizing specifications per UCM § 1.5.2.6 and coordination documentation with Austin Energy.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4; UCM § 1.5.2.6","sourceId":"2:EL-2.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer Pad 3 is positioned less than 5 feet (nearly flush) against the exterior wall of Unit 801, violating the minimum 10-foot clearance requirement from any adjacent building or structure per UCM § 1.10.4(hot-stick/padlocked side). Transformer Pad 2, located in the tight corridor between Units 404 and 504, also appears to be positioned less than 10 feet from building exteriors. Additionally, no dedicated AE easement is shown on the site plan to encumber the transformer pad areas as required. Relocate transformer pads to satisfy minimum 10-foot clearance from all adjacent structures, and provide a dedicated AE easement plat encumbering the pad locations."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pads shown on the preliminary electrical design plan lack required specification and documentation. Pad dimensions must be sized per AE Design specifications (UCM § 1.5.2.6 requires customer to furnish pad per AE Design based on customer's AutoCAD site drawings). Each pad must be encumbered by a dedicated AE easement and protected by a License Agreement from AE Public Involvement (UCM § 1.10.10.3). Coordinate with Austin Energy to obtain final pad dimensions and establish recorded utility easements for each pad."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility routing conflicts and incomplete documentation","summary":"Utility lines are routed through incompatible areas without complete documentation. Electrical and wastewater utilities cross the detention pond; water utility crosses a street tree planting zone; and new private utility routing to/from service connections is undefined.","sheets":[8,15,19,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Landscape/Arborist (street tree planting zone and root barriers); Watershed Management (detention pond design and utility conflicts); Public Works (ROW permitting and coordination)","attn":"Cannot fully verify routing details from submitted sheets — utility routing plans lack sufficient depth/profile detail. Confirm all electrical and wastewater utilities avoid the detention pond footprint entirely. Identify and protect root barrier zones for street trees. Clarify routing for new water and wastewater service connections to/from service points.","details":[{"text":"Electrical and wastewater utility lines are routed directly through the biofiltration/detention pond footprint, crossing through the sedimentation basin and biofiltration media on Sheet 15.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.10","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Sheet 15 (Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan) shows electrical (E) and wastewater (WW) utility lines routed directly through the biofiltration/detention pond footprint, crossing through the sedimentation basin and biofiltration media. Utilities must not be routed under detention or retention ponds. Revise utility routing to avoid the pond area entirely."}]},{"text":"Water utility line crosses through H.2 Street Yard planting zone along Valley View Road where street trees are present. No root barrier boundaries, designated planting zone delineations, or utility type designation (Austin Water vs. private service) are documented.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.C","sourceId":"2:EL-2.11","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water utility line shown crossing through H.2 Street Yard planting zone along Valley View Road where street trees are present. However, no root barrier boundaries or designated planting zone delineations are marked on landscape plan, and utility type (Austin Water vs. private service) is not specified. Planting zone design cannot be verified from available documents."}]},{"text":"New private water and wastewater service connections lack clear routing documentation. Site plan does not specify whether new utilities are routed through public ROW, private property, or dedicated easements.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.17","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing public water and wastewater utilities in Valley View Road ROW are identified for demolition/removal. New private utility service connections are proposed. Site plan does not clearly show whether new private utilities are routed through public ROW or relocated to private property or dedicated easements. Final routing and ROW status cannot be determined from available plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Demolition and utility removal documentation incomplete","summary":"Demolition plans lack specific documentation for utility removal methods and coordination with city departments. Abandoned utilities from prior use, public utility termination procedures, and power pole relocation coordination are not documented.","sheets":[8,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (power pole and overhead electric line removal); Public Utilities/Austin Water (public utility termination and ROW restoration); Engineering (demolition sequencing and coordination)","attn":"Demolition plan must be revised to explicitly document: (1) locations and removal methods for all abandoned utilities from the prior assisted living facility use; (2) termination procedures and standards compliance for public utilities at property/ROW boundary; (3) Austin Energy coordination letters, permits, and removal approvals for overhead power lines and poles.","details":[{"text":"Property formerly housed an assisted living facility (demolished June 2022). Abandoned utility infrastructure from prior use may conflict with biofiltration/detention pond, new building locations, and utility routing. Documentation of removal (caps, plugs, abandonments) is not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.18","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The property was previously developed with an assisted living facility (demolished June 2022). Abandoned utility infrastructure from the prior use may remain on site or in ROW. Demolition plans must explicitly document that all abandoned utilities creating conflicts with proposed improvements have been removed, with particular attention to conflicts with the biofiltration/detention pond, new building locations, and utility routing. Provide documentation of abandoned utility removals (caps, plugs, abandonments) prior to construction."}]},{"text":"Demolition plan requires removal of public water and wastewater infrastructure in Valley View Road ROW. Method of termination at property line/ROW boundary (capping, plugging, or abandonment procedures per applicable standards) is not specified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"2:EL-2.19","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Demolition plan shows existing public water and wastewater infrastructure in Valley View Road ROW requiring removal. However, specific method of termination at property line/ROW boundary (capping, plugging, complete removal, or abandonment procedures) is not documented. Demolition notes address private utility abandonment but do not specify how public utilities will be terminated per applicable standards."}]},{"text":"Demolition notes require City of Austin coordination for removal of overhead power poles and electric lines on southern boundary. No Austin Energy coordination letters, permits, feasibility studies, or removal approvals are provided in the submittal.","citation":"UCM § 1.3.15; UCM § 1.3.16; UCM § 1.3.19","sourceId":"2:EL-2.21","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Demolition plan notes require coordination with City of Austin for removal of power poles and electric lines. Existing overhead electric line shown on southern property boundary. However, no Austin Energy coordination letters, permits, relocation feasibility studies, or removal approvals are provided in available submittal. Power pole relocation coordination and compliance with clearance/access requirements cannot be verified."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0a16bc45-8945-4162-a625-26ef369a67bc"}
