{"level":30,"time":1776952439761,"pid":35263,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"3.json","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01F6bUUQkjvEe2y9Ew9DejqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tqva8KXTSynv8gbEtN8g4g","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Austin Energy Service Approvals Not Documented","summary":"Multiple required Austin Energy approvals and coordination letters are absent from the submittal, preventing verification of electrical service readiness and design compliance.","sheets":[1,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy – service availability, design approval, and ESPA coordination","attn":"Clarify with Austin Energy whether ESPA submission and design approval are required before site plan approval (AE notes indicate some may follow regulatory exception). Verify Service Availability Letter requirement timing.","details":[{"text":"Electric Service Planning Application submission to Austin Energy and approval documentation not provided. ESPA is required before or concurrent with site plan approval.","citation":"AEDC 1.4.2.1","sourceId":"3:EL-3.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric Service Planning Application (ESPA) approval is not documented in the plan set. While new Austin Energy electrical service is clearly proposed (transformers, meters, pull boxes, and underground lines shown on Sheet 21), the ESPA submission and approval status cannot be verified from the current submittal. ESPA is normally submitted after site plan approval per the regulatory exception; current status cannot be determined from available documents."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No Electric Service Planning Application (ESPA) approval letter or submission documentation is visible in the site plan package. Austin Energy completeness check being marked complete does not constitute ESPA approval documentation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric Service Planning Application submission to Austin Energy and approval documentation not provided in the site plan submittal package or supplementary documents. An ESPA is required before or concurrent with site plan approval for electrical service; verification of submission and approval status cannot be determined from available documents."}]},{"text":"Austin Energy Utility clearance letter confirming service availability is not present in the submittal package.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"3:EL-3.2","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Austin Energy Utility (AEU) clearance or approval has not been located in the submittal package. No clearance letter from Austin Energy confirming service availability is present in the supplementary documents provided, though Austin Energy noted that the completeness check is complete."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Austin Energy Utility (AEU) clearance letter is not documented in the site plan package. While Austin Energy completeness check is noted as complete, no separate AEU clearance letter is visible to confirm approval."}]},{"text":"Electric Service Availability Letter from Austin Energy Public Involvement has not been provided.","citation":"AEDC 1.4.1","sourceId":"3:EL-3.3","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric Service Availability Letter from Austin Energy Public Involvement has not been provided. Although the site is in Austin's established service territory, this letter may be required depending on AE's standard procedures for new service; its absence cannot be verified as compliant or deficient without clarification of AE service availability determination."}]},{"text":"No evidence of Austin Energy approval for proposed transformer and pull box designs shown on Sheet 21.","citation":"AEDC 1.4.2.4","sourceId":"3:EL-3.7","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows preliminary electrical design with transformer and pull box locations, but no evidence of Austin Energy approval for these designs has been provided in the documents. Applicability cannot be determined without confirmation that final transformer and pull box designs are required before site plan approval."}]}]},{"headline":"Required Electrical Service Notes Missing","summary":"Three required site-specific notes are absent from the General Notes Sheet (Sheet 3), creating gaps in electrical service area designation, developer responsibilities, and preconstruction coordination.","sheets":[3],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Verify whether transmission easement preconstruction meeting language on Sheet 3 satisfies UCM 3.8.0 requirement, or confirm whether additional general note is needed.","details":[{"text":"Site plan lacks required note stating 'This site lies within the Austin Energy service area' per AEDC 1.16.0(7). Four standard Austin Energy notes are present but this specific service area designation is not included.","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(7)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.4","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan does not include a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area. This is a required site-specific plan note per AEDC 1.16.0(7) for all sites within Austin Energy's service territory."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan lacks a note stating that the site lies within the Austin Energy service area. Although four Standard Austin Energy Notes are present on Sheet 3, none explicitly states the service area designation required by AEDC 1.16.0(7). Add a note: 'This site lies within the Austin Energy service area.'"}]},{"text":"Plans do not include required note stating developer responsibility for designing and constructing all conduit and related electrical infrastructure to current Austin Energy standards, including conductor installation costs and utility coordination.","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(7)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.5","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Plans do not include the required developer responsibility note stating that the developer is responsible for designing and constructing all conduit and related infrastructure to current Austin Energy Electric Service Standards, including conductor installation costs, and for coordinating with other utilities to resolve conflicts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Plans lack the required note stating developer responsibility for designing and constructing all conduit and related electrical infrastructure to current Austin Energy Electric Service Standards, including conductor installation costs and coordination with other utilities. Sheet 3 contains four standard AE notes but does not include this site-specific developer responsibility statement per AEDC 1.16.0(7)."}]},{"text":"No general note states preconstruction meeting with Austin Energy is required prior to demolition. Transmission easement notes reference 48-hour preconstruction safety meeting but no explicit UCM 3.8.0 requirement appears in General Notes.","citation":"UCM 3.8.0","sourceId":"3:EL-3.9","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No general note found stating that a preconstruction meeting with Austin Energy is required prior to starting demolition. Although transmission easement notes on Sheet 3 mention a 48-hour preconstruction safety meeting requirement, no explicit note in the General Notes or Demolition Plan requires this AE coordination per UCM 3.8.0."}]}]},{"headline":"Electrical Infrastructure Coordination Documentation Incomplete","summary":"Required submissions and plan documentation for Austin Energy electrical infrastructure coordination are not evident, including easement recording, georeferenced drawings, and equipment access documentation.","sheets":[2,21],"applicableArea":"Electrical Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Energy – coordination on easement placement, access design, and design submission requirements","attn":"Verify with Austin Energy which of these submittals (AutoCAD drawing, easement documents, access documentation) are required before site plan approval vs. post-approval. Only Run 3 flagged these items; other runs may have accepted preliminary status.","details":[{"text":"No recorded electrical easement documents or correspondence demonstrating coordination between applicant and Austin Energy regarding final layout and easement recording have been provided.","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(3)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.10","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No recorded electrical easement documents or correspondence demonstrating coordination between the applicant and Austin Energy regarding final layout and easement recording have been provided in the application. Verification of easement acquisition and AE coordination status cannot be determined from available documents."}]},{"text":"No evidence of a georeferenced AutoCAD drawing (land development application drawing) submitted to Austin Energy with required content (easements, existing facilities, permanent structures, topology, property lines, building setbacks).","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(1)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.11","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No evidence of a georeferenced AutoCAD drawing submitted to Austin Energy has been provided in the site plan documents or supplementary materials. Verification that the required land development application drawing was submitted to AE with all required content (easements, existing facilities, permanent structures, topology, property lines, building setbacks) cannot be determined from available documents."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 does not depict labeled access routes, truck access dimensions (minimum 12-ft width and 16-ft vertical clearance), or clear paths to proposed Austin Energy equipment.","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(4)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.12","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer and pull box locations but does not depict labeled access routes, truck access dimensions (minimum 12-ft width and 16-ft vertical clearance), or clear paths to proposed AE equipment. Demonstration of unobstructed access for Austin Energy personnel cannot be verified from the available plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Addressing Plan & Administrative Approvals Not Documented","summary":"The site plan lacks documented address reservation with 911 Addressing, an approved addressing plan from Address Management Services, and a comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table on the cover sheet listing all applicable external approvals.","sheets":[1,18,29],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Development Services, 911 Addressing/Address Management Services – address reservation and plan approval coordination","attn":"Address Management Services and/or 911 Addressing may have reviewed the plan (Completeness indicates Addressing Review complete), but explicit written approval documentation was not identified. Confirm whether address reservation occurs before or after site plan approval. Clarify whether partial AULCC/water/wastewater table on Sheet 18 is supplemented by comprehensive cover sheet table.","details":[{"text":"Comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not completed on the cover sheet per UCM 2.5.1.F. Required table must list TxDOT, railroad, gas, easement, county, water district, TCEQ, service extension, and Planning & Development Review approvals.","citation":"UCM 2.5.1.F","sourceId":"3:EL-3.29","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not present on the cover sheet. This table must list all applicable external reviews, approvals, and permits including: TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district or MUD approval, Texas Department of Health approval, TCEQ approval, non-occupancy letter, service extension approval, and Planning and Development Review Department approvals."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not completed on the cover sheet listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district approval, TCEQ approval, service extension approval, etc.) per UCM 2.5.1.F. A partial Additional Review Acknowledgement form addressing only water/wastewater and AULCC requirements is located on Sheet 18, but does not satisfy the requirement for a complete table on the cover sheet."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Cover sheet (Sheet 1) contains only a partial 'Reviewed By' table with spaces for Development Services, City Fire Department, and Austin Water dates. A comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (including TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, MUD, Texas Department of Health, service extensions, and Planning & Development Review approvals) per UCM 2.5.1.F is not present on the cover sheet or identified elsewhere on the plans."}]},{"text":"Only partial approval tracking is present on cover sheet: 'Reviewed By' table on Sheet 1 lists Development Services, Fire, Austin Water; water/wastewater and AULCC form on Sheet 18. Neither satisfies comprehensive UCM 2.5.1.F requirement.","citation":"UCM 2.5.1.F","sourceId":"3:EL-3.29","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not present on the cover sheet. This table must list all applic