nd permits including: TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district or MUD approval, Texas Department of Health approval, TCEQ approval, non-occupancy letter, service extension approval, and Planning and Development Review Department approvals."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not completed on the cover sheet listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district approval, TCEQ approval, service extension approval, etc.) per UCM 2.5.1.F. A partial Additional Review Acknowledgement form addressing only water/wastewater and AULCC requirements is located on Sheet 18, but does not satisfy the requirement for a complete table on the cover sheet."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Cover sheet (Sheet 1) contains only a partial 'Reviewed By' table with spaces for Development Services, City Fire Department, and Austin Water dates. A comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (including TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, MUD, Texas Department of Health, service extensions, and Planning & Development Review approvals) per UCM 2.5.1.F is not present on the cover sheet or identified elsewhere on the plans."}]},{"text":"Only partial approval tracking is present on cover sheet: 'Reviewed By' table on Sheet 1 lists Development Services, Fire, Austin Water; water/wastewater and AULCC form on Sheet 18. Neither satisfies comprehensive UCM 2.5.1.F requirement.","citation":"UCM 2.5.1.F","sourceId":"3:EL-3.29","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not present on the cover sheet. This table must list all applicable external reviews, approvals, and permits including: TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district or MUD approval, Texas Department of Health approval, TCEQ approval, non-occupancy letter, service extension approval, and Planning and Development Review Department approvals."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table is not completed on the cover sheet listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (TxDOT permit, railroad permit, gas company permit, easement acquisition, county approval, water district approval, TCEQ approval, service extension approval, etc.) per UCM 2.5.1.F. A partial Additional Review Acknowledgement form addressing only water/wastewater and AULCC requirements is located on Sheet 18, but does not satisfy the requirement for a complete table on the cover sheet."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Cover sheet (Sheet 1) contains only a partial 'Reviewed By' table with spaces for Development Services, City Fire Department, and Austin Water dates. A comprehensive Additional Review Acknowledgement table listing all applicable external reviews and approvals (including TxDOT, railroad, gas company, TCEQ, water districts, MUD, Texas Department of Health, service extensions, and Planning & Development Review approvals) per UCM 2.5.1.F is not present on the cover sheet or identified elsewhere on the plans."}]},{"text":"No evidence that proposed street addresses or unit numbers (Units 101–806 per Sheet 29) have been reserved with 911 Addressing/Address Management Services prior to site plan approval.","citation":"Addressing Standards, Streets","sourceId":"3:EL-3.30","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"While Sheet 29 shows an addressing plan with all proposed unit addresses (Units 101-104, 201-206, 301-305, 401-405, 501-504, 601-604, 701-705, 801-806), there is no evidence in the submittal that these street addresses or unit numbers have been reserved with 911 Addressing/Address Management Services prior to site plan approval."}]},{"text":"Documented approved addressing plan from Address Management Services is not provided in the submittal. While Sheet 29 displays the addressing plan and Completeness Check indicates Addressing Review is complete, explicitly documented approved plan (distinct from Address Validation Letter) is not visible.","citation":"Addressing Standards, Introduction","sourceId":"3:EL-3.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No evidence of an approved addressing plan from Address Management Services is present in the submittal. Sheet 29 shows an addressing plan layout, but there is no separate approval documentation confirming that Address Management Services has formally approved the addressing scheme. Note that an Address Validation Letter (AVL), if issued, is distinct from an approved addressing plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"While Sheet 29 displays the addressing plan with individual unit numbers (Units 101-806), no documentation of approved addressing plan from 911 Addressing/Address Management Services is visible in the site plan package. An Address Validation Letter, if issued, does not constitute an approved addressing plan per UCM requirements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Completeness Check Results show Addressing Review as COMPLETE, suggesting the addressing plan has been reviewed. However, an explicitly documented approved addressing plan from Address Management Services is not provided in the supplementary documents reviewed. Verification of formal addressing plan approval (distinct from an Address Validation Letter) cannot be confirmed from available documentation."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility Coordination & Transmission Easement Documentation","summary":"Utility locating and coordination letter status is unclear, and verification of transmission easement plat note requirements is incomplete due to inability to review the recorded easement plat.","sheets":[3,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Utility Locating and Coordination (AULCC) – utility coordination thresholds and public ROW work documentation; Austin Energy – transmission easement plat notes","attn":"Verify with Austin Energy whether recorded easement plat has been prepared and submitted, or if this is preliminary. Clarify AULCC threshold analysis and whether Completeness Letter submission is required before site plan approval. Confirm public ROW utility work extent and whether it triggers AULCC review.","details":[{"text":"Linear footage of public right-of-way utility construction/excavation and utility pole relocations are not clearly documented on the plans. AULCC Completeness Letter is not identified in submitted documents. Project threshold determination (≥300 LF citywide, ≥25 LF DAPCZ, pole relocations, main assignments) cannot be made.","citation":"UCM 3.2.0","sourceId":"3:EL-3.23","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The site plan shows primarily interior utility infrastructure with water/wastewater connections to existing City mains. Linear footage of public ROW utility construction/excavation and any utility pole relocations are not clearly documented or quantified on the plans. AULCC Completeness Letter not identified in submitted documents. Whether the project triggers AULCC review thresholds (≥300 LF citywide, ≥25 LF in DAPCZ, pole relocations, or main assignments) cannot be definitively determined from available documents."}]},{"text":"Verification that all eight required transmission easement plat notes (AE tree pruning rights, additional easement/access, erosion control, clearance maintenance, NESC, 24-hour access, road capacity, 48-hour notice) are recorded cannot be confirmed. Verification that transmission easement is not labeled parkland per AEDC 1.16.0(9) is not possible.","citation":"AEDC 1.16.0(8); AEDC 1.16.0(9)","sourceId":"3:EL-3.32","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 contains 16 Electric Transmission Notes with detailed restrictions and requirements. However, verification that all eight specific plat notes required by AEDC 1.16.0(8) are present (AE tree pruning rights, additional easement/access, erosion control, clearance maintenance, NESC compliance, 24-hour access, road capacity, 48-hour construction notice) cannot be fully confirmed without reviewing the recorded easement plat. Additionally, confirmation that no portion of the transmission easement is labeled as parkland per AEDC 1.16.0(9) is not verifiable from the current site plan review."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"558b5b53-f6da-48e6-9ec0-c14fb6f020b9"}
